Please listen to Mr. Teav Vannul's voice as follows: Some small and medium-sized handicrafts in Battambang province participate in the implementation of environmental conservation projects and prevent other emissions that lead to climate change.
(Battambang): By educating and disseminating the dangers of emissions from the Ministry of Institutions and Environmental Partners for local organizations in Battambang province, small and medium-sized handicrafts have participated in the implementation of environmental conservation projects, food hygiene and climate change. Ministry of Environment, a staff of the Royal Government.
The Ministry of Environment has worked with stakeholders to implement projects in response to climate change, including activities to reduce greenhouse gas emissions, adapt to climate change, protect the environment, manage natural resources, conserve biodiversity and Improve the lives of people in the community to reduce the pressure on the environment.
According to Mr. Keung Sok Kheng, Director of the Handicraft Industry Office of the Battambang Provincial Department of Handicraft Industry, some small and medium-sized handicrafts in Battambang Province have started implementing environmental conservation projects in response to Cambodia's climate change and environmental impacts. And public health.
Mr. Keung Sok Kheng stated that 7 out of 900 small and medium handicrafts in Battambang province have successfully implemented environmental conservation, food hygiene and climate change projects.
Speaking to reporters during a visit to explore the implementation of green industry organized by the Ministry of Environment on the occasion of the campaign to raise awareness on climate change to journalists in Battambang on 22 December, Mr. Keung Sok Kheng claimed that the participating crafts Environmental protection projects, they participate in reducing the management of solid and liquid waste, as well as emissions or gases as required by the Ministry of Environment.
"The Ministry of Environment is involved and encourages craft and enterprise owners to implement climate change mitigation measures through the construction of a drainage system," he said. For drainage, this is a contribution to preventing climate change. In particular, it also helps in the workplace environment, the environment is also good for the health of workers and people around, as well as good for the quality of food.
Ms. Vong Sokyem, the owner of a fish sauce, soy sauce and chili sauce factory with the logo of "Quarter Handicraft" located in Romchek 4 Village, Sangkat Rattanak, Battambang City, said that she set up a quarter hand craft in 2009 with the help of the Samdech Techo Hun Foundation Project. Sen to reduce poverty and migration. Through this project, a clean environment is implemented and helps to reduce climate change as well as help reduce poverty.
She stated that since the construction of many production lines to participate in maintaining good hygiene, environmental protection and participation in reducing climate change, including: the preparation of sewer systems, the construction of exhaust pipes to eliminate odors. To reduce the use of firewood by neighbors by turning to steam boilers on production processes and other activities that do not have a serious impact on the environment.
