(Phnom Penh): The Angkor Writing Program is getting a lot of attention from the public as the organizers of the program are calling for more support, including funding, materials and volunteers to use in this important program.
It should be informed that the Angkor Writing Program will be officially held on the morning of January 21, 2024 in front of the bridge in front of Angkor Wat, Siem Reap Province. We can call this Angkor Writing Program a Khmer Literacy Competition because it is a competition to write essays in Khmer language, which is open to people from all walks of life, regardless of age, gender, or role.
Mr. Lim Bunhok said that the program also needs philanthropists to donate souvenirs to encourage candidates and winners to participate in the Khmer literacy competition.
For the volunteer team, a program is also needed to help organize the competition program at the bridge in front of Angkor Wat. This is according to Mr. Lim Bunhok.
Please note that the Angkor Writing Program is an important event in the promotion of Khmer literature, especially to help people change the spelling habits in writing and reading Khmer words correctly, which Mr. Lim Bun Hok wants to inspire this program. As a national movement going forward to promote Khmer national literature, provide accuracy for the next generation.
For those who want to participate in the competition, please hurry to register by telegram above, because the registration will close by January 7, 2023.
