Stong District Governor Considers Private Schools as Partners in the Promotion and Development of Education and Human Resources
(Kampong Thom): Mr. Say Kim Lam, Governor of Stong District, stated that private schools have great potential to promote and develop the education sector and human resources and asked private schools to continue to pay attention to improving the quality of behavioral education. School rules, regulations, professional ethics of teachers, especially the enhancement of professional qualifications.
This was stated by the Governor of Stong District at the distribution ceremony of certificates, certificates and awards to the students who graduated in 2022-2023 at SED School, Stong District Branch on December 24, 2023.
"Private schools have great potential and are an indispensable partner in the promotion and development of education and human resources in Cambodia," he said.
He added that the nation's progress depends on human resources and capital with real knowledge and skills in line with the context of modern digital technology.
He instructed the school management to pay more attention to strengthening the quality of education, behavior, school rules, discipline, professional ethics of teachers, especially to increase professional qualifications.
In addition, he advised parents and guardians to focus on learning, co-learning, mentoring their children at home and digitally, and encouraging them to learn a language other than their native language. It is better to go to college and have a successful career, especially to stay away from drugs.
Mr. Say Kimlam expressed his deep gratitude to the principal for providing scholarships to poor students through the Stong District Administration and instructed the principals, both private and public, to participate in promoting and cultivating a sense of love for the environment in particular. In the context of current climate change.
It should be noted that for the academic year 2022-2023, SED School, Stong District Branch has a total of 547 students, 295 girls, full-time and part-time classes, General Education Khmer, English, Chinese, Quick Calculator, Pam, Computer, Sports and Car For transporting students as well.
