Deputy Prime Minister Neth Savoeun mentions three challenges that officials at all levels must work together to solve
(Kampong Cham): Dr. Neth Savoeun, Deputy Prime Minister and Chairman of the Cambodian People's Party (CPP) Working Group for Kampong Cham Province, said that despite the successful results of the leadership and members of the party, there are still challenges. Some that officials need to make changes to meet the needs of the people.
Mr. Santibandith said this on the occasion of presiding over the meeting to disseminate the content of the Extraordinary General Assembly of the National Representative of the Cambodian People's Party and the announcement of the decision to appoint the party's working group to help cities / districts in Kampong Cham province on the 24th. December 2023 at the headquarters of the Cambodian People's Party, Chamkar Leu district.
The event was attended by Dr. Hang Chuon Naron, Deputy Prime Minister, Member of the Standing Committee of the Central Committee of the Cambodian People's Party and First Vice-Chairman of the Kampong Cham Provincial Working Group, Member of the Senate, National Assembly and Royal Government as Vice-Chairman of the Party Working Group. Assisted the province and chaired the party's deputy working group to visit more than 600 districts.
Deputy Prime Minister Santi Dr. Neth Savoeun highlighted some of the challenges that our officials need to recognize and work together to correct:
* First, the problem of public services, the service is still slow, in which the local authorities, our officials still have the attitude of inappropriate words, so need to improve
