Obey traffic rules, drive carefully every second! 6 killed and 6 injured in traffic accidents nationwide on December 23 yesterday
(Phnom Penh): According to the report of the General Commission of the National Police, on December 23, 2023, there were seven traffic accidents across the country, resulting in six deaths and six minor injuries.
At the operation site, they were led by Senior Minister Kun Kim, First Vice President of the National Committee for Disaster Management, Mr. Khuong Sreng, Governor of Phnom Penh, Mr. Mean Chanyada, Deputy Governor and Lt. Gen. Chuon Narin, Deputy Commissioner and Commissioner. Phnom Penh police, as well as specialized forces and local authorities.
According to the report of the Fire Prevention and Rescue Office of the Phnom Penh Municipal Police, during the 3 nights 4 days, the police used 52 fire trucks and used a total of 3,797 water trucks with a total force in More than 400 rescue operations.
Although the fire was completely under control, on the night of December 23, 2023, Colonel Prohm Yorn, Director of the Office of Fire Prevention and Rescue, continued to deploy his specialized office to stand another night at the scene. Fearing that there would be a gap or something, the flames could be re-ignited, while other units were allowed to return to the unit.
Senior Minister Kun Kim expressed his gratitude and admiration for the rescue forces of all units that cooperated well to completely control the fire. He considered this an additional experience for the rescue force, as the location of the building was complicated and difficult to access.
