Monks set fire to a wood factory at Svay Chek Chas pagoda, Romduol district, Svay Rieng province
(Svay Rieng): There is a case of fire caused by monks collecting garbage and burning it in flames, which spread to the wood factory in Svay Chek Chas pagoda. Completely extinguished.
This incident happened at 10 pm on December 23, 2023 at Wat Svay Chek Chas, Svay Chek village, Svay Chek commune, Romduol district, Svay Rieng province.
Prior to the incident, at around 6 pm, the monks in the pagoda collected garbage and burned it in the fire, and at about 7-8 pm, the monks went up to the roof and disappeared. At 10 o'clock at night, suddenly heard a startling sound, the monks in the pagoda were coming up to help put out the fire, but could not put out the fire, so they reported to the police to use fire trucks to spray water to control 100%, including the use of fire water The fire destroyed more than 20 cars.
Authorities confirmed that the amount of damage to the pile of fire is not yet known because the authorities are working and in this incident did not cause the fire to spread to the pavilion or other achievements in the pagoda, just burned the wood shed. He left to use is almost completely burned.
