(Phnom Penh): The "Angkor Writing" program is an important event in the promotion of Khmer literature, especially to help the general public to change the spelling habits in writing and reading Khmer words correctly, while the general public Ministry The private sector has been very supportive of this important program.
We can call this Angkor Writing Program a Khmer Literacy Competition because it is a competition to write essays in Khmer language, which is open to people from all walks of life, regardless of age, gender, race or role to choose. The winner who writes the Khmer words correctly.
Mr. Lim Bunhok, the initiator of the Angkor Writing Program, in a press conference on 22 December 2023, explained that seeing the mistakes in writing, the use of Khmer words was not good or limited in Cambodian society. Now, he and his friends have agreed to initiate this Angkor writing program and find many partners, including in the media.
Mr. Bun Hok continued that this important program will be officially held on the morning of January 21, 2024 at the bridge in front of Angkor Wat, Siem Reap. The duration of the competition is about an hour and the topic is related to Angkor, the land of wonders of the Khmer nation, the former capital of Cambodia during the Angkor Empire for more than 600 years.
Currently, the program team is receiving registration from the public, students, foreigners, while so far there are about 500 people registered. He said that the program can receive a maximum of about 1,000 participants. For those who want to participate in the competition, please hurry to register by telegram above, because the registration deadline is January 7, 2023.
According to Lim Bunhok, this literacy program to promote national literature is very popular in France, which mobilizes French people to compete and gain a lot of knowledge from writing words in their language.
