Russia's economy resists Western sanctions
The Kremlin remains confident of continuing to finance the war in Ukraine, with experts predicting gross domestic product (GDP) growth of between 1 and 3 percent next year.
The increase comes as European leaders consider another round of sanctions aimed at putting pressure on Moscow to stop the war. Russia is currently the most heavily sanctioned country in the world.
Some observers have said that measures taken by the West do not seem to be working and that Russia's financial future looks optimistic.
