(Phnom Penh): The Prime Minister of Cambodia, Samdech Thibodi Hun Manet, presided over the closing ceremony of the Ministry of Commerce on 20 December 2023 to review the business results of 2023 and 2024. Two days ago.
The conference is designed to review and evaluate the achievements of the Ministry over the past year, as well as to discuss in depth and address challenges and implement directions for the next year in line with the first phase of the Pentagon's political program and strategy. Royal Government, 7th legislature of the National Assembly.
The following are the main contents of Samdech Thibodi Hun Manet, the opportunity to close the meeting to summarize the business results:
* Samdech Thipadei Hun Manet highly appreciated and appreciated Mr. Pan Sosak, Ms. Chamnimol and commercial officials who achieved excellent results. In particular, the trade volume reached more than 43 billion US dollars.
* Hun Manet praised the leaders and officials of the Ministry of Commerce for reaching trade agreements with partner countries, especially free trade, which opened up additional markets for Cambodian products.
Samdech Samdech Hun Manet said that it is not yet a market, but if it is, it will be very dangerous to lose it. In particular, the loss due to the seller makes the buyer lose confidence.
* Samdech Manipadei Hun Manet stated that new markets must be found and old markets must be maintained.
Samdech Samdech Hun Manet stated that we must work together to diversify the market. Eggs Do not put in one basket, put in as many baskets. Avoid breaking one basket or breaking the other.
* Samdech Thipadei Hun Manet stated that in order to open the Cambodian market, it is necessary to use the strategy of knocking on doors, not just handing over documents to others.
* Samdech Thipadei Hun Manet stated that every time Samdech goes abroad, Samdech always instructs the Minister not to sit next to Samdech and to organize a meeting with stakeholders to find investment opportunities.
* President Hun Manet stated that the state must play a role in opening the door for the private sector and must provide opportunities for the private sector to participate. Government institutions need to reduce the complexity associated with doing business in the private sector.
* Samdech Thipadei Hun Manet instructed the Ministry of Commerce to disseminate market-related information widely to producers and stakeholders.
* Samdech Thipadei Hun Manet stated that Samdech has two formulas for product marketing. The first is to have a product and go to the market and the second is to determine the market and then produce the next product.
* Samdech Thipadei Hun Manet decided to set up a working group to study and download local furniture to meet local needs through the allocation of the national budget to support. This program is scheduled to be implemented in 2025.
* Samdech Thipadei Hun Manet shared some recommendations as an additional contribution to the work direction of the Ministry of Commerce.
* The Ministry of Commerce must participate with a high sense of responsibility in eliminating barriers to trade and business to create a favorable environment for domestic trade activities and serve exports.
* The Ministry of Commerce must provide all kinds of support to promote Cambodian enterprises, both formal and informal, to be competitive and to be able to connect to regional and global supply chains.
* The Ministry of Commerce must strengthen governance and private sector development by focusing on the management of trade associations and private enterprises.
* The Ministry of Commerce must participate in promoting the production of local products and develop strategies to promote the use of Cambodian products.
* Establishment of representatives of the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce in potential countries, as well as the establishment of business associations and products to participate in the supply chain and seize business opportunities.
* The Ministry of Commerce must pay attention to continue to research and register more GI trademarks and collective trademarks in order to improve the quality and brand of Cambodian products in the domestic and foreign markets by developing strategies. Reduce imports of goods that Cambodia can produce.
* Through the strategy of strengthening old markets and expanding new markets, the Ministry of Commerce must continue to negotiate market opening and export promotion in collaboration with relevant ministries and institutions, as well as the private sector, to develop strategies to take advantage of regional and bilateral free trade agreements. Parties.
* The Ministry of Commerce must be prepared to negotiate for a new preference through the GSP Plus system in order to maintain the market and maintain production balance and attractiveness for investment in Cambodia.
