Banteay Meanchey Provincial Police issued a press release regarding the nine Thais fleeing from Poipet to Thailand, accusing them of cheating the Big Brother to work in an illegal casino
(Phnom Penh): A spokesman for the Banteay Meanchey Provincial Police on December 22, 2023, issued a press release stating that nine Thais had stolen from a workplace in Poipet City and returned to Thailand. They cheated large groups to work in illegal casinos.
A spokesman for the Banteay Meanchey Provincial Police confirmed that on December 19, 2023, Thai media reported that nine Thais had fled across the border into Thai territory for rescue by Thai authorities on December 18. 2023, claiming that cheating the Big Brother led to work in an illegal casino in Poipet.
The team inspected the scene of the fire in the dormitory of employee A7 in the apartment building in the Poly Casino in Kbal Spean 2 village, Sangkat O'Chrov, which is suspected of involving nine Thai nationals illegally crossing into Thailand. On December 18, 2023.
According to the results of careful research by the competent experts and listening to the explanations of those involved in the above incident, it was found that nine Thai people had an argument, set fire to the bedroom and used violence on the security during the arrest by Fearing arrest by the authorities to enforce the law, they escaped by jumping over a barbed wire fence, causing injuries and illegally crossing the border into Thailand on December 18, 2023.
As for the use of violence and detention of nine Thai nationals, the authorities have not yet found any relevant evidence as alleged by the Thai media.
