Dr. Sok Touch requested the Korean side to continue to support the Asian Research Center of the Royal Academy of Cambodia
(Phnom Penh): Dr. Sok Touch, President of the Royal Academy of Cambodia, requested the Victory Institute for Higher Education of the Republic of Korea to continue to support the Asian Research Center of the Royal Academy of Cambodia in order to be able to organize an international conference to find input for ASEAN governments and The Republic of Korea in further enhancing the relationship between ASEAN and the Republic of Korea.
He made the request at the opening ceremony of the 18th Annual International Conference on "Korea-ASEAN Solidarity Initiative: Restoring Socio-Economic Connectivity" organized by the Royal Academy of Cambodia on the morning of December 22. This 2023.
The four objectives of the 18th International Conference are:
* First, an overview of the history of ASEAN-Korea relations over the last 30 years.
* Second: Gather ideas to be an input to the governments of both Cambodia and Korea in contributing to the strengthening of the relationship between Cambodia and Korea to be even better.
* Third: Discuss the general aspects of ASEAN-Korea relations in general and with Cambodia in particular.
* Fourth: Analyze and evaluate the strengths, weaknesses, challenges and opportunities and expectations of ASEAN-Republic of Korea relations in the context of the New World Order.
Once again, Dr. Sok Touch commends the efforts of the Conference Organizing Committee of the Asian Research Center of the Royal Academy of Cambodia and relevant institutions to achieve proud results today. Finally, he wished the international conference success in all three topics and wished him good health, a smile and love.
