Israel claims 2,000 more Hamas members killed in December, a total of 9,000 since the outbreak of war
JERUSALEM (Reuters) - The Israeli military on Thursday claimed that since the ceasefire on the Gaza Strip erupted on December 1, its forces have killed more than 2,000 members. Others of Hamas Palestine through air strikes and ground offensive operations. This was released by the AFP news agency on Friday, December 22, 2023.
This brings the Israeli military's estimate of the number of Hamas fighters killed in Gaza since the war broke out on July 7 to about 8,000. According to the Israeli military, another 1,000 Hamas members were also killed in Israeli territory during a large-scale Palestinian militant raid on Israel on the same day.
