(Phnom Penh): A four-week training course on the use of Nivel heavy machinery on the Cambodia-Japan bilateral project in Cambodia was successfully concluded on the morning of December 22, 2023.
The four-week Cambodia-Japan Bilateral Training Project on the Control and Use of Nivel Heavy Engineering Machinery with 18 participants. This training provided training to the Cambodian Blue Hat Forces in the use of machinery, as well as developing the ability to become trainers to ensure effective participation in peacekeeping operations, quality and high capacity.
She said the project was implemented to support the deployment of Cambodian forces to UN peacekeeping missions. In addition, in the future, the Ministry of National Defense and the Japanese Self-Defense Forces will continue to strengthen defense cooperation with Cambodia, a strategic partner in all aspects.
He praised the diligence of the Cambodian trainees in their efforts to control high-tech machinery with the guidance of the Japanese military. Through this project, Taninai Ichimoto believes that cooperation between the two countries will be further strengthened.
Lt. Gen. Tan Saly said that the course completed now is another source of pride for our motherland and a beacon for the Cambodian trainees by bringing better knowledge and skills.
Heng Sour: The Royal Government is willing to reduce illegal migration and protect the rights of Cambodian workers abroad
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Heng Sour, Minister of Labor and Vocational Training, on Friday morning, December 22, 2023, stated that the Royal Government of Cambodia, led by His Majesty the King Hun Manet, is committed and willing to reduce migration. Illegal districts and promote and protect the rights of Cambodian workers working abroad.
In addition to the protection, the Royal Government as well as the Ministry of Labor have organized various religious ceremonies such as Pchum Ben New Year and other festivals in the target countries to provide warmth to the workers who are far from their hometowns, and these events will continue. Prepare more as well.
At the same time, the Minister also emphasized to the ceremony that in the seventh mandate, the Department of Migration has become an important program and a priority for the Ministry to pay attention to promote and protect the rights of Cambodian citizens abroad. As well as foreigners working in Cambodia.
However, the Minister called on all stakeholders to continue to work closely with the Royal Government as well as the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training with a high sense of responsibility, ethics and professional conscience to unite. Each achieves the common goal of promoting the protection of the rights and legitimate benefits of migrant workers.
