President Hun Manet Asks Japan to Collaborate with Cambodia to Transform Sihanoukville Autonomous Port into a Regional Logistics Center (Video inside) (Preah Sihanouk) Aim to develop Sihanoukville Autonomous Port to become a logistics center for the region.
To help achieve this goal, the Prime Minister requested the Royal Government of Japan to cooperate with Cambodia in preparing a master plan and encourage the Japanese private sector to develop Sihanoukville Port into a regional logistics center.
This proposal was made on the occasion of Samdech inaugurating the construction site of the first phase of deep water container terminal at Sihanoukville Autonomous Port worth $ 243 million on the morning of December 22, 2023.
The Prime Minister also urged the consideration of more locations to be ready to expand the scope, because the establishment of logistics centers for the region requires a larger location.
Please note that Sihanoukville Autonomous Port has been playing an important role in contributing to support the growth and development of the nation. Freight through the port is increasing significantly from year to year, making the port's revenue as well as national revenue increase steadily.
For the construction of the deep-water container port, the first step to be opened today is 350 meters long and 14.5 meters deep. The container port will be able to accommodate container vessels with a capacity of 60,000 tons or 4,000 TEUs, with transit routes in the Asia-Pacific region to the Sihanoukville Autonomous Port, and will increase the total port capacity to approximately 1.25. Millions of TEUs per year.
After the completion of the first phase of construction, the Royal Government plans to expand the construction of the second and third phases. The second phase will allow container vessels with a capacity of 120,000 tons or the equivalent of 10,000 TEUs to transport goods within the Indo-Pacific region to the Sihanoukville Autonomous Port and will increase the total port capacity to more than 1.8 million. TEUs per year.
The third phase will allow container vessels with a capacity of 160,000 tons, or 15,000 TEUs, to transport goods within Europe, the United States and around the world to the Sihanoukville Autonomous Port without having to pass through other ports in No more in the region. The container port will increase the total port capacity to about 2.5 million TEUs per year.
His Excellency Hun Manet said this on December 22, 2023, on the occasion of presiding over the groundbreaking ceremony for the construction of the first phase of the deep-water container port worth 243 million dollars in Sihanoukville Autonomous Port, Sihanoukville Province. Sihanoukville.
According to the report of Mr. Lou Kimchhun, the Royal Government delegate in charge of the Director General of Sihanoukville Autonomous Port now, the cost of shipping per container is nearly $ 700. Ready to reduce more than $ 200 per container to transport goods to this deep-sea port more through cheaper shipping to Cambodia.
Samdech Hun Manet: The Royal Government will turn Sihanoukville Autonomous Port into a regional logistics center (Video inside) (Preah Sihanouk) This reflects the vision of the Royal Government of Cambodia in transforming Sihanoukville Autonomous Port into a regional logistics center.
On the occasion of the groundbreaking ceremony for the construction of the first phase of the deep-water container port at Sihanoukville Autonomous Port worth $ 243 million, Samdech Maniphath Hun Manet reminded that in the past, Sihanoukville Autonomous Port only served to import agricultural products from abroad. But now it has become a potential port not only for Cambodia, but for the region as well.
Samdech Hun Sen stated that the goal of transforming the port into a regional logistics center is the goal that the previous government, with Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the former Prime Minister, has already set the direction for construction, and the new government. Will continue to work on this as well.
"This is the goal that the previous government of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the former Prime Minister, has set in the construction of this port for many terms, and we have reached a new stage," said Hun Manet. "In the future, we will do more work to turn this port not only into a container port but also a regional logistics center."
According to Samdech Hun Manet, the vision of the Royal Government of Cambodia's efforts to turn the potential of this region into a potential that serves the regional and international trade sector to connect Cambodia with the international region and be the lifeblood of Cambodia's economy. Without having to rely on foreigners.
His Excellency Hun Manet added that Cambodia now has a port, but the capacity and possibilities are limited, so it means that ships can not come to this place, having to rely on neighboring ports to transfer goods, resulting in loss and loss. More competition, but when completed, it will be easier and more profitable for Cambodia.
