France to close embassy in Niger
PARIS (Reuters) - France will close its embassy in Niger, where anti-French sentiment has been on the rise since a coup in July, the embassy said on Monday. Many have left the country after an attack on the embassy. This was released by the AFP news agency on Friday, December 22, 2023.
