(Phnom Penh): On the morning of Friday, March 22, 2023, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, Samdech Moha Bovathibodi Hun Manet, presided over the groundbreaking ceremony for the construction of the deep-sea container port. 1 is located in Kampong Autonomous Region, Sihanoukville, Preah Sihanouk Province.
The second and third phases of the new deep-water container terminal are expected to cost a total of 698 million US dollars, of which more than 500 million US dollars will be concessional loans from the Japanese government and more than 100 million US dollars. Contribution of the Royal Government of Cambodia.
According to the feasibility study, the construction project of these three new container ports will transform the capacity of Sihanoukville Autonomous Port, which is now a small international port, into a competitive large international port, which allows large container vessels from Every area in the world can be docked easily and quickly without any water depth restrictions.
Along with the groundbreaking ceremony for the construction of the first phase of the deep-sea container port, there was also the official inauguration of two mobile cranes on the edge of the port, a type of crane with a capacity of up to 100 tons. . Both machines are a grant from the Government of Japan to the Royal Government of Cambodia under the Economic and Social Development Program with a total budget of approximately 13.9 million US dollars.
In addition, the volume of containers passing through the Sihanoukville Autonomous Port totaled more than 750,000 TEUs, an average increase of 10.83 percent in the last 12 years from 2010 to 2022.
Six Thais Arrested for Poisoning in Poipet
(Banteay Meanchey): Six Thai men and women who came to stay in Poipet City actively smoked and sold drugs, were arrested and confiscated a large amount of drugs by the police force. The crackdown took place on the night of December 20, 2023 at Borey Thi Thi in O'Chrov village, Sangkat O'Chrov, Poipet city, Banteay Meanchey province.
According to police, the arrests of the six Thais were made under the command of Banteay Meanchey provincial police chief Major General Sithi Loh.
The General Commissioner ordered professional officers to crack down on all drugs in Banteay Meanchey province, whether smoking or selling. After receiving the order, the specialized force investigated and arrested six smokers and drug dealers and brought them to the Poipet City Inspector for questioning.
With the permission of Major General Sithi Loh and the coordination of the procedure by Mr. Lim Bun Sopheak, Deputy Prosecutor of Banteay Meanchey Provincial Court, the specialized police force sent the six suspects to the Provincial Police for questioning and construction. The case was sent to court for further legal proceedings.
