BEIJING (Reuters) - In December 1978, China launched one of its most important policies, which had a profound effect on the nation's destiny: "reform and openness." It is a great historical turning point that guides the giant ships of China towards development and prosperity and brings China back to the world.
Forty-five years ago, China became one of the world's poorest countries and the first country in the world to lift its poor out of poverty. This miraculous cause is recorded in the pages of human history, and China's experience and poverty reduction policy have been included in several UN General Assembly resolutions to share with other countries.
