(Phnom Penh): On the afternoon of Thursday, March 9, 2023, which is on December 21, 2023, Samdech Moha Bovathibodi Hun Manet, Prime Minister of Cambodia, will preside over the closing ceremony of the 2023 work review meeting. Work direction 2024 of the Ministry of Environment.
As a way of governing the government, as well as ministries, state institutions hold annual meetings and joint meetings at the end of the year to review the results of their work throughout the year and set out action plans to be done for The new year continues.
The Ministry of Environment has convened a meeting to review the work in 2023 and raise the work direction in 2024 for two days, on December 20 and 21, 2023. The two-day conference was attended by ministry leaders, government officials, as well as government officials from the Department of Environment across the country.
The two-day conference highlighted the achievements of officials under the joint management of the Ministry of Environment in 2023, such as: building a modern digital administration, sustainable development, and environmental protection. , Natural Resource Protection and Conservation, Local Community Development, Environmental Education and Dissemination, Environmental Environment, Social Affairs and Cooperation and Foreign Affairs.
In addition to presenting the results of the work, the conference also presented challenges and suggestions for further implementation in 2024 to be more effective.
In this conference, the Ministry also highlighted the results and achievements of more than 100 days of the Ministry of Environment after the formation of the new Royal Government.
For more than 100 days, the Royal Government of the 7th Legislature of the National Assembly, under the leadership of Samdech Moha Bovathibodi Hun Manet, the Ministry of Environment and the National Council for Sustainable Development, has been working hard to fully cooperate and achieve important achievements. As follows:
Second, the Ministry also initiated the campaign "Plant 1 million trees per year" on October 10, 2023 in order to expand forest cover throughout the country. The Ministry encourages the public to participate in tree planting by the Ministry of Environment has organized nurseries and announced the distribution of free seedlings to the public who wish to participate in tree planting.
Third, the Ministry has put in place the strictest measures to prevent natural resource crimes by ending all cultures, signing contracts to release natural resource perpetrators, and promoting 100 percent law enforcement.
Fourth, the Ministry has been approved to implement the "Environmental Strategy" 2023-2028, with three angles, including "strengthening policy, building digital administration and expanding dissemination" aimed at becoming a carbon neutral country. And 60% forest cover by 2050 "in response to global efforts to achieve the pentagonal strategic goals.
Fifth, the Ministry has continued to support and improve the livelihood of local communities by promoting ecotourism and mobilizing private sector participation to increase employment as well as encourage protected area communities to plant useful trees and become more neutral. Carbon.
Seventh, the Ministry has set up an internet system that is faster, more secure and can cover the use of the entire Ministry of Administration building, which is a necessary step in modernizing the institution and responding to the development of the technology industry 4.0.
Eighth, the Ministry has continued to strengthen bilateral and multilateral environmental cooperation in solving global problems, and has received additional support and cooperation in expanding the scope of the Ministry's campaign and priorities, especially in reducing the use of plastics. Expansion of forest cover and improvement of livelihoods of local communities.
