At a time when the world is suffering from the spread of Kovid-19 and the negative impact of the conflict between Russia and Ukraine in early 2022, which caused a sharp rise in global commodity prices, as well as disasters. Severe floods in some provinces in Cambodia The Royal Government has launched a number of urgent social assistance interventions to help absorb the pressure of rising inflation and reduce the economic vulnerability of the poor and vulnerable.
After the cash assistance program for vulnerable families during inflationary pressures and floods ended, the National Council for Social Protection and the United Nations Development Program (UNDP) conducted a joint assessment, finding that social assistance interventions These two in particular have contributed significantly to reducing the negative consequences on vulnerable families.
In fact, more than 97% of the target households are satisfied and support the intervention as a financial support of the Royal Government, with the beneficiaries to use the necessary expenditures as expected, especially the cost of food, health services and medicines, education. Of children, water, electricity, rent, and other necessary expenses.
The results of this assessment also show that almost 100% of the target households, especially the vulnerable families who receive cash subsidies, have a positive view of the Royal Government and local authorities, which contributes to raising and strengthening the spirit of Citizens come to the Royal Government more.
With these positive results and suffixes, a number of challenges are also highlighted, such as limited awareness of vulnerable families about identification and a small number of target households experiencing problems when paying subsidies due to Wing Bank counters. Away from their homes.
Under the high guidance and clear vision of His Excellency Hun Manet, Prime Minister of Cambodia, the National Council for Social Protection, chaired by Dr. Aun Porn Moniroth, Deputy Prime Minister, Minister of Economy and Finance, has been considering And as a system in line with the progress of the development of the social protection system.
