(Phnom Penh): Wing Tower Bank, a unique architectural building and a symbol of creative talent, was officially inaugurated in the heart of Phnom Penh. With a height of up to 120 meters on a busy boulevard, the Wing Tower Bank is a testament to the growth of the digital banking sector in Cambodia.
The official inauguration ceremony was presided over by His Excellency Hun Manet, Prime Minister of Cambodia, on the morning of December 20, 2023, in the presence of Duke Kith Meng, CEO of Royal Group and Chairman of the Board of Directors of the Bank. Wing, with the participation of senior government officials and many other business people, has made this event one of the most important events of the financial sector in Cambodia.
The 25-storey Wing Tower Bank, the headquarters of Wing Bank, is one of the leading financial institutions that has evolved from a complete money transfer service provider. This three-story section of the building is specially designed to provide banking services to general customers as well as VIP and VVIP guests in the most luxurious and private banking services.
In addition to these attractions, Wing Tower also has an Innovation Center, a location for Wing Bank to pursue its active vision of leading the development of digital solutions tailored to the needs of all Cambodians. Thinking forward to becoming a bank that combines traditional banking services and Wing Bank's digital capabilities is clearly visible on the walls of Wing Tower.
With its state-of-the-art artificial intelligence Wing Bank App, customers can easily enjoy a wide range of financial services at their fingertips. Wing Bank's commitment to the environment and its financial authority is reflected in the significant growth of its business operations.
Wing Bank currently has 21 operating offices along with 15,000 Wing networks serving more than 14.5 million users. This remarkable achievement was achieved thanks to the solidarity and participation of the entire team and staff, which now number nearly 3,000, with a focus on gender equality and empowerment. To women in the banking sector.
