French Embassy in Cambodia Inaugurates New Visa Application Center for France and Other European Countries
(Phnom Penh): A new center for applying for visas to France and other European countries was inaugurated on December 19, 2023 on the 5th floor of Vattanac Building.
At the inauguration of the center, the French Ambassador to Cambodia, Jacques Pellegrini, said that from December 13, visa applications to France and 12 other European countries (Schengen) would take place at the TLScontact in Phnom Penh. Selected to receive the public, provide information, arrange visa applications and collect fees. Passport withdrawals are also made at the center.
He said that the selection of the above center to accept visa applications shows the willingness of the French Embassy to improve the reception conditions for the growing number of visa applicants, as well as to reduce the duration of appointments and services. Extra to ensure the optimal comfort of the visa applicant.
Please be reminded that all Cambodians must apply for a visa to be able to travel to France, regardless of the length of stay or hold any travel document (official passport or diplomacy), unless they have a card. Stay in France, valid for stay in France or any country of the Schengen area.
