Samdech Mani President Hun Manet issued some recommendations in the 20th Editorial Forum of Cambodian Press, continue to participate in the fight against false information that pollutes society and leads to social unrest
(Phnom Penh): Through the congratulatory message of the 20th Editorial Forum of the Cambodian Press on December 21, 2023, His Excellency Hun Manet, Prime Minister of Cambodia, in addition to the congratulations, also provided some recommendations to be Basis for discussion, solving problems related to violations of professional ethics, dissemination of false information, distorting facts, polluting society, insulting and inciting hostility, disintegration of national unity.
* First, to continue to participate in maintaining peace, national development, and strengthening democracy based on the implementation of the law, professional ethics, and to eliminate opportunists who take refuge under the label of the press.
* Second: Provide true information to the national and international public about the real situation in Cambodia and disseminate the Royal Government's policy to the people and bring information from the people to the Royal Government to solve problems in a timely and effective manner.
* Third: To be a mirror of reality and inactivity in society for the Royal Government to solve problems effectively in accordance with the reform program of the Royal Government.
* Fourth: Educate the public about measures to prevent traffic accidents, dangers of drug use, human trafficking, safe village and commune policy to reduce traffic accidents, drug use and maintain social safety.
* Fifth: Continue to participate in the fight against false information that is polluting the society can cause national instability, political unrest, chaos and loss of social order.
* Sixth: Adhere to professional ethics, publish true information, be balanced in all aspects, avoid disseminating information that harms national interests and loses public trust.
* Seventh: Training the professional skills of journalists, both technical and professional, to improve the quality of information, media order and prestige of the media.
