79 articles related to the working visit of Prime Minister Hun Manet to Japan to attend the ASEAN-Japan Anniversary Summit
The following is information related to the working visit of Samdech Manet Hun Manet to Japan:
(Phnom Penh): Through a press conference after a high-level delegation of the Royal Government of Cambodia led by His Excellency Hun Manet, Prime Minister of Cambodia, returned to the country on the night of December 19, 2023, Mr. Sonaro, Minister accompanying The Prime Minister in charge of ASEAN Affairs presented the results of the 50th Anniversary Meeting of ASEAN-Japan Relations.
Dr. Sonaro confirmed that on the morning of December 17, 2023, His Excellency Hun Manet attended the opening ceremony of the 50th Anniversary Summit in the presence of Mr. Kishida Fermio, Prime Minister of Japan and Chief of Staff. Lead other ASEAN countries as well.
In his opening remarks, Kishida Fermio said that ASEAN-Japan relations have been underway for half a century, and ASEAN has expanded to become a trading partner, investment and other sectors, and people-to-people exchanges. People.
He expects that in the next 50 years, ASEAN-Japan will increase closer ties based on the trust that has been built in the past. The Japanese Prime Minister affirmed that ASEAN-Japan will jointly address current and future challenges to ensure and maintain the Asia-Pacific region as a free, open and prosperous region.
During the First Plenary Session, President Hun Manet intervened, emphasizing that the current ASEAN-Japan Memorial Summit is a historic event of a long-standing partnership and a turning point. Another of these relationships is to promote peace, common growth and sustainable development to create golden friendships and golden opportunities that truly benefit our people.
The Prime Minister of Cambodia added that 2023 is very meaningful for the people of Cambodia because ASEAN-Japan has established a comprehensive strategic partnership at the ASEAN level, while Cambodia this year is also the 70th anniversary of the relationship. Diplomacy between Japan and Cambodia has also been raised to the same level. "Cambodia is doubly happy with its wonderful and traditional friendship with Japan," he said.
Later, the second session on the evening of the same day focused on two topics, including: first: partners and passions of all generations, and second: partners for co-creation of the economy and society of the future. In that, Samdech Thipadei Hun Manet stated two other interventions separately, expressing his happiness when he saw that the past implementation has been fruitful.
According to Dr. Sonaro, President Hun Manet said that the unpredictability and unpredictability of the regional and global framework, cooperation, friendship and kindness are important in promoting people-to-people contacts. And people, trust and understanding of ASEAN-Japan solidarity. Reduce the gap and digital technology, promote joint development, human resource development.
Samdech Hun Sen also praised the cooperation between Japan and Cambodia in the fields of education, technology, science, social protection, exchange visits, study, culture, society and so on.
President Hun Manet also expressed support for the ASEAN-Japan New Generation Automotive Industry Co-Initiative, an initiative of Kishida Fermio, which could raise $ 35 billion in both public and private funds over the next five years. Samdech announced that Cambodia hopes to become a component of this initiative as well.
The meeting concluded the adoption of two important documents: the Joint Vision Statement on ASEAN-Japan Friendship and Cooperation as a Trusted Partner and a detailed plan to implement this declaration.
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Son Naro, Minister Delegate to the Prime Minister in charge of ASEAN Affairs, stated that the opposition in Japan has failed miserably in asking Japan not to recognize Samdech Hun Manet as the Prime Minister of Cambodia, but on the contrary Descended the stairs on the red carpet and attended the ASEAN Summit in a fair and equitable manner with all Heads of State.
In this regard, Mr. Sonaro stated that the opposition group forgot that at the time of the election on July 23, 2023, 82.3% of Cambodians who went to the polls had their black fingers dipped. Already voted for the CPP, and to put it simply, out of 1,000 people, 823 voted for the CPP, a number that has never been in the history of the CPP.
Mr. Sonaro added that in addition, Cambodia also attended the bilateral meeting, with the Cabinet of Ministers of Japan, the Minister of Security Advisers, and the Deputy Prime Minister of Cambodia face each other, equal negotiations between Cambodia equal rights. Again, we see that the reality is one of the highest levels of recognition that the Prime Minister represents the Royal Government of Japan and Cambodia.
He added that in addition to the hearing before the Emperor of Japan, who is the head of state of Japan, it is the recognition level not only of the government, but also the level of the head of state who receives the accession of Samdech. His Excellency Hun Manet with Lok Chumteav Dr. Pech Chanmony Hun Manet, this is another recognition from the head of state, so the opposition calling for Japan not to recognize the Cambodian government is a complete failure.
Mr. Sonaro stated that the second defeat of the opposition is that the number of participants in the demonstration is very small compared to previous years, the march is also less than about 100 people compared to the meeting of His Majesty the King Hun Manet. There are more than 2,000, so the movement is dwindling because people have lost faith in the extremist, adventurous, extremist politics.
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Son Naro, Minister Delegate to the Prime Minister, said that ASEAN and Japan have been partners since 2013 and have been fruitful, and President Hun Manet hopes that Japan will continue to provide short-term scholarships. And long-term training courses for more research in Cambodia.
Mr. Sonaro said that through his intervention speech, Mr. Hun Manet stated that the organization of the 50th Anniversary Summit of ASEAN-Japan Relations is now a historic event of a long-term partnership. And a new chapter in the relationship of promoting peace, common growth and sustainable development to create a "golden friendship and golden opportunity" that truly benefits the people.
Mr. Sonaro quoted President Hun Manet as saying that 2023 is a very meaningful year for the Cambodian people because ASEAN and Japan have established a strategic partnership at all levels at the ASEAN level and Cambodia and Japan think 2023 marks the 70th anniversary of the establishment of diplomatic ties between the two countries, and has been upgraded to a strategic partnership.
Mr. Sonaro added that the creation of unpredictability and unpredictability of regional and global frameworks makes cooperation partners, friendly and pious partners important in promoting people-to-people contacts, trust and confidence. Understand the solidarity between ASEAN and Japan.
At the same time, Mr. Sonaro stated that through cooperation, friendship and friendship between Japan and ASEAN, the technological and digital gap has been narrowed, and joint development and human resource development have been promoted. "Samdech Hun Manet hopes that Japan will continue to provide short-term and long-term scholarships, training courses, as well as vocational training to Cambodia," Sonaro said in a statement.
He added that on that occasion, Samdech Hun Sen also welcomed and supported the announcement of the launch of a 40 billion yen people-to-people exchange program focused on the exchange of young businessmen, civil servants and research officials. .
Mr. Sonaro also stated that President Hun Manet also praised the cooperation between Japan and Cambodia in the fields of education, technology, medicine, social protection, exchange visits, study, culture, society, etc. And so on.
