5. Promoting research in collaboration with more national and international partners to find new discoveries as an important input in health policy formulation and strategy, especially in future training.
6: Continue to strengthen the partnership between the university and internship at all levels.
On that occasion, the Minister called on the leaders of all hospitals and internships to continue to support close cooperation with the University to help provide professors who come to teach at the University of Health Sciences and provide professors. Help strengthen the quality of internships for students to be good and pay high attention.
On that occasion, Prof. Minister Chheang Ra thanked all the partner organizations that have supported the university in the past and sincerely hope that all partners will work hard to cooperate well with the University of Health Sciences. Continuing.
At the same time, the Minister encouraged all students to make every effort to learn with all their physical, mental and intellectual strength. In addition, we must work together to promote and adhere to professional ethics both at school and at the end of the profession.
Please be informed that on the occasion of Prof. Chheang Ra presiding over the opening of the new school year, the Minister provided recommendations as well as additional tips to the leaders, professors, parents and students who participated.
At the same time, Prof. Saphon Vattanak, Advisor to the Ministry of Health and Rector of the University of Health Sciences, stated that with high attention and guidance from Professor Chheang Ra, the University has been working to strengthen And expand the quality of its training, research, innovation and service delivery to achieve excellence and quality recognition at the national, regional and international levels.
