(Phnom Penh): Dr. Ouk Rabun, Chairman of the Council for Agricultural and Rural Development and Chairman of the National Committee for the Promotion of One Village, One Product, on December 19, 2023, presided over the opening of a consultative workshop on strategic planning. Third National Food Security and Nutrition 2024-2028.
The consultation was attended by members of the Joint Technical Working Group on Food Security and Nutrition, the Capital-Provincial Coordinating Steering Committee for Food Security and Nutrition, and representatives of other relevant ministries and institutions to present the framework to be included in Development of the third National Strategy on Food Security and Nutrition 2024-2028.
This consultative workshop aims to set out priority strategies, sectoral responsibilities, cross-sectoral issues and priorities for multidisciplinary coordination, and to initiate an environmental policy process.
The workshop aims to clarify the roles and responsibilities at the sub-national level and gather participants' input on good and effective implementation activities implemented at the national and sub-national levels. The goal of the Third National Strategy on Food Security and Nutrition 2024-2028 is to achieve the first phase of the Royal Government's Pentagon Strategy and to contribute to policies and strategies in other areas.
This workshop will link with other consultations at the national and sub-national levels to achieve the achievement of the third National Strategy on Food Security and Nutrition 2024-2028.
The second review of the National Strategy on Food Security and Nutrition 2019-2023 reveals further implementation approaches in the implementation of the Third National Strategy on Food Security and Nutrition 2024-2028.
Key recommendations from the sub-national review are detailed below:
1. Start developing new strategies into sectoral responsibilities and frameworks, monitor and evaluate, and improve the process of preparing sectoral responsibilities and reducing duplicate reports.
5. Establish a clear food security and nutrition information system, ensuring that sub-nationals receive relevant information on planning and strengthening environmental practices.
6. Examine progress in capacity building at the sub-national level, including further reflections on efficiency and organization at the sub-national level. National.
7. Facilitate a comprehensive policy process based on lessons learned during the dialogue on the food system and use communication to broaden individual and social attitudes in the community.
This workshop will give a brief presentation on the review of the 2nd National Strategy on Food Security and Nutrition 2019-2023 and the direction for the 3rd National Strategy on Food Security and Nutrition 2024-2028, focusing on relevant aspects. Sub-national and key sectors (health, agriculture, water and sanitation).
(Tokyo-Japan): Through the Cambodia Investment 2023 seminar held in Tokyo, Japan this morning, December 19, 2023, Duke Kith Meng, President of the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce and Chairman of the ASEAN Business Advisory Council. He mentioned the great potential of Cambodia to attract Japanese investors to decide to invest more in Cambodia.
The Cambodia Investment Forum 2023 is co-organized by the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce, the Japan External Trade Organization, the Council for the Development of Cambodia and the Mizuho Bank under the chairmanship of His Excellency Hun Manet, Prime Minister of Cambodia, and with the participation of investors. Japan and Cambodia as well.
Speaking on the occasion, Duke Kith Meng said that Cambodia and Japan have a long history of friendship and cooperation. From the establishment of diplomatic ties in 1953 to the present, the two countries' ties have been strengthened and deepened. 2023 marks the 70th anniversary of diplomatic relations between Cambodia and Japan.
The two countries have enhanced bilateral relations to a comprehensive strategic partnership that reflects the depth and breadth of cooperation and mutual trust that have been built over the years.
He added that Japan is one of Cambodia's largest trade and investment partners and also one of the largest donors, making a significant contribution to Cambodia's socio-economic development. As of November 2023, Japan has invested $ 2.9 billion in 151 investment projects in Cambodia.
2023 is the 50th anniversary of ASEAN-Japan relations and also the year of ASEAN-Japan friendship and cooperation. ASEAN and Japan share a common vision for a peaceful, stable, prosperous and resilient region, an open and environmentally friendly region.
Cambodia is a member of ASEAN and a member of the Comprehensive Economic Partnership Agreement, a strategic location in the heart of Southeast Asia. Cambodia is one of the fastest growing economies in the region, with a growth rate of 7.7% per year for more than two decades.
Cambodia is a market base to RCEP countries. Cambodia is ideally located next to the most populous neighbors of Thailand (71 million) and Vietnam (98 million). Cambodia has a young and skilled workforce.
Japan can get a lot from Cambodia in terms of markets and economic cooperation, as well as strategic and political partnerships that can help Japan enhance its role and position in the region. The next 25 years are a turning point for Cambodia.
Cambodia enacted the Fiscal Law on May 16, 2023. This law aims to create an investment environment that is transparent, predictable and conducive to investment, as well as preventing tax evasion.
In addition, in 2021, the Investment Law is enacted with the main goal of creating a legal framework conducive to investment and attracting quality, efficient and effective investment to support socio-economic development.
The Royal Government of Cambodia, the seventh mandate, under the leadership of Samdech Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, has launched a Pentagon strategy, a long-term plan aimed at achieving Cambodia to become a high-middle-income country by 2030 and an income-generating country. High in 2050.
"I would like to encourage Japanese and Cambodian companies to find partners and invest more in Cambodia," he said. "To promote business and tourism activities, I would like to encourage ANA to reopen direct flights from Japan to Cambodia."
At the same time, the Duke, President of the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce, considered that the organization of the Cambodia Investment Workshop is the most appropriate time to exchange views and information, seek new opportunities and potential and find new partners, and this workshop will act as a motivator. Trade and investment flows, business cooperation and innovation, and mutual understanding and friendship between the two countries.
