(Pursat): Mr. Khoy Rida, Governor of Pursat Province and Chairman of the Provincial Administrative Unity Command, on December 18, 2023, led a team to inspect the fishery harvest of fishermen along the river in the province. Pursat from the border of Kampong Luong commune, Krakor district to the bottleneck of Boribo district, Kampong Chhnang province.
Speaking in a live interview with Fresh News, Khoy Rida said that the current visit is to inspect the fishery harvests of fishermen along the river in our geographical area of Pursat province. Falling or rising. In fact, during the 12 months of each year, the fish are flowing down the river, and our people are also starting to harvest fish to make prahok.
The governor of Pursat province added that at this point, if we let the fishermen fish as he pleases, the people below will not be able to catch fish to make prahok. Therefore, this visit is to check the dam along the river to make sure that the fish go in and out to distribute to our people to eat together.
In fact, today we see that the riel fish that our fishermen can wear nets is a lot of fish for today, tomorrow and the day after. This is due to the efforts of the head of the Royal Government as well as the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, as well as fisheries skills and total strength at all levels to maintain the sustainability of fish species to meet the needs of our people.
The governor of Khoy Rida province also said that our Minister of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries was very attentive, devoting the usual budget to the sub-national level to protect this fishery resource. At the same time, the provincial level, with him as the chairman of the Provincial Administrative Unity Command, is also determined to do this work together. As a result, in front of us, the fish resources are really increasing. .
On that occasion, Mr. Khoy Rida also handed out artifacts to the 11 national intervention forces and national intervention teams that are constantly monitoring the work to prevent and suppress fisheries crimes on the surface of the Tonle Sap Lake in Pursat province, including rice noodles. Fish sauce, soy sauce and some budget.
