SEOUL: Tensions on the Korean Peninsula have risen again as North Korea fired short- and long-range missiles following a warning from the United States that any North Korean attack on the United States The United States or its ally will suffer the outcome of North Korea
A confrontation on the Korean Peninsula has led to fears of another war in South Asia. North Korea fired at least one ballistic missile on Monday, December 18, just hours after launching one of its short-range missiles last night. .
No other force can come to mediate the conflict, while the United Nations has also opposed North Korea's nuclear weapons program. North Korea, in self-defense, sees its nuclear weapons program as a strong defensive belt in the face of Washington and its allies.
"The United States' commitment to the defense of the Republic of Korea and Japan remains strong," the statement said. The Allies will face a quick counterattack and the end of the North Korean regime.
