Military Arrests Two Thais for Poisoning in Poipet
(Banteay Meanchey): On December 15, 2023, the Poipet Municipal Gendarmerie Base Force, led by Brigadier General Nuon Ninaro, the Municipal Gendarmerie Local Commander, led a force to crack down on drug trafficking, storage and use. Addicted by detaining two Thai nationals at the residence building around the mouth of the stream in O'Chrov village, Sangkat O'Chrov, Poipet city, Banteay Meanchey province.
On the afternoon of December 18, 2023, the two suspects were sent to court for legal action.
Col. Nuon Ninaro said that the two suspects were named Akaraphon Senivong Na Yutaya, 28, a casino employee living in Kbal Spean 1 village, O'Chrov commune, and 25-year-old Chhay Yong Boon Song, alias Kim, a current casino employee. Staying at Kbal Spean 1 Village, Sangkat O'Chrov.
He said that before the crackdown, the Poipet City Gendarmerie received information from security that there were cases of drug trafficking, storage and illegal use of the above points.
He immediately led the force to the scene and arrested two suspects, including the confiscation of exhibits, including 3 small bags of white crystalline powder (ice), pills. 5 round red tiles (WY), small bags and small bags for some drug ports. After the arrest, the suspect was brought to the Municipal Gendarmerie Base for questioning.
After being arrested and questioned, the suspects admitted that the two men had actually trafficked, stored and used illegal drugs. Based on the confession and the actual evidence, the local force of the Municipal Gendarmerie has prepared a case file and sent it to the Provincial Gendarmerie Command to proceed with the procedure.
Colonel Chea Dara, Deputy Commander of the Provincial Gendarmerie in charge of anti-drug work, said that the crackdown was ordered by Brigadier General Born Bin, Commander of the Provincial Gendarmerie and coordinated the procedure from him. Born Vannareth, a prosecutor with the provincial court.
