(Phnom Penh): The International Organization for Migration (IOM) recently released its World Migration Report 2022, noting that there are four countries in ASEAN that send the largest number of migrants abroad. The Philippines, Indonesia and Burma or Myanmar and Vietnam and other countries sent more than 1 million people.
There are more than 3.4 million Vietnamese migrant workers, while Laos and Cambodia have more than 1.3 million respectively. Thailand, meanwhile, has more than 1.1 million migrant workers, while Malaysia and Singapore alone have the smallest number at less than 1 million. According to the same report.
The countries where ASEAN workers migrate the most are North America, Europe and major Middle Eastern countries such as Saudi Arabia and the United Arab Emirates and developed countries in Asia.
In the world, the country with the largest number of migrant workers is India, with more than 18 million people traveling abroad in search of work, followed by Mexico, China and Russia.
In Cambodia, more than 1.3 million people are working in Thailand, South Korea, Japan and other developed countries, and more than 1 billion deposits a year flow into the country to supplement their livelihoods. National economy.
The International Organization for Migration (IOM) emphasizes that all citizens have the right to choose the workplace of their choice, and the search for employment, mostly to developed countries, is a high-income opportunity. Vocational skills in the new workplace and it is a contribution to support local economic activities and social development.
