The growth trend of the irrigation system has supported the increase in agricultural productivity and supported the Cambodian government's export policy of 1 million tons of rice.
An Sithav, an economic researcher, explains the current state of agricultural development in Cambodia:
He said that in the first six months, after the price of rice began to rise since June, it has risen by about 30 percent, the highest price in more than 10 years. Despite the increase in rice, mill owners who are members of the Rice Federation continue to rush to buy districts for storage to compete with Vietnamese traders for milling exports.
According to Duke Song Saran, rice has started to grow since mid-2023 due to climate change, which has forced some Asian countries to stockpile food to keep their country stable as India shuts down. Temporary rice export.
He said that while India is temporarily shutting down white rice exports, the white rice market is still good, but farmers must be careful because if India reopens white rice exports, it will have an impact because no country can Compete in exporting white rice with India. When white rice cannot be exported, the price of white rice will fall, so farmers need to monitor the situation in deciding which type of rice to grow.
However, the Rice Federation will examine the possibility of advising farmers to grow white rice to serve the white rice market.
During the first half of 2023, India, the world's largest exporter of rice, shut down the export of white and broken rice in order to maintain food security in its country. Pushing the price of white rice in some markets in the region seems to have increased significantly.
