Cambodia-Indonesia Business and Investment Forum plays an important role in promoting economic, trade and new investment opportunities between the two countries
(Phnom Penh): Ms. Soy Bopha, Undersecretary of State of the Ministry of Commerce, said that the Cambodia-Indonesia Business and Investment Forum is an important part in promoting economic, trade and new investment opportunities between the two countries in line with program priorities. Fifth, the Royal Government of Cambodia in promoting production, marketing and maintaining the balance of prices of important agricultural products at a reasonable level.
Ms. Soy Bopha made the remarks at the Cambodia-Indonesia Business and Investment Forum on December 16, 2023.
Ms. Soy Bopha stated that under the leadership of Samdech Prime Minister Hun Manet, the Prime Minister of Cambodia launched the first phase of the Pentagon Strategy and the priority policy program of the Royal Government of Cambodia in August 2023 to build the foundation to achieve the vision. Cambodia 2050 and the Royal Government of Cambodia's six priority policy programs include:
He added that the Cambodia-Indonesia Business and Investment Forum is an important part to help promote and promote the economic, trade and investment between Cambodia and the Republic of Indonesia, especially to find new partners and new investment opportunities. "Both countries are in line with the priority areas of the Royal Government of Cambodia's fifth program to boost production, find markets and keep prices of key agricultural products at a reasonable level."
The main products that Cambodia imports from Indonesia include tobacco, coal, grain, tractors, pharmaceuticals, machinery, fins, refined oil.
In particular, the products that Cambodia exports to the Indonesian market include garments, garments, shoes, embroidered fabrics, suitcases, paper, glass, electronics, plastic products and by-products for other production.
