President of the Cambodian Mathematician Community Requests Teachers to Participate in Strengthening Students' Capacity and Research on Mathematical Education in Cambodia
(Phnom Penh): Dr. Chan Rath, President of the Cambodian Mathematical Society, on December 16, 2023, requested teachers to participate in strengthening the capacity of students as well as strengthening the quality and effectiveness of teaching and research. On mathematics education in Cambodia.
The ceremony was held at the National Institute of Education on the afternoon of December 16, 2023 under the chairmanship of Dr. Oum Romney, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports, on behalf of Dr. Hang Chuon Naron, Deputy Prime Minister, Minister of Education, Youth and Sports.
Dr. Chanrath stated, "I would like to ask the principals, teachers, teachers who have students full of talent and ability in mathematics, please continue to provide additional training to participate in strengthening the capacity of students and strengthen the quality and effectiveness of "Learning, teaching and research on mathematics education in Cambodia."
In addition, Dr. Chanrath said that having good ability in mathematics alone is not enough to become a full citizen, global citizens must be healthy, have good manners, morals and virtues.
Therefore, Dr. Chan Rath would like to ask parents who have sons, daughters, beloved and capable like a rising star, please continue to educate more to be healthy, moral, ethical and virtuous.
At the same time, Dr. also asked the Head of the Royal Government to continue to support, encourage and encourage young students with talent and ability in mathematics and provide opportunities for young people who have graduated from high school. Get a scholarship to continue your higher education both in the country and abroad.
Dr. Chanrath emphasized that this is to build potential human resources for the country and future young leaders in response to the vision of the Royal Government of Cambodia by 2030, Cambodians have a high middle income. And by 2050, Cambodians will have higher incomes.
Please be informed that the Cambodian Mathematician Community, in collaboration with the Mathematical Research Institute of the University of Brooks, Canada, has organized an online math curriculum test from Kindergarten to Grade 12. There are six exams per academic year.
There were a total of 55,788 participants. In 2023, 1985 Cambodian students participated in the exam, as a result of the first two exams, 11 kindergarten and first grade students and 9 second grade students were ranked first in the world. Out of 26 countries that participated in the exam.
It is the pride of Cambodia to have a good education system that can educate boys and girls who have participated in international online math competitions and ranked first among more than 3,000 students from the same level from 26 countries. .
