Spokesman of the General Commission: 649 more vehicles were inspected and fined on December 16, 2023
According to the spokesperson, for December 16, 2023, the traffic police nationwide inspected and fined a total of 7,500 vehicles, including 5,482 motorcycles and 1,018 vehicles.
Notable offenses for motorcycles include: drunken driving under the influence of drugs, processing without a license plate, and offenses against fire-signs. In particular, the car includes: drunk, recycled, no driver's license, transporting bulky, violating fire-signs and violating speed.
It should be noted that for December 16, 2023, there were 13 traffic accidents throughout Cambodia, in which 8 people were killed and 13 people were injured (10 people were seriously injured). In 16 days, there were 145 traffic accidents, resulting in 67 deaths, 239 injuries (128 serious injuries).
