PM Hun Sen Instructs the Ministry of Foreign Affairs to Study the possibility of establishing more Consulate General in Japan to facilitate services to Cambodians and reduce costs (Video inside) (Japan): Samdech Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia December 2023 instructs the Ministry of Foreign Affairs to study the possibility of establishing a Consulate General in Japan in the near future to facilitate the provision of services to citizens and interns, as well as reduce other costs.
His Excellency Hun Manet's introduction was made on the occasion that Samdech Samdech and Lok Chumteav Dr. met with Cambodian people in Japan on the morning of December 16, 2023 during Samdech's participation in the Japan Summit. - ASEAN.
He stressed the need to study the possibility of establishing a Consulate General, because in the future there may be more Cambodians to work as well as study in Japan, while the geographical factors in Japan are long. Other services at the Cambodian Embassy in Japan, located in Tokyo, are time consuming and expensive.
At the same time, visiting and solving problems for the trainees and skilled workers of the sub-work is not timely and costs a lot of money to travel.
Samdech said, "Now I would like to examine the possibility of studying. "The Ministry of Foreign Affairs is looking at whether we can in the future create another consulate general to help our brothers below."
While urging the Ministry of Foreign Affairs to establish a Consulate General in Japan in the past, Samdech also recommended the establishment of another Consulate General in Songkhla Province in southern Thailand, as there are already many Cambodians working there. They have to travel long distances to receive services and spend a lot of money.
In addition, Samdech Thipadei also instructed the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training to review the preparation of another sub-division to facilitate the visit and visit the people here, especially when there is an accident. .
