A census by the US Department of Development, Urban Planning and Housing shows that by 2023, about 653,000 people across the United States will be homeless. That figure is 70,650 more than the 2022 figure, or 12 percent, and the highest since the survey began in 2007.
African-Americans, who make up 13 percent of the American population, make up 37 percent of all homeless people in the United States. The highest increase in homelessness was among Native Americans, who increased by 28 percent, or 39,106, between 2022 and 2023.
