The Royal Government is working to develop roads to reduce the urban-rural gap
(Siem Reap): Dr. Nuon Danhel, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Rural Development, said that the Royal Government of Cambodia is working to develop roads to reduce the gap between urban and rural areas, as well as to facilitate people's travel to various destinations. .
While leading the working group of the Inter-Ministerial Commission to inspect and evaluate the work of restoring a gravel road in Ta Siem commune, Svay Leu district, Siem Reap province on December 15, 2023, Dr. Nuon Danhel said that a road This line has really contributed a lot to help improve the living standards of the people in the area, including transporting agricultural products to market as well as transporting goods to the town.
He added that not only this road will also contribute to the promotion of tourism by transporting tourists to visit some ancient temples in Siem Reap, as well as make it easier for students to travel to school.
The Secretary of State added that the road will also facilitate the development of other achievements in Ta Siem commune and make it easier to bring sick people to hospitals in the city or Svay Leu district town, in general, has greatly reduced the cost of citizens.
This gravel road is more than 6 km long, accompanied by the construction of a 30-meter-long concrete bridge, a box drain, a number of round drains, which are implemented by the Department of Engineering, Ministry of National Defense, using Chapter 21 budget.
