DPM Sar Sokha Closes a Workshop on Dissemination of Civil Status and Identification Law
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Aphisandi Dr. Sar Sokha, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of the Ministry of Interior, on the afternoon of December 15, 2023, closed the seminar on dissemination of the Law on Civil Status and Identification.
Lt. Gen. Dr. Top Net, Director General of the General Department of Identification, said that the workshop was held throughout the day, divided into discussion groups to explore practical challenges and find inputs.
The Law on Civil Statistics, Civil Statistics and Identification was approved by the National Assembly on June 12, 2023 at the 9th National Assembly Session of the 6th Legislature, which was fully reviewed by the Senate on 21 June. 2023 at the 10th plenary session of the 4th legislature. This law has 12 chapters and 182 articles.
The purpose of this law is to determine the rules and procedures related to civil registration, residence registration, registration of civil status statistics, registration of personal identities, and preparation and management of the population in order to:
* Ensure consistent, permanent and permanent universal duty registration.
Ensure consistent and permanent universal identification of individuals.
* Ensure that residency registration is a universal obligation, consistently and permanently.
* Ensure that everyone has a legal identity through civil registration and identification by providing each individual with an individual identification number.
