Samdech Hun Manet Announces Continuation of Cooperation with Sofia University of Japan on Temple Preservation
(Tokyo, Japan): Cambodian Prime Minister Hun Manet has said that the temple is more than the soul of Cambodia, which is priceless. In this regard, the President asserted that the new Royal Government continues to cooperate with the Japanese Sofia University on the conservation, maintenance and restoration of temples.
The Prime Minister made this remark during a courtesy call and discussion with Prof. Dr. Ishizawa Yoshiaki, President of the Center for Asian Studies, Research and Human Resources at Sofia University, located in Tokyo, Japan on the afternoon of December 15. This year 2023.
In addition, the professor also asked the President to support the University of Sofia to continue cooperation in the repair and conservation work in the Angkor resort area.
Samdech Hun Manet expressed his pleasure to meet with Professor Ishizawa Yoshiaki again after the meeting in November recently. He thanked the professors and the University of Sofia for their contribution to the preservation of the temples and the training of human resources in Cambodia. .
The Prime Minister also informed the Professor that Angkor Wat and its temples represent the priceless soul of the Khmer nation, and the Royal Government of all mandates has always paid close attention to the preservation of Angkor and its livelihood. People living in the surrounding area adhere to the concept of "conservation for development, development for conservation".
He also stated that the Royal Government of the 7th mandate will continue to cooperate with Sofia University in repairing temples and training human resources in Cambodia by providing coordination to make this work. The process went smoothly.
