(Phnom Penh): Following the 1993 Constituent Assembly elections organized by the United Nations Transitional Authority in Cambodia (UNTAC), Cambodia is committed to organizing and administering its own elections to ensure Independence, sovereignty, peace, neutrality in accordance with the principles of multi-party liberal democracy as stated in the Constitution of the Kingdom of Cambodia.
In this spirit, the National Election Committee, an independent body, was established on January 30, 1998 to organize and administer elections in Cambodia.
The new NEC would like to express its deep gratitude and appreciation for the invaluable achievements of the previous NEC, and please record these legacies as an experiment for the NEC. All mandates, as well as election officials at all levels, serve as a basis for better organization, management, and subsequent elections in order to continue to promote liberal democracy, pluralism, the rule of law, peace, and national development.
With the commitment of the composition of the National Election Committee of this new mandate, together with the leadership of the General Secretariat of the NEC and professional officers at all levels, who are experienced technical staff, we strongly believe that we will organize Both by-elections were successful as promised by NEC Chairman HE Prach Chan on the occasion of his inauguration.
