(Phnom Penh): On December 13th and 14th, 2023, Try Pheap Group of Try Pheap, Advisor to Samdech Techo Hun Sen, President of the Cambodian People's Party, held a meeting to review the work results of the old year 2023 and Raise the work direction for the new year 2024.
The meeting, which was held at the company's headquarters in Phnom Penh, was chaired directly by Duke Try Pheap and was attended by the company's locomotives, as well as the leaders of the subsidiaries and divisional directors.
Try Pheap Group is a company that does business in many fields such as construction, transportation, port, hotel, leisure, tourism, fuel and rubber plantations. During the two-day meeting, the leaders of each division presented a report on the work they have done, the challenges and suggestions for the work direction for implementation in 2024.
After presenting the report on the challenges and suggestions, on the last day of the meeting, Duke Try Pheap raised his opinion to evaluate the work and make various recommendations to strengthen the work spirit of the staff to improve the work efficiency even more.
On that occasion, the Duke also reminded all employees of the company to continue to adhere to the spirit of unity, love for the company and continue to strive to fulfill their duties better, help the company to run well and continue to maintain a source of income to support daily life. The Duke also thanked all the leaders and employees who worked tirelessly to serve the company.
According to the report, Try Pheap Group has a total of about 4,000 employees and pays a monthly salary of more than 1 million US dollars. The report also shows that as of November 2023, the company has contributed up to 20 million US dollars in taxes to the state.
Along with doing business, Try Pheap Group also adheres to the principle of helping the community with the Royal Government by helping to build achievements to serve the public interest, including buildings, health centers, schools and roads. In addition, when Cambodia encounters disasters such as floods, Try Pheap Group has donated food, rice, fish and noodles to the Royal Government to help people affected.
Please note that after concluding the meeting to review the work of the old year and the direction of the new year, Duke Try Pheap also organized a party for the management and staff, and there was a raffle, including motorcycles, mobile phones and TVs. Happiness.
