Rice farmers in Anlong Metrey village, Chulkiri district, accuse authorities of stealing water from their fields
(Kampong Chhnang): There is a dispute between the people and the authorities in Chulkiri district, Kampong Chhnang province, related to the sale of a watermelon in Anlong Metrey village, Peam Chkork commune, Chulkiri district, Kampong Chhnang province, to a fishing trader, which makes them the owner of the rice field. In the above location, he was upset and asked the provincial leaders to help solve this problem.
Residents said that in the location above the river is a rice field with 55 families. Many years ago, they sold the river to fishermen to raise money for pumping water to irrigate fields, repair dams, and raise money for various achievements in the village.
According to the report, on the day of the meeting to resolve the dispute, Peam Chkork commune chief Keo Met asked the people to reconsider a new agreement to end the dispute. Phrase to discuss with another representative of the dam chief.
The commune chief also requested that professional officers report to the director of the Fisheries Administration when the authorities coordinate the completion of work, and the commune chief will report to the director and the Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries later. Start harvesting cassava gradually with a happy face, while the price in Vietnam is better than last year
(Ratanakkiri): Farmers in Ratanakkiri province are busy harvesting their cassava to sell to traders, while prices at the end of 2023 in the Vietnamese market are better than last year.
In fact, on December 15, 2023, in Pak Po village, Pak Nhay commune, O'Yadao district, a group of about 30 farmers, who own their own plantations, were busy harvesting cassava, working hand in hand for free. One field after another rotates. They are busy digging and drying the bay to sell to traders.
Mr. Chheavna, a Jarai, representing the people who own the plantation, described that every year, they work together in the village for free, helping each other from planting to harvest by shaking hands as a tradition from the ancestors. .
He said that the owners of the cassava fields, who were digging and working together, brought rice from home to eat, and this year's cassava yielded more than last year, with about 10 tons per hectare. Happy.
The price of dried cassava is 890 riel per kilogram, market in Vietnam (O'Yadaw-Le Thanh international gate). Mr. Sem Saroeun, Director of the Office of Agriculture and Agricultural Productivity of the Ratanakkiri Provincial Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, told Fresh News on the morning of December 15, 2023 that a total of 18,370 hectares of cassava cultivation throughout the province has arrived. Farmers now start harvesting about 15 percent.
He said that in O'Yadao district, there is a large-scale cassava flour factory, which buys fresh cassava 410 riel per kilogram (15 percent cut on the roots of other wastes), while the purchase price of dried cassava 700 riel per kilogram. Winter storms swept across Russia, causing heavy snowfall
MOSCOW (Reuters) - Winter storms swept across Russia on Friday and left Moscow covered in unprecedented snow for years, disrupting traffic on major roads. While the car was driving on snow more than 20 cm thick. This is according to the release by Reuters on Friday, December 15, 2023.
Meteorologists say the cyclone has brought relentless snowstorms to Moscow, arguably one of the worst snowstorms in 60 years. More than one-fifth of the average snowfall for December was recorded in just 24 hours at all stations across Moscow.
Russian television reports that some schools in the Russian subcontinent have been closed due to snowfall. Traffic jams for 10 kilometers throughout the night on the M4, one of Russia's main roads to the south, left drivers stranded in cold weather.
(Phnom Penh): The "Samdech Bun Rany Hun Sen Water Pipe" with a diameter of 2 meters and a length of 540 meters, which is the largest project in the history of Cambodia, has completed drilling under the Tonle Sap from the east bank to the west. The flooding of Prek Pnov Bridge on December 15, 2023 will ensure a better water supply in Phnom Penh.
Mr. Long Naro, the Royal Government Delegate in charge of the Director General of the Phnom Penh Water Supply Authority, said that after the completion of the drilling of the pipeline under the Tonle Sap River, the Water Supply Authority will need more than a month to complete the work and connect. The existing "Samdech Bun Rany Hun Sen" water pipeline is scheduled to be officially launched in the first quarter of 2024.
He said that after the water pipe "Samdech Bun Rany Hun Sen" officially launched will ensure adequate water supply in Phnom Penh, including the suburbs.
According to the Director General of Water Supply, by the end of the first quarter of 2024, the production capacity of Phnom Penh Water Supply Authority will increase to 1 million cubic meters per day, while the current water consumption is about 850,000 meters. Cubes per day. Currently, the PPWSA is speeding up the installation of main pipes in some lanes to expand the supply.
Please be informed that the construction of 2 meters of clean water pipe under the Tonle Sap from the east bank to the west bank of the 540-meter-long Prek Pnov bridge is the first ever infrastructure in Cambodia that has started to be implemented in September 1, 2023 and completed on December 15, 2023.
Sub-project for construction of sewer system and another wastewater treatment plant was officially inaugurated in Kampot province
(Kampot): Mr. Peng Po Na, Minister of Public Works and Transport, presided over this morning, December 15, 2023, the inauguration ceremony of the Kampot Municipality Drainage System and Sewerage Project. Develop 2 corridors and hand over to the provincial administration to manage and continue to serve the public interest.
The ceremony was attended by Mr. New Saem, Chairman of Kampot Provincial Board, Representative of the Asian Development Bank (ADB) in Cambodia, a delegation accompanied by government officials, local authorities, citizens and many students.
The Minister also thanked the Kampot Provincial Authority, the Asian Development Bank and all stakeholders for their active cooperation in achieving this achievement and urged all stakeholders to take care of it. Protect and ensure that this project is stable, durable and can be used for a long time in the future.
Please be informed that this project is located in Kampot City, Kampot Province, covering a total area of 395.72 hectares, located in 4 Sangkats, including: Sangkat Kampong Bay, Sangkat Kraing Ampil, Sangkat Kampong Kandal and Sangkat Kampong Samrong. The wastewater treatment plant covers an area of 9.84 hectares.
The project started construction on October 25, 2019 and was completed on September 30, 2023, with a total budget of about 20 million US dollars, a loan from the Asian Development Bank. In general, the completed infrastructure is divided into two main parts: (1) wastewater treatment system and (2) urban drainage system with pumping capacity of 180 cubic meters / hour and water filtration capacity. Natural pollution is 3360 cubic meters / day.
Deputy General Commissioner of the National Police urges professional officers to carry out their work more effectively to eliminate the production, trafficking, distribution and use of all types of drugs
(Phnom Penh): Lt. Gen. Prum Santhor, Deputy Commissioner General of the National Police, this morning, December 15, 2023, urged the professional officers of the Department of Anti-Drug Crimes to work more effectively to eliminate production, trafficking and distribution. And all forms of drug use.
The introduction of Lt. Gen. Prum Santhor was made on the occasion of the closing ceremony of the training course on the investigation of drug offenses, money laundering, procedures and laws on drug control. At the General Commission of the National Police.
The study lasted for 5 days from 11 to 15 December 2023, with the participants paying attention, listening to the trainers and gaining good and medium skills.
Lt. Gen. Prum Santhor praised the course management team for organizing this training course to enhance the capacity of our law enforcement officers to have more knowledge and skills in drug crime prevention.
Samdech Hun Sen and Lok Chumteav Bandit Arrive in Japan
(Tokyo, Japan): The Prime Minister of Cambodia, His Excellency Hun Manet, and His Excellency Dr. Pech Chanmony Hun Manet led a delegation to Japan on the afternoon of December 15, 2023.
It should be noted that at the invitation of Mr. Kishida Fumio, Prime Minister of Japan, His Excellency Hun Manet, Prime Minister of Cambodia, led a high-level delegation to attend the ASEAN-Japan Memorial Summit to celebrate the 50th anniversary of friendship and cooperation. ASEAN-Japan Cooperation to be Held in Tokyo from December 16-18, 2023
He will also attend the AZEC Community Leaders Meeting to discuss policies on energy transitions and promote cooperation towards reducing carbon emissions in Asia.
During his stay in Tokyo, the President will hold a working breakfast with the Prime Minister of the Lao People's Democratic Republic, Mr. Sansai Siphandon, and the Prime Minister of the Socialist Republic of Vietnam, Mr. Pham Minh Chinh, as well as a bilateral meeting with the Prime Minister, Setha Thavisin. Of the Kingdom of Thailand.
In connection with this hosting, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, President of the Cambodian People's Party (CPP), has assigned the task of Samdech Moha Bovatei Hun Manet, Vice President of the Cambodian People's Party and Prime Minister, to chair the 12th ICAPP General Assembly. This is according to the announcement of the Cambodian People's Party, which was received by Fresh News.
The delegation paid a courtesy call on Samdech Akka Moha Sena Padei Techo Hun Sen, President of the Cambodian People's Party, President of the National Assembly, President of the National Assembly Yuon Sodary, President of the National Assembly and Vice President of ICAPP
Mr. Chung Iyong highlighted the important role of the Cambodian People's Party under the long-term vision of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, who has actively contributed to the initiative to support and nurture cooperation and strengthen democracy in Asia. Since the founding of the ICAPP in 2000, the organization has become an increasingly influential and important political forum in the global context of intense geopolitical competition.
The 12th ICAPP General Assembly and related meetings, including the 42nd ICAPP Standing Committee Meeting, the 3rd Asian Cultural Council Meeting, and the 7th ICAPP Press Forum in Cambodia in November 2024 will be major historical events. And another success of the reunion of families, political parties in Asia representing 52 countries and partner institutions from different regions.
The Cambodian People's Party will push ICAPP to increase the role of youth and promote digital revolution in social and economic connectivity, and to continue to actively participate in the mission for a peaceful and prosperous Asia and to see a lasting peace on the Korean Peninsula.
