(Phnom Penh): The Tonle Sap Lake is considered to be the heart of Cambodia, which has provided a rich crop to the people of this country. The history, culture and way of life of the Cambodian people are closely linked to this vast freshwater sea, as many have expressed curiosity about the mysteries of the Tonle Sap Lake and when they were born. ?
According to research by the Cambodia-Japan Joint Working Group, the Tonle Sap Lake appeared between 6,000 or 5,000 years ago. Compared to the age of the planet, our Tonle Sap Lake is very young.
Researchers have defined the stages of the Tonle Sap Lake formation into eight stages, including prenatal, postnatal and postnatal, including:
* About 15,000 years ago, the continental shelf rose above sea level, making the seabed much lower than the Mekong River, and the Mekong River flowed from the upper reaches into the South China Sea. At the same time, the sea level is 100 meters lower than the current sea level.
* About 3,000 years ago, sea level began to gradually decrease to the current level, while the Mekong Delta gradually formed during the period of sea level decline. That. Due to the decrease in sea level, the Tonle Sap Lake expands in the rainy season and shrinks in the dry season every year.
Dr. Hang Chuon Naron Closes the 31st Sub-National Congress of Priests
