On the occasion of the closing ceremony of the 31st National General Assembly of Monks, on this occasion, the two groups of monks of the Mahanikaya of the Kingdom of Cambodia and the Judiciary of the Kingdom of Cambodia unanimously decided at the following joint proclamation:
On this occasion, Dr. Hang Chuon Naron highly appreciated Mr. Chay Borin's report on the remarkable progress in the field of religion, especially Buddhism, under the careful management of the Ministry of Cult and Religion. Religious Harmony in Cambodia. In the context of education through Buddhism, it has played an important role in material and spiritual development within the framework of law, justice, equity, ethics and virtue.
He said that under the attention of the head of the Royal Government of Cambodia set out in the win-win policy of Samdech Techo Hun Sen until now, continuing under the leadership of Samdech Thep Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia decided to convert to Buddhism. In public and private school education programs as well.
(Phnom Penh): Four police officers from the police unit shot and killed themselves, causing a surprise at more than 12 midnight on December 15, 2023 in Khve village, Sangkat Trapeang Krasang, Khan Por Sen Chey, Phnom Penh.
The victim, Noy Phara, 36, a police officer, a sheriff, a lieutenant colonel, and his wife, Ngin Solita, 35, was a factory worker and had two children. The victim was born in Romlong village, Sopor Tep commune, Chbar Morn city, Kampong Speu province and lived at home.
At more than 10 pm on December 14, 2023, his wife called because it was late at night and did not see him return home, but did not enter at that time. The wife kept waiting to see the road, only to find him drunk when she arrived home, then had a verbal dispute with his wife. Sleep outside the house.
After the incident, Trapeang Krasang police reported to the Phnom Penh Municipal Police Technical and Scientific Office for forensic examination and found that the man had indeed shot himself, and that his family had brought the body to the funeral. Hometown. Ministry of Public Function issues instructions to candidates during the 2023 Commune Agriculture Officer Competition
According to the Ministry of Public Works, candidates for the 2023 Commune Agriculture Officer Competition must respect and follow the following guidelines:
* Must come to the examination center with your ID card or Chhaya (monk) or ID card (or official certificate) as well as the blue pen and line to use during the exam
* In case of late "less than 15 minutes" after the start of the course, permission must be obtained from the director of the examination center in order to be able to enter the exam and hand in the exam worksheets on time. Arriving later than "15 minutes" after the start of the course is not allowed.
* Absence of any subject exam will not be allowed for the next subject exam.
* Do not enter the examination room before calling the name, sit at the table number shown, write the name and table number on the head of the exam worksheet as instructed by the supervisor and return the worksheet to the supervisor, even if the exam paper does not write the answer or any solution Anyway. Failure to hand over the exam worksheet to the supervisor is considered absent.
* Do not write in the cross of all pages of the exam worksheet and do not make a mark to indicate the inclusion of the exam worksheet.
* Do not commit any form of plagiarism, attempt to plagiarize or share information with others.
Candidates who do not follow the above instructions or threaten or damage the honor and integrity of the competent officials, both inside and outside the examination room, will be immediately suspended from the examination during the current examination period and prohibited. Not to participate in the competition for the selection of civil servants and to be responsible according to the rules and regulations in force.
Interior Ministry Spokesman: 64 people arrested for criminal and drug offenses on December 14
(Phnom Penh): At least 64 suspects were arrested in criminal and drug offenses across Cambodia on December 14, 2023 yesterday. This was confirmed by General Khieu Sopheak, spokesman for the Ministry of Interior, to Fresh News on December 15, 2023.
General Khieu Sopheak added that of the 64 suspects, 55 were arrested in 25 drug cases and nine were arrested in nine criminal cases.
Ministry of Economy organizes the second phase of Public-Private Partnership (PPP) project management training in Cambodia under the Human Resource and Institutional Capacity Development Program
The Capacity Development Program was developed by the P4I team in detail, covering all aspects of the PPP project cycle, and was subjected to a series of follow-up meetings for review, revision, and consultation for nearly a year.
The capacity development program has three phases, as planned as planned in the first phase of the training program, the Ministry of Economy and Finance, in collaboration with P4I, has continued to implement P4I's human resource and institutional capacity development program for the second phase. .
The second phase of the training program is divided into two levels, with a half-day management level on December 12, 2023 at the Rosewood Hotel Phnom Penh and a three-day project manager level from December 13th to 15th, 2023 at Sofitel Phnom Penh Phokitra Hotel, and the completion of the second phase of the training will require an exam on December 15, 2023.
Heng Sour Asks OTIT to Encourage Large Japanese Companies to Increase Recruitment of Skilled Workers from Cambodia and Continue to Pay More Attention to Cambodians in Japan
At the same meeting, the Minister of Labor also requested OTIT to coordinate with stakeholders to shorten the waiting time from the Japanese side, while currently the average Cambodian worker has to wait at least 4 to 6. That month.
More importantly, during the cordial meeting, the Minister requested the Japanese side to examine the possibility of facilitating Cambodian trainees already working in Japan to change jobs without having to return to Cambodia after serving. Work through any appropriate deadline.
Meanwhile, OTIT also pointed out to the Minister that Japan is revising its foreign workers' reception law, which will be more transparent and effective to protect foreign workers more and more effectively. According to OTIT, the Japanese government also plans to take strict legal action against employers who violate the law.
Please note that OTIT is an organization of the Royal Government of Japan under the Ministry of Justice and the Ministry of Health, Labor and Welfare of Japan. The organization, which was established in 2017, is a licensee of Japanese associations and investment companies with the right to train and recruit international workers.
Analysts urge some unions to stop holding microphones, shouting in the streets because it is not the solution
(Phnom Penh): Analysts at the Royal Academy of Cambodia have found that holding a microphone on the street, shouting from a distance and reporting outside attacks from their country is not a good solution, but a closer relationship between Unions and the Royal Government, which is to find a good solution to protect the common interests of the nation.
The remarks came after it was observed that the Royal Government of Cambodia, with the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training as its chief of staff in the seventh mandate, met frequently in order to discuss work and put issues on the table to find common solutions. Avoid activities that cause social insecurity. However, a handful of unions still hold this position.
Dr. Yong Pov, Secretary General of the General Secretariat of the Royal Academy of Cambodia, said that a small number of unions should stop holding microphones and shouting in the streets because it is not a good solution. Face-to-face dialogue mechanisms put issues on the table to protect the national interest as a whole, which is the real need of the local workers.
He explained that the Royal Government of Cambodia and all local unions have been fulfilling their role and the sole purpose is to protect the rights of workers and maintain job stability in Cambodia. Therefore, intimacy and the ability to negotiate solutions, as well as protect common interests, are very important today.
"I think it is very good for the union and the political and social environment, and especially for the benefit of the local workers, it is easy to work without explosions," he said. Alas, various problems are obvious on the union's point of view! . "Overall, I think it would be good if the two sides could sit down and talk peacefully."
Dr. added: "Problems occur between people, no matter how big the problem, no matter how tense, as long as we know how to sit face to face, solve it a little bit to create a good atmosphere. "Of course, there are still disagreements and disagreements in some places, but it will only decrease if we sit face to face and talk to each other."
He added that the two sides should have such a mechanism from the beginning, but even so, it is too late, now both sides have to meet occasionally to put issues on the table. . Shouting at a microphone and issuing a report of a remote attack is not a good solution.
Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen Continues the Role of the President of the Cambodian Red Cross for the 7th Mandate
(Phnom Penh): Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen continues to be the President of the Cambodian Red Cross for the seventh mandate. This is according to the press release on the results of the 7th General Assembly of the Cambodian Red Cross.
