(Kampot): On the morning of December 15, 2023, Mr. Peng Po, Minister of Public Works and Transport, continued to meet with leaders and civil servants of Kampot Provincial Department of Public Works and Transport with the participation of Mr. Nouv Saem, Chairman of the Provincial Board and many accompanying delegates.
During the meeting, the Minister made good recommendations, emphasizing the strengthening of labor discipline, maintaining solidarity and internal cooperation, especially the study of learning more about digital technology to work faster and faster. And the Pentagon Strategy - Phase 1 of the Royal Government of the 7th Legislature.
At the same time, he also mentioned the reform of the Ministry, which has two main priority plans and four other support mechanisms to inform the members of the ceremony who are officials to continue to implement in the unit. To be more efficient and effective.
At the same time, the Minister decorated the officials with the badges and provided 200 bags of safety badges, road helmets, reflective jackets, reflectors, lawn mowers and cold rubber to the department for use in repairs. Maintain roads within its jurisdiction. Ministry of Commerce: Exhibition of Cambodian products and export-import goods will promote trade and investment activities in Cambodia
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Kem Sithon, Acting Minister of the Ministry of Commerce, on December 15, 2023, stated that the event "16th Cambodian Products and Import-Export Fair 2023" will participate in promoting trade activities and Investment in Cambodia.
This statement was made on the occasion that Mr. Kem Sithon, Representative of Ms. Cham Nimmol, Minister of Commerce, presided over the opening ceremony of the 16th Cambodian Products and Export-Import Fair 2023 on the morning of December 15, 2023. Koh Pich Convention and Exhibition Center. The event runs for four days from December 15-18.
Mr. Kem Sithon said that the exhibition of Cambodian products and export-import goods is an annual international trade event organized by the Ministry of Commerce 15 times since its first organization in 2006 and There is also the support of some relevant ministries and institutions of the Royal Government of Cambodia.
He said that this event has contributed to disseminate the real situation of Cambodian society today and show the business environment, investment and growth in all sectors of Cambodia, especially contributed to the implementation of the policy of the Royal Government from one mandate to another mandate. Help promote national economic growth with environment and equity.
In addition, Mr. Kem Sithon emphasized that through this trade event, Cambodian and foreign businessmen have the opportunity to meet and discuss directly on trade and investment to promote business and mutual investment within the framework. Internal districts, regions and the world as well.
The Acting Minister of Commerce said that trade has now become the lifeblood of economic development, investment, tourism and cultural exchange between the region and the world.
He said the trade fair was not only a product show, but also a celebration of entrepreneurial spirit, business resilience and a testament to the development of the business sector and the creation of opportunities for investment partners. Growth and social prosperity.
Please be informed that this event is organized in order to promote trade and investment activities in Cambodia, especially to promote trade links between Cambodia and the international community, as well as to promote the export-import of goods and services to the target market. Part of boosting national economic growth.
This year's Cambodian Products and Import-Export Fair is more unique than previous years, with the support of 17 countries and more foreign delegates than last year, with the exhibition of key products. Many such as:
* GI products include Kampot pepper, Kampong Speu palm sugar, Kampot-Kep salt, grapefruit, Koh Trong, Takeo lobster, Kampot-Kep fish sauce and Mondulkiri wild honey. Cambodian pepper and spices, groceries, food and beverage products.
* Cosmetics and car accessories and accessories, clothes, shoes and travel accessories for export of jewelry and precious stones, electronics, souvenirs, general consumer goods from abroad, etc.
In this year's exhibition event, the Ministry of Commerce will also organize some important accompanying events, such as: business meetings on the promotion of Cambodian products to international markets, the Cambodia-Indonesia Business and Investment Forum, and concerts.
