In order to be in line with the first phase of the Pentagon strategy of the new government, the Ministry has been pursuing its vision of improving the quality and value of rural people's lives, both economically, socially and culturally, through programs. The four priorities are:
2. Improving the living conditions of rural communities so that rural people can live with dignity, good attitude, good health and good hygiene, and be comfortable.
3. Diversification of rural economic activities through the training of basic skills to create jobs and occupations in order to increase household economic income in rural areas.
4. Strengthen administrative and general affairs support services to strengthen national and sub-national institutions to be able to serve rural people with integrity and high responsibility.
At the same time, the Secretary of State informed the delegates about the six directions, including:
2. Encouraging construction and public investment in basic infrastructure systems (roads and water distribution and sanitation systems) in areas with high economic potential.
3. Long-term sustainable maintenance of built-in achievements
4. Training of human resources in basic skills to create income-generating businesses
5. Preparation of policies, laws and standards
6. Strengthening institutions by continuing to promote decentralization and deconcentration to local officials to strengthen their capacity and efficiency.
