The 4-week Heavy Engineering Equipment Training (HEE) course will begin on November 20, 2023, with seven officers from the Japan Self-Defense Forces (JGSDF) training Cambodian trainees. 18 people.
Japan sent its first peacekeeping operations engineering unit to Cambodia 31 years ago. Today, Cambodia has become one of the leading contributors to the United Nations peacekeeping mission. Japan has supported the capacity building of Cambodia's PKO since 2013.
With bilateral relations evolving into a comprehensive strategic partnership this year, Japan intends to increase cooperation with Cambodia in addressing regional and international issues, especially in the field of peacebuilding.
Cambodia and Japan have a long history of peacekeeping cooperation since Japan deployed the JGSDF Engineering Unit on the first peacekeeping operation in Cambodia 31 years ago. The two sides agreed to work together to build the capacity of the Cambodian Peacekeeping Operations Unit in 2012 and to begin training in civil engineering and road construction the following year.
