Police in Preah Vihear province continue to patrol the river to crack down on illegal fishing and confiscate some illegal fishing gear
(Preah Vihear): Police in Preah Vihear province's Kulen district police inspectorate confiscated a lot of illegal fishing gear in an operation to crack down on illegal fishing in a river in Kulen district on the evening of December 13, 2023. .
On the evening of December 14, 2023, Colonel Ou Seng, Kulen District Police Inspector, said that in accordance with the order of Major General Suos Sok Dara, Preah Vihear Provincial Police Commissioner, five specialized forces of Kulen District Police Inspectorate cooperated with Police from the Kulen Cheung Administrative Police Station patrolled along the Cold River to Peam Samrong point in the village of Chrouch Chrouk, cracking down on one case of illegal fishing (fishing).
In this operation, the police confiscated some equipment, including: 6 fish electric machines, 12 electric fishing rods equal to 6 pairs and 6 batteries. The confiscated materials were taken to the Kulen District Police Inspectorate for further injection.
Mr. O Seng stated that for the people involved in this case of illegal fishing, the authorities have educated and instructed with the signing of a thumbprint contract as evidence to stop illegal fishing activities from today onwards.
He also called on the people, especially those living along the river as fishermen, not to fish with illegal equipment, which leads to legal challenges, especially to destroy the species.
