Investors are keeping a close eye on policy hints and a reform agenda next year as Beijing struggles to boost its post-epidemic economic recovery amid a worsening housing crisis and escalation. Rising government debt.
According to Reuters, China's state-run media reported the annual Central Economic Work Conference, which runs from December 12 to 12, as China's top leaders set economic targets for 2024. That China will focus on boosting demand effectively next year and strive to expand domestic demand.
"In order to further promote economic recovery, we need to overcome some difficulties and challenges," the media reported. "Key issues include a lack of effective demand, overcapacity in some industries, weak public expectations and hidden risks."
China will adhere to a prudent fiscal and monetary policy next year. According to Reuters.
Indonesia eases tariff on electric car imports to attract investment (Video inside) (Jakarta): Indonesia will provide tax incentives to carmakers planning to build electric car factories for the whole of electric vehicle imports for up to a year. 2025 as Jakarta government seeks to attract more investment According to Reuters.
Under the new regulations signed on December 8 and released this week, companies that have invested in electric vehicles are planning to increase their investment in electric vehicles or are planning to invest in electric vehicles, Reuters reported. Eligible for this tax incentive.
The new law will eliminate import duties and taxes on the sale of luxury goods on non-imported vehicles and provide tax incentives collected by the provincial government.
Previous laws provided these incentives only for the importation of domestic butcher vehicles for parts and assembly for sale. Indonesia is Southeast Asia's largest car market.
However, the number of cars that the company can import depends on the size of the investment and the development of the factory and must be approved by the Ministry of Investment.
Rachmat Kaimuddin, deputy director of the Ministry of Investment and Maritime Affairs, was quoted by Reuters as saying at a seminar on Indonesia's economic outlook on Wednesday that the new decree would help automakers in the country. Building their market in the country through the import of electricity.
"We are trying to make progress because when we set up the electric car industry in Indonesia (the industry), batteries will also come and we already have (raw materials) and can make chains," he said. Can supply.
Thai Labor Minister to Propose Higher Minimum Wage Increased by Wage Committee (Video inside) (Bangkok) The daily minimum wage averaged 2.37 percent and seeks higher than the proposal after the Wage Committee decided to offer a lower wage than the government target.
Reuters reports that the minister's comments came after Thai Prime Minister Setha Thaksin Shinawatra said last week's wage increase agreed with government officials, the private sector and trade unions was too low.
The previous Thai government raised the minimum wage by 5.02 percent in October last year. The ruling Pheu Thai party has campaigned on a key populist policy: raising the minimum wage to 400 baht a day.
Businesses have highlighted rising costs and wages as a deterrent to competition at a time of slowing economic growth.
Southeast Asia's second-largest economy grew 1.5 percent slower than expected in the third quarter from a year earlier, the slowest pace this year due to declining exports and spending. Government.
The Federation of Thai Industries on Tuesday raised concerns that higher minimum wages will hurt businesses, which will bear the burden of spending, along with higher interest rates, amid global uncertainty. According to Reuters.
