The following is a video of support and welcome: The Fisheries Administration calls on fishermen not to fish with equipment that obstructs the movement of fish during the migration season from the Tonle Sap Lake
(Phnom Penh): The Fisheries Administration of the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries has issued a notification on the migratory fish season from the Tonle Sap Lake.
According to the announcement, biologically, some species of fish migrate from the Tonle Sap Lake along the Tonle Sap River to the Upper Mekong River in search of food, shelter and reproduction from the month of June to December. Where the water of the Tonle Sap Lake flows out at high speed.
In light of the situation mentioned above, the Fisheries Administration would like to ask the people not to fish with the equipment that obstructs the fishery and call on the fishermen and stakeholders to comply with this notice. Effective to ensure the sustainability of fishery resources.
