(Phnom Penh): Mr. Som Soreida, Member of the National Election Committee (NEC) of the new mandate, claimed that although the leadership of the new NEC is composed of two political parties with seats in The National Assembly, however, all the actions of the NEC are not decided by any individual, that is, to maintain neutrality and fairness in the election.
The assertion of the new NEC members was made during an interview with the media after the announcement of the new chairman, vice chairman and nine new members of the NEC this morning. December 14, 2023.
Mr. Som Soreida stated: "The current NEC, as well as the NEC in the past, is still the NEC that adheres to the implementation of the law on the organization and functioning of the National Committee. "I have stated that the independence, neutrality of the NEC is about respecting and enforcing the law."
Mr. Som Soreida said that the NEC still maintains the same position, respecting and implementing this law and orienting the NEC and ensuring the neutrality of the NEC in organizing. Voting shall be free, fair and just, and especially in accordance with the rules and procedures for the election. The NEC procedures are based on the law and involve all stakeholders.
Responding to questions regarding the composition of the NEC from two political parties with a majority in the National Assembly, he added: "For the NEC's general work experience, although "In any environment, the NEC implements its work smoothly and, in particular, harmonizes its work."
"Therefore, all the implementation of the NEC is a committee-type practice, so the committee regime is not decided by any individual, which is a good experience for the implementation of the NEC," he said. In the national institutions will continue to implement and will strengthen this practice to be better.
Mr. Som Soreida claimed that the NEC is committed to respecting and enforcing the law for the implementation of the law, which is accepted by the majority of the people, but nevertheless can not satisfy everyone. In particular, for the point of some shortcomings on the NEC in the past by analysts and politicians can confirm that Cambodia has implemented a liberal, multi-party democratic society that allows people to have the right to express themselves. Everyone.
For Mr. Prach Chan, Chairman of the National Election Committee (NEC), the new mandate is committed to continue to lead the NEC in fulfilling its duties and responsibilities to better manage and manage the election in accordance with the law. In accordance with the laws, regulations and procedures of the election to ensure that each election is free, fair and increase the trust of voters and stakeholders.
