(Phnom Penh): A group of economists and policy analysts of the Royal Academy of Cambodia said that the "Roadmap on Skills Development in Cambodia 2023-2035" of the Royal Government of Cambodia is a strategic plan to go along with the developed countries in In the region and the world on the development of the skills of citizens, because it is a factor in promoting the lifelong learning of citizens, motivating a citizen to have a clear skill.
Dr. Kin Phea, an analyst at the Royal Academy of Cambodia, sees this roadmap on skills development in Cambodia as a roadmap for the Royal Government of Cambodia to move towards a country with professional citizens. Life is clear for them. This roadmap is a strategy that goes hand in hand with some of the developed countries in the region as well.
Meanwhile, Dr. Ky Sereyvath, an economist at the Royal Academy of Cambodia, called the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training's roadmap on skills development in Cambodia 2023-2035 now an important strategy to transform the workforce. Countries from labor to force have specific skills through this rigorous technical training.
For Dr., this map of human resource development will provide high-skilled people with high incomes, as the labor market will attract more value-added technological investment, which will improve people's lives. For this policy to be successful, the government alone cannot implement it successfully, requiring the participation of the private sector and the people.
It should be noted that through this roadmap policy on skills development, the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training, which is the staff for the Royal Government, has set out five strategic pillars to achieve this ambition. First, improving the quality of vocational education, second, promoting reputation and promotion, third, vocational education that meets industry needs, fourth, governance and leadership, and finally, financing and sustainability. .
Through these pillars, the Ministry expects to be able to fulfill the potential of current and future growth to contribute to maintaining and promoting national economic growth as well as sustainable development.
