Mr. Oknha Song Saran emphasized that although Cambodia's rice exports have grown less than neighboring countries, Cambodia is trying to export at a reasonable level so as not to cause any loss to the rice industry to farmers and can make factories Machines can survive even if they suffer minor losses.
He said the slight increase in rice exports was due to the fact that Cambodia did not have enough rice for export recently, as mills that are members of the federation had to compete with Vietnamese traders to buy rice from Vietnamese traders. Rice has grown.
He said the shortage of rice for export this year would also affect next year's exports. Until now, the price of rice in the market and the price of rice is still high, however, mill owners must strive to collect rice from farmers, otherwise can not compete with Vietnam.
He added that the price of rice in 2024 will continue to rise, as Cambodia may be short of rice and rice for export in the first quarter of 2024 due to the early harvest from January to March is not large. Enough for export. However, he expects that from the second quarter of 2024, the momentum of exports will increase when the dry season rice harvest arrives.
