Cambodian Women's Association for Peace and Development Branch of the Ministry of Information Donates 300 Boxes of Vitamin Rice and 500 Cans of Fish to Calmette Hospital
(Phnom Penh): The branch of the Cambodian Women's Association for Peace and Development, Ministry of Information, led by Ms. Tuy Serey Ratanak Netpheaktra, Honorary President and her leadership, brought 300 cases of vitamin rice and 500 cans of fish to Calmette Hospital to help To meet the needs of patients staying in Calmette Hospital, Phnom Penh.
Prof. Dr. Kong Sanya, Director General of Calmette Hospital, stated that Calmette Hospital is one of the oldest in the field of health in Cambodia under the wise leadership of the head of the Royal Government who always cares about the well-being of the people. At all times, Calmette Hospital is one of the largest public hospitals in the country to provide general medical care and health care to the people.
Indeed, Calmette Hospital plays an important role in rescuing, treating, caring for, and improving public health. However, the provision of 300 cases of vitamin rice and canned fish on this occasion is very important to meet the needs of patients who are being treated and treated at Calmette Hospital.
Mrs. Tuy Serey Ratanak Net Pheaktra brought a message from Samdech Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, as well as Lok Chumteav Dr. Pech Chanmony Hun Manet to send his deepest condolences to her as a doctor, health officer and relatives. Get treatment and get medical check-ups at Calmette Hospital. May you be healthy and recover quickly from various ailments for the smile of one great Khmer family.
She said that the Royal Government of Cambodia, the 7th legislature of the National Assembly, has been active and has launched a pentagon strategy - the first phase for the growth of employment, equity, efficiency and sustainability, as well as attention to the well-being of the people. Essential, important and indispensable for daily life.
Mrs. Tuy Serey Ratanak Net Pheaktra told the general public to be extremely careful in taking care of their health. The important factor is to live a clean life, eat clean, clean the environment around you, health problems are a challenge that must be addressed together for the harmonization of Cambodian society today and into the future.
Ms. Tuy Sereyratanak continued that although the supply of this vitamin rice is small, it can not meet the needs of Calmette Hospital, but this offer can contribute to the shortage of the hospital for a while. On the other hand, the Cambodian Women's Association for Peace and Development, Ministry of Information will continue to cooperate with Calmette Hospital.
