The following is a sub-decree of the Royal Government of Cambodia: France will increase cooperation to organize courses for the National Peacekeeping Center of Cambodia to become a regional and ASEAN model training institute.
(Phnom Penh): Lt. Gen. COLCOMBET Régis, Director of the Department of Security and Defense Cooperation, Ministry of European Affairs and Foreign Affairs of the French Republic, said that France will increase its cooperation to organize courses for the National Peacekeeping Center to become an institute. Training regional and ASEAN models.
This statement was made by a senior official of the Ministry of European Affairs and Foreign Affairs of the French Republic during a hearing and discussion meeting with General Sem Sovanny, Director General of the National Peacekeeping Center on the afternoon of December 13, 2023 yesterday. .
General Sem Sovanny warmly welcomed the arrival of the delegation of the French Republic. Through good cooperation between the two countries, France has provided training both domestically and internationally on peacekeeping, officers, officers, military observers, etc. So far, 84 sessions have been completed and all trainees have been on missions under the United Nations umbrella.
The general added that under the joint efforts of the French Adviser at the National Peacekeeping Center, we are developing a strategy to increase the number of French language classes to encourage trainees to graduate to the mission area.
At the same time, General Sem Sovanny requested the French side to continue to support the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces, especially in the field of human resource training and increase the level of training in a tripartite manner. At the same time, the general also asked the French side to provide study materials to equip the new school building, which will be completed in the near future.
He gladly accepted the request of General Sem Sovanny. He also called on Cambodia to further enhance cooperation to further enhance relations between the two countries. Hun Sen Receives Former South Korean Foreign Minister
