South Korean Defense Chief Warns North Korea There Are Two Options: Peace and Destruction
SEOUL (Reuters) - South Korea's defense minister on Wednesday issued a stern warning to North Korea if its neighbor dares to act recklessly. This was released by Reuters on Wednesday, December 13, 2023.
Seoul's use of harsh rhetoric comes after North Korea announced last month its decision to withdraw from the 2018 military deal with South Korea, which was designed to ease tensions. Before North Korea decided to do so, South Korea announced the suspension of parts of the agreement after the launch of Pyongyang's spy satellite.
"North Korea has only two options: security and destruction," South Korean Defense Minister Shin Won-sik said in a statement. "If North Korea dares to act without long-term thinking, which will affect the peace, only the most devastating destruction will await them."
