It should be noted that Cambodia sent Blue Hat forces to join the peacekeeping mission under the United Nations umbrella among 63 countries donating troops in April 2012.
Deputy Prime Minister Aun Porn Moniroth commends Rural Development and Agriculture Bank for its efforts to strengthen and expand its activities to achieve many important achievements
(Phnom Penh): The Bank for Rural Development and Agriculture (ARDB) on December 13, 2023 celebrated the 25th Anniversary of the Bank at the Garden City Hotel in Phnom Penh under the chairmanship of Dr. Aun Porn Moniroth, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Economy. And Finance, with the participation of senior leaders of the Royal Government, national and international development partners, a total of 500 ARDB customers and staff.
The purpose of the event was to celebrate and promote the Bank's 25-year achievements in implementing the Royal Government's policies by providing support to stakeholders in the agricultural and agro-industrial production chain. Improving the livelihood of farmers in rural areas and socio-economic development.
Dr. Aun Porn Moniroth praised and commended the Board of Directors, management and staff for their efforts to strengthen and expand its banking activities, which have achieved significant achievements since 1998, including the following:
First, financing to expand the capacity of warehouses, dryers and rice mills under the Agricultural Support and Development Fund of approximately US $ 36 million with the aim of ensuring stable rice prices and food security;
Second: Expanded intervention funding as an investment capital of approximately US $ 30 million for the construction of warehousing and rice drying mills in Battambang, Kampong Thom, Kampong Speu and Prey Veng provinces and a working capital of approximately US $ 90 million. To collect rice from farmers and under the special financing program of the Royal Government in order to ensure the stability of rice prices and boost rice exports;
Fourth: Implemented a special intervention package within the framework of the strategy and program to restore and promote economic growth in living with Kovid-19 along the new normal path 2021-2023, amounting to approximately 178 million US dollars.
In the spirit of promoting the operational efficiency of the Rural Development and Agriculture Bank in participating in the implementation of the Royal Government's policies, the General Secretary requested the ARDB to continue to pay attention to a number of important tasks, including:
* Continue to issue detailed measures and action plans in accordance with its jurisdiction in close cooperation with relevant ministries and institutions.
Continue to participate in the process of preparing, monitoring and evaluating the implementation of policies and strategies of the Royal Government related to agriculture and rural development, participate in raising investment from the private sector,
* Continue to contribute to improving the financial environment and promoting the expansion of digital banking services in line with the digital business development policy through additional investment in digital infrastructure and new product development.
* To continue to improve the efficiency of the Bank's operations through additional training as well as the establishment of an incentive system for employees at all levels.
