Police in Preah Vihear Province Crack Down on Illegal Fishing and Seize Some Evidence
(Preah Vihear): Many illegal fishing gears were confiscated by the police force of Kulen district, Preah Vihear province, along Stung Sen river in Kulen district, Preah Vihear province.
Colonel O Seng, Kulen District Police Inspector, said on the evening of December 13, 2023 that, following the order of Major General Sous Sok Dara, Preah Vihear Provincial Police Commissioner, 5 specialized forces of Kulen District Police Inspectorate Patrol along Stung Sen River cracked down on one case of illegal fishing (shock).
In this operation, the police confiscated some equipment, including: 8 electric shock machines, 18 electric fishing rods equal to 8 pairs and 8 batteries. The confiscated materials were taken to the Kulen District Police Inspectorate for further injection.
Mr. O Seng stated that for the people involved in this case of illegal fishing, the authorities have educated and instructed with the signing of a thumbprint contract as evidence to stop illegal fishing activities from today onwards.
He appealed to the people, especially the people living along Stung Sen as fishermen, not to fish with illegal equipment, which leads to legal challenges, especially to destroy the species.
