(Phnom Penh): The Rural Development and Agriculture Bank (ARDB) on December 13, 2023 celebrated the 25th anniversary of the establishment of ARDB at the Garden City Hotel in Phnom Penh under the chairmanship of Dr. Aun Porn Moniroth, Deputy Prime Minister. Ministry of Economy and Finance.
On that occasion, both Dr. Aun Porn Moniroth and Dr. Kao Thach, the Royal Government Delegate in charge of ARDB, highlighted the Bank's 25-year significant financial achievements from 1998 to 2023.
Dr. Kao Thach also noted that the increase in ARDB Bank's portfolio to date through the Royal Government's special financing scheme includes:
First, the Fund for the Support and Development of the Agricultural Sector to implement the policy on promoting rice production and rice export in accordance with the concept of Samdech Techo Hun Sen to turn Cambodia into an exporter of "white gold (rice)".
Third, a special intervention financing project to provide loans to support SMEs in the agricultural sector, including the cultivation of fruits and vegetables, cashews, lentils, Pailin mango, animal husbandry, aquaculture and processing of agricultural products, etc. to support SMEs' business expansion and Improve production chains that contribute to job creation and expand local production bases during and after the Kovid-19 crisis.
He said that with the regular support of the Royal Government through the Ministry of Economy and Finance, which is the guardian, especially Dr. Aun Porn Moniroth, Deputy Prime Minister, ARDB Bank has strengthened and expanded the scope of banking services, including:
Dr. Kao Thach emphasized that in order to expand digital banking operations safely, efficiently and effectively, ARDB Bank has become a member of the Bakong System and a member of CamDX, the Royal Government Data Exchange, to verify the identity of customers and other data. Customers will be able to open an online account with ARDB.
Overall, this 25-year achievement comes from the close support of the Royal Government, as well as the professionalism and high responsibility of the Board of Directors, management and staff at all levels of the Bank, as well as There is good cooperation from relevant ministries and institutions and competent authorities as well.
Speaking on the occasion, Dr. Aun Porn Moniroth, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Economy and Finance, said that for the past 25 years, the Bank for Rural Development and Agriculture has been building many achievements, starting from First served as a wholesale bank and was transformed into a commercial bank in 2019 to serve government policies more effectively.
At the same time, Dr. Aun Porn Moniroth highlighted the important achievements of the Rural Development Bank and Agriculture in participating in the implementation of the following special policies and programs of the Royal Government:
1: Established the "Agricultural Support and Development Fund" to expand the capacity of warehouses, dryers and mills and rice processing in order to ensure the stability of rice prices and food security, with a value of approximately $ 36 million.
2: Provided capital for the construction of rice warehousing and drying facilities worth approximately $ 30 million in Battambang, Kampong Thom, Kampong Speu and Prey Veng provinces, and provided special intervention funding as working capital of approximately $ 90 million for collection Buy rice from farmers to ensure stability and keep farmers' rice prices stable
4. Implemented a package of special intervention measures in the "Strategic Framework and Program for the Rehabilitation and Promotion of Economic Growth in Living with Kovid-19 in the New Ordinary Path 2021-2023" worth approximately $ 178 million.
Phnom Penh Capital Council praises the safe and secure Water Festival under the shadow of peace, more than 5 million people attended
(Phnom Penh): The 55th Ordinary Meeting of the Phnom Penh Capital Council of the Third Mandate was held on the morning of December 13, 2023 under the chairmanship of Mr. Mop Sarin, Chairman of the Phnom Penh Capital Council and Mr. Khuong Sreng, Governor of the Board of Governors of Phnom Penh. .
On that occasion, Mr. Khuong Sreng said that the Royal Water Festival, floating lanterns, worshiping the moon and Ok Ambok for 3 days and 3 nights, more than 5 million national and international guests came to enjoy without worries. From security issues to safety. At the same time, the Phnom Penh Capital Administration has arranged for comfortable accommodation, a bathroom, a health examination site, and a light headquarters to provide security for the players and the people.
He said, "The problem of garbage, we manage the collection and storage of garbage better with the garbage collection company, in the past during the Water Festival, floating lanterns, worshiping the moon and Ok Ambok for 3 days and 3 nights tonight, the Capital Administration "Phnom Penh needs to use billions of riels to clean up and transport garbage, but for this year we have diverted this money to support the forces."
"Following the instructions of His Excellency Hun Manet, Prime Minister of Cambodia, we have installed security cameras to facilitate the security forces in charge of security, which made this big national festival run smoothly and get Succeeded to receive praise from national and international guests.
Mr. Mop Sarin commended the Phnom Penh Capital Administration for its work on the celebration of the 70th anniversary of the 9th National Independence Day and the Royal Water Festival, the floating of lanterns, the worship of the moon and the success of the people Citizens after a three-year hiatus due to the global epidemic of Kovid-19.
He praised the Board of Governors of Phnom Penh, officials, competent authorities, the Armed Forces, the Armed Forces at all levels, as well as the leaders of all relevant units and private companies that have cooperated well to celebrate the Royal Water Festival. Floating lanterns to worship the moon and Ok Ambok in 2023 in Phnom Penh ensures the maintenance of stability, security, order and better security.
Mr. Mop Sarin stated that on behalf of the Council and the Board of Governors, the people sincerely praised the Royal Government under the energetic and energetic leadership of Samdech Hun Manet, which was successful in just 100 days. In launching the six-point program, which is a contribution to boosting national economic growth.
Deputy Prime Minister Sun Chanthol Chairs a Meeting of the Inter-Ministerial Commission for the Phnom Penh-Siem Reap-Poipet Expressway Infrastructure Project
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Sun Chanthol, Deputy Prime Minister, First Deputy Chairman of the Council for the Development of Cambodia and Chairman of the Inter-Ministerial Commission, this morning, December 13, 2023, chaired a meeting of the Inter-Ministerial Commission of the Expressway Infrastructure Project. From Phnom Penh-Siem Reap-Poipet, with the participation of Mr. Peng Po Na, Minister of Public Works and Transport, and members of the Inter-Ministerial Commission and relevant officials.
Please be reminded that the Phnom Penh-Siem Reap-Poipet Expressway Infrastructure Project is Cambodia's third expressway project after the first Phnom Penh-Sihanoukville Expressway, which opened more than a year ago. The second Phnom Penh-Bavet Expressway project started construction on June 7, 2023 and is currently in the process of implementing the procedures as planned.
The third expressway is more than 400 kilometers long, passing through six capitals and provinces: Phnom Penh, Kandal, Kampong Cham, Kampong Thom, Siem Reap and Banteay Meanchey.
