In fact, Dr. Eang Sophalleth, Minister of Environment, was appointed as the representative of the Prime Minister Hun Manet to lead the Cambodian delegation to attend and deliver a keynote address at the 28th United Nations Framework Convention on Climate Change (COP28). From November 30 to December 12, 2023 in Dubai, United Arab Emirates, with new achievements in Cambodia's policy on the international stage.
Dr. Eang Sophalleth, on the way to the 28th Summit, stated: “Cambodia is highly committed to contributing to the prevention and mitigation of climate change by bringing gifts as an important mechanism and strategy. Seven submissions and discussions at this world conference include:
The 28th Parties Summit of the United Nations Framework Convention on Climate Change (COP28) officially opens on November 30, 2023, with leaders of 196 States Parties, prominent figures, scientists and representatives of the United Nations. National development partners, civil society organizations, countries, observers, journalists, a total of nearly 70,000 participants.
Dr. Eang Sophalleth was welcomed by world leaders at the conference.
The Joint Declaration on Sustainable Agriculture, Sustainable Agriculture and Climate Action was then officially launched at COP28 in Dubai. HE Dr. Eang Sophalleth spoke about the full participation and support of Cambodia's commitment to the Universal Declaration on Food Sustainability, Agriculture and Climate Change Response, which focuses on three priorities, including:
First, improving the livelihoods of local communities vulnerable to the effects of climate change. Second, advocating for food security and nutrition welfare for those in need, especially those experiencing losses and damage from natural disasters related to climate change; and third, expanding smart agriculture practices and strategies. Low carbon emissions are a key component of adaptation and climate reduction efforts.
The leaders of more than 120 countries, including Cambodia, represented by Dr. Eang Sophalleth, adopted an official joint statement on sustainable food systems, agriculture and climate change within the framework of COP28. The significance of this Joint Declaration is consistent with the Royal Government's commitment to smart agriculture, carbon offsets and sustainable development.
On the morning of December 2, 2023, the Minister of Environment, representing Samdech Hun Manet, led a Cambodian delegation to the G77 + China Summit in the framework of COP28 in Dubai, discussing and presenting a common position in response to Global Climate Change Crisis, the Royal Government of Cambodia's Highly Concerned Climate Change
Afterwards, the Minister on behalf of the Royal Government of Cambodia delivered a keynote address at the Nutrition-Climate Nexus program, emphasizing that climate change has adversely affected public health. Causing increased food and financial insecurity leading to malnutrition and diet.
On that occasion, Dr. Eang Sophalleth highlighted Cambodia's priorities, including: campaign to reduce the use of plastic bags and planting 1 million trees per year, aiming to increase forest cover to 60% by 2050 and contribute to land quality For agricultural crops as well.
It should be noted that during the mission, the Minister attended many other multilateral meetings, all of which supported the commitment to respond to climate change at both the national and global levels.
In each meeting, Minister Eang Sophalleth spoke about priority areas and green investment in Cambodia, increasing forest cover by 60%, improving community livelihoods through bamboo plantations, and promoting a clean Cambodia through non-profit campaigns. Use plastic bags in accordance with the Royal Government of Cambodia's first pentagon strategy and especially support environmental chakra strategies that prioritize cleanliness, greenness and sustainability.
