Preah Vihear National Authority will hold a meeting to monitor the progress of work and make recommendations on the conservation of Preah Vihear and Koh Ker temples
The meeting began by welcoming and congratulating the Royal Government of Cambodia on its efforts to include Koh Ker as a World Heritage Site in September 2023, which will increase the focus on conservation activities. From the international community on the mechanisms being implemented within the ICC-Preah Vihear framework.
The meeting highlighted some important work such as the progress report on the restoration of the 5th gopura of Preah Vihear temple by Indian experts, the report on the preliminary study results for the conservation and restoration of the 1st, 2nd and 3rd gopura of the temple of Preah Vihear. By Chinese experts and work to repair the statue of Isoram at the main temple.
In addition, the meeting reported on the report of the National Authority of Preah Vihear, such as: the conservation and repair of ancient stairs north of the Temple of Preah Vihear, the preservation of the temple of Throne (Ping Ling 3), research on human settlements through observation See archeological remains at Koh Ker and Preah Vihear temples, study of ancient irrigation systems in Koh Ker and road improvement projects in Koh Ker.
The Meeting commended the ICC-Preah Vihear Member States for their financial and technical assistance. In fact, since 2018, the United States has provided $ 767,000 for the renovation of the ancient northern staircase being carried out by the National Authority for Preah Vihear and English language training.
