(Phnom Penh): Two armed thieves were sent by the Criminal Police Department of the General Commission of the National Police to the Phnom Penh Municipal Court on December 12, 2023, after cracking down on December 9 at the park. Chbar Wat Botum Vatey is located in Daun Penh district.
The crackdown was carried out under the direction of Lt. Gen. Neng Chuor, director of the Criminal Police Department, and led by Brigadier General But Vannarath, deputy director of the department. But in this operation, Brigadier General But Vannarath was wounded by a group of thieves.
The two suspects were identified as 35-year-old Ros Chanthy alias Ros Sarin alias Mao, who lived in a rented room in Tuol Sangke village, Tuol Sangke commune, Russey Keo district, and 34-year-old Thy Saroeun, a resident of Daun Tung village, Preah Net Preah commune, Mesang district, Prey Veng province.
During the operation, the assailants succeeded and tried to escape, but the police arrived and fired back at the police, injuring one of the officers. When the shots were fired, the police arrested them. As for the small arms, they are from Pov, who used to steal motorcycles together, and Pov was shot dead by the police half a year ago.
Currently, the specialized force is building a case and exhibits to be sent to the Phnom Penh Municipal Court for sentencing according to the law.
