Samdech Hun Sen led a high-level delegation to return to Cambodia safely after a two-day visit to Vietnam
(Phnom Penh): The Prime Minister of Cambodia Samdech Hun Sen led a high-level delegation of the Royal Government of Cambodia to return to Cambodia on the night of December 12, 2023, after concluding two busy official visits. Day in Hanoi, Vietnam.
Please be reminded that His Excellency Hun Manet led a high-level delegation of the Royal Government of Cambodia to pay an official visit to Vietnam at the invitation of Mr. Pham Minh Chinh, Prime Minister of Vietnam on Monday, December 11, 2023.
The visit to Vietnam aims to strengthen the 56-year-old ties and cooperation between Cambodia and Vietnam. More importantly, the current visit of the Prime Minister is to boost trade and investment between the two countries, while the two countries' trade volume has already reached 11 billion US dollars. That.
The visit of the President lasted only two days, but there were many meetings and events with Vietnam's top leaders, presidents of major Vietnamese companies, as well as programs related to trade and investment promotion.
During the meeting with Vietnam's top leaders, both President Hun Manet and Vietnamese leaders discussed the importance of strengthening diplomatic and political and economic ties and cooperation. In every meeting with the Vietnamese leader, the President reaffirmed the policy of the Royal Government of Cambodia, led by Samdech, to maintain good relations with Vietnam without change.
At every meeting, the leaders of Vietnam expressed their congratulations to Samdech Hun Sen, whom the CPP trusted to elect the party's vice president.
Political diplomacy is an important task of Samdech Manet. During his visits abroad, he never missed a meeting with the private sector. During his visit to Vietnam, President Hun Manet met with the leaders of six major Vietnamese companies, including companies investing in Cambodia.
During the visit, His Excellency Hun Manet was also invited to deliver a keynote address to Vietnamese students at the Foreign Trade University. In his keynote address, the Prime Minister, who is a Doctor of Economics from the United Kingdom, focused on the Royal Government of Cambodia's economic development policy and economic relations between Cambodia and Vietnam.
President Hun Manet also co-chaired the meeting with Mr. Pham Minh Chinh, Prime Minister of Vietnam, and Mr. Hun Manet and Mr. Pham Minh Chinh presided over the Cambodia-Vietnam Trade and Investment Promotion Forum 2023. The forum aims to expand trade and investment between Cambodia and Vietnam, which currently has a bilateral trade volume of about 11 billion US dollars.
During this visit, three important documents were signed, including:
1: Memorandum of Understanding on Cooperation in Science, Technology and Innovation between the Ministry of Industry, Science, Technology and Innovation and the Ministry of Science and Technology of Vietnam 2: Memorandum of Understanding on Cooperation between National Institute of Diplomacy and International Relations Vietnam Diplomatic Chamber 3: Memorandum of Understanding between the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce and the Vietnam Chamber of Commerce
