(Phnom Penh): On the afternoon of December 12, 2023, the criminal police of Po Sen Chey district sent the assailant who killed his girlfriend, a factory worker, in a rented room and hanged her body in a room in Po Sen Chey district, Phnom Penh.
The police confirmed that the assailant was named Phum Pha, 20 years old, born in O'Kiki Kandal village, Lumlong commune, Anlong Veng district, Oddar Meanchey province. Prior to his arrest, he was temporarily staying in a rented room in Trapeang Thleung 2 village, Sangkat Choam Chao I, Khan Por Senchey, Phnom Penh.
The murder case occurred at 11 am on December 7, 2023, with a surprise in a rented room in Trapeang Thleung 2 Village, Sangkat Choam Chao I, Khan Por Senchey, Phnom Penh, a worker was found dead. Hanging.
Immediately after receiving the information, the local force went down to the scene and surrounded the scene to wait for the professional officer to come for the autopsy. After the inspection, the police confirmed that: "The victim was covered with a pillow to cover the nose, causing death, and then hung the body in the bathroom. The suspect escaped and authorities also suspected that the case was a murder.
The victim, 19-year-old Sim Rady, was a factory worker living in Room 12C in Trapeang Thleung 2 Village, Sangkat Choam Chao I, Khan Por Senchey, and was born in Sambour Village, Prey Kuy Commune, Kampong Svay District, Kampong Thom Province.
After escaping on December 8, 2023, the suspect confessed in front of the Kralanh District Police in Siem Reap Province after imitating the act of strangling his girlfriend, Sim Marady, until Sla In his rented room in Por Senchey district, Phnom Penh at around 7 pm on December 5, 2023.
Senior Minister Ly Thuch Presents to Donors and Development Partners on the Chairmanship and Hosts of the 2024 Ottawa Convention
(Phnom Penh): Dr. Ly Thuch, Senior Minister and First Vice President of the Mines Authority, on behalf of the Prime Minister of Cambodia Samdech Hun Manet and Chairman of the Mines Authority, made a presentation to donor countries and mine development partners on their chairmanship and hosting. Fifth Review Meeting of the Ottawa Convention 2024.
The presentation of Senior Minister Ly Thuch took place on 12 December 2023 at the Residence of the Australian Ambassador to Cambodia.
Senior Minister Ly Thuch stated that Cambodia is the first country in Asia to receive the support and the right to chair and host the review meeting of the Ottawa Convention, which Cambodia has dubbed the Siem Reap Summit. Angkor on a landmine-free world with about 200 countries and about 700 participants from around the world.
Senior Minister Ly Thuch said that at the upcoming Siem Reap-Angkor Summit, the Mine Authority is actively establishing inter-ministerial commissions and sub-committees to strategize and coordinate all aspects of the event. Careful planning takes place in the areas of transportation, administration, security, health, hospitality and finance, ensuring that every detail is met.
The Senior Minister emphasized that the Siem Reap-Angkor Summit will review the 2019 Oslo Action Plan, revise the strategic plan and develop a high-level Siem Reap-Angkor Statement, and the Siem Reap-Angkor Five-Year Action Plan, which these documents will guide. Let all States Parties and stakeholders implement for the next five years to move towards a landmine-free world.
