(Phnom Penh): A group of Cham cultural youths jointly organized the Cham Cham Traditional Cake Day for 2023 at the Bophana Audiovisual Resource Center last weekend to show the public as well as contribute to the preservation of their identity as part of multiculturalism. Rich in Cambodia.
The ceremony was attended by about 300 people, with a procession of cakes accompanied by drums or drums performed by young people from their community in traditional costumes.
"Champa Traditional Cake Day is a contribution to the promotion and dissemination of Cambodia's multiculturalism," said Apubaka Aputlip, a representative of the Cham Cultural Youth Group. In addition, through this day, the youth of Cham and the youth of other nationalities have the opportunity to meet and exchange cultural knowledge, which is an important foundation of the harmonization of Cambodia.
