By Dr. Chea Monirith, Member of the Executive Committee of the Cambodia-China Friendship Association, Mobile Scale Team Seizes 4 Trucks Over 20% of Permitted Weight in Chbar Ampov District, Fines and Detains for 1 Year
(Phnom Penh): The Mobile Scale Team led by Mr. Seng Chhuon, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Public Works and Transport and Chairman of the Standing Coordinating Committee of the Overweight Transport Inspection Committee, including relevant forces, on 12 December. 2023 Inspected overweight vehicles on Street 110, Sangkat Prek Thmey, Khan Chbar Ampov, Phnom Penh.
During the operation, the team seized four overweight trucks carrying up to 9 tons. The four offending vehicles carrying more than 20% of the allowable weight were fined and detained for one year in accordance with the Law on Roads, Article 60 and Notification No. 049. Proclamation on the enforcement of more stringent measures for heavy transport vehicles driving on the road network.
Traffic accident in Kong Pisey district, Kampong Speu province, injured more than 40 workers, today, the provincial governor visited workers
(Kampong Speu): Mr. Vy Samnang, Governor of Kampong Speu Province, led the Red Cross team of Kampong Speu Branch to visit the workers who met with traffic accident on the morning of December 12, 2023.
The accident occurred when a fuel truck collided with a motorcycle and oversteered to collide with a truck carrying workers on National Road 41 at km 23-24 in Makak village, Snom Krapeu commune, Kong Pisey district. One person was killed (motorcyclist) and 43 workers were injured, including one who was nine months pregnant, while the driver of a truck carrying workers broke both legs.
Mr. Vy Samnang regretted the accident. He also urged drivers to comply with the road traffic law as much as possible to avoid such accidents.
The provincial governor stressed that when encountering the above case, you lose time to work and eat, as well as damage to property, injury to the point of loss of life, so the driver is responsible for the lives of the passengers. On the car must be very careful. In that, the provincial Red Cross branch provided 50,000 Riels per person and 6 general patients 50,000 Riels per person.
