(Pursat): Pursat Polytechnic Institute provides scholarships to 330 young people from poor and vulnerable families to study vocational and technical skills in 16 major subjects for free and receive stipends. From the Royal Government. This is according to the press release of the Institute on December 11, 2023.
According to the institute, young people must be 15 years old or older to study this vocational and technical training course. Vocational and technical training The institute will provide advice on the selection of skills and information on the labor market, especially internships at enterprises, industrial establishments and private companies. After completing this training, young people will receive a technical and vocational degree and the opportunity to study.
Sihanoukville announces end to open defecation
(Sihanoukville): The completion of high-level open defecation (ODF +) in Sihanoukville demonstrates the concern of the Royal Government and the Ministry of Rural Development, as well as sub-national administrations. Leadership is to be more motivated to fulfill the roles and responsibilities aimed at improving the well-being and living standards of local people.
This is what Mr. Cheam Him, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Rural Development, said on December 12, 2023, in the celebration of the victory of Sihanoukville as a city to end open defecation with the participation of provincial leaders, municipal authorities, districts, communes, sangkats and villages. From the 5 districts of Sihanoukville, partner organizations and chairmen of deputy departments around the province.
The Secretary of State of the Ministry of Rural Development commended the authorities at all levels and the people of Sihanoukville, especially Sihanoukville, for being thoroughly evaluated by the provincial Department of Rural Development in cooperation with the provincial commission. Complete open defecation (ODF) in August 2023.
At the same time, Mr. Prak Sovann, Director of the Department of Rural Development of Preah Sihanouk Province, said that the activities to encourage people to change their habits from open urination to the construction and use of toilets, which so far the whole province of Sihanoukville has just received There are 15 ODF villages, 4 ODF communes and 1 ODF + city.
The provincial administration, which has the technical working group for rural water supply and sanitation, the provincial rural development department, district authorities, communes and partner organizations must continue to work together to support the rural water supply and sanitation sector so that the whole of Sihanoukville can Complete the provincial ODF defecation in 2025, especially to achieve ODF in 4 more districts and to achieve ODF throughout the province.
Lok Chumteav Pech Chanmony: Under the Shadow of Peace, Cambodians Have Many Opportunities and Options to Practice Their Favorite Sports
(Phnom Penh): On the evening of December 11, 2023, at the National Olympic Stadium, Lok Chumteav Dr. Pech Chanmony Hun Manet presided over the closing ceremony of the 2023 National Dance Competition organized by the Ministry of Education. Youth and Sports in collaboration with the National Olympic Committee of Cambodia and the National Sports Federation.
On that occasion, Lok Chumteav Dr. Pech Chanmony Hun Manet praised the ability and talent of the Cambodian dance players who showed their skillful dance techniques and highly appreciated the efforts of the Ministry of Education. Youth and Sports and the National Olympic Committee of Cambodia and the National Sports Federation for their proud achievements.
At the same time, Lok Chumteav Dr. called on the relevant ministries and institutions as well as the private sector to continue to support the budget, equipment, techniques and training facilities for the Dance Sports Federation of Cambodia to continue the mission and develop the resources of athletes in this sport. Even more progress.
She added that under the shadow of peace, the people of Cambodia, especially among the youth, have many opportunities and options, both time and ability to practice their favorite sport and have developed into a good resource for society to be able. Participate in international competitions and win more national medals.
Taking that opportunity, Lok Chumteav Dr. also instructed the Cambodian Dance and Sports Federation, as well as all athletes to continue training and good health, adhere to the code of ethics and good representation of Cambodia. Create memories of international friends as well as maintain solidarity and friendship with athletes of different countries for the upcoming competitions.
It should be noted that the 2023 National Dance Championship was held on December 11, 2023 with the participation of 50 athletes from 5 clubs under the support of the Ministry. Education, youth and sports.
