(Phnom Penh): The Australian Federal Police has pledged to further strengthen cooperation with the Cambodian National Police in training law enforcement officers and combating transnational crime.
The pledge was made this morning, December 12, 2023, when General Sar Thet, General Commissioner of the National Police, allowed Mr. Anthony Mok Kwai, Senior Police Chief of the Australian Federal Police, at the Embassy of Australia to pay a courtesy call and say goodbye. Mission to Cambodia and Introduce Ms. Ras Ball, Senior Police Chief, who will continue to work as the Australian Federal Police Representative at the Australian Embassy in Cambodia at the Ministry of Interior.
General Sar Thet welcomed and gave some key recommendations to Ms. Ras Ball, Senior Australian Federal Police Chief at the new Australian Embassy in Cambodia, and thanked Mr. Anthony Mok Kwai for his cooperation with the Cambodian National Police. Achieved good results, including training, information exchange, and the suppression of many types of transnational crime in many cases.
General Sar Thet also requested Ms. Rasbell to continue to improve the existing cooperation, especially to increase the cooperation on training law enforcement officers so that the resources of the National Police officers can be achieved in accordance with the current strategic needs of the Royal Government. The government in the seventh mandate, with Samdech Hun Sen as Prime Minister.
In response, Mr. Anthony Mukquay and Ms. Ras Ball agreed and pledged to further strengthen cooperation with the Cambodian National Police, including the training of law enforcement officers and the fight against cross-border crime.
At the same time, in return for the past efforts during the mandate of Mr. Anthony Mukquay, Senior Police Chief of the Australian Federal Police, the National Police Commissioner through the Ministry of Interior also requested the Royal Government to award him the Medal of Honor. Anthony Mukquay, who was inaugurated in the presence of His Excellency Australian Ambassador Justin Whyatt.
