(Hanoi, Vietnam): Duke Lim Heng, Vice President of the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce, on December 12, 2023, highlighted that Cambodia is a good destination for foreign investors who want to find a wide market, favorable policies and growth potential. .
This emphasis was made on the occasion of Duke Lim Heng's participation in the Cambodia-Vietnam Investment and Trade Promotion Forum 2023, chaired by Cambodian Prime Minister Hun Manet and Vietnamese Prime Minister Pham Minh Chinh.
The ceremony was held in Hanoi, Vietnam on the afternoon of December 12, 2023.
"Cambodia is a great destination for foreign investors looking for a wider market, favorable policies and growth potential," said Duke Lim Heng. "Cambodia has shown resilience to the crisis, adapting to the global epidemic, Kovid-19 and global trade tensions."
In addition, Duke Lim Heng said that Vietnam and Cambodia have a long history of friendship and solidarity. Bilateral relations continue to be strong and jointly developed in all fields, especially trade and investment.
He added that the two countries' economic ties have been growing remarkably and have achieved a lot in recent years thanks to the efforts and initiatives of both governments and the business community. Two.
At the same time, Duke Lim Heng highlighted that in the future, some sectors provide important opportunities for cooperation and joint investment:
* Agriculture: Utilizing Vietnam's agricultural technology skills and Cambodia's fertile land to boost agricultural productivity and food security.
* Tourism: Promote tourism development cooperation by using the richness of the cultural heritage and natural beauty of the two countries to attract international tourism.
Infrastructure: Invest in infrastructure projects such as roads, bridges and power lines to improve connectivity and trade flows.
* Technology: Promote the transfer of technology and the exchange of digital knowledge and support the growth of the two countries' innovative industries.
Education and training: Promote cooperation in education and training programs for the two countries' labor force to have the necessary skills in line with the globalized economy.
He added that these are just some of the potential areas that can cooperate and benefit from each other, and he believes that there are still many opportunities that can be explored and exploited because Cambodia-Vietnam has a vision and The same desire for peace, stability and prosperity in the region.
Duke Lim Heng emphasized that Cambodia is a good destination for foreign investors to find a wide market, favorable policies and growth potential. Cambodia has shown resilience to the crisis, adapting to the global epidemic, Kovid-19 and global trade tensions.
Meanwhile, Duke Lim Heng said that the new investment law came into force in 2021, which provides a clear and complete legal framework for investment in Cambodia. The law provides many incentives, guarantees and protections for local and foreign investors.
The Royal Government of Cambodia, under the leadership of Samdech Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, has launched a Pentagon Strategy, a long-term plan towards achieving Cambodia to become a high-middle-income country by 2030 and a high-income country. High in 2050.
In addition, Duke Lim Heng said that Prince Hun Manen has promoted the bilateral relations between Cambodia and Vietnam, especially the business forum to promote investment and trade twice a year and agreed on the sector. Tourism by targeting three countries: Cambodia, Vietnam and Laos.
Duke Lim Heng said that on this occasion, an agreement was signed between the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce and the Vietnam Chamber of Commerce and Industry. Economic trade between the two countries. Samdech Hun Sen: Cambodia is not only focused on new investment, but also on all existing investment projects.
(Hanoi, Vietnam): Cambodian Prime Minister Hun Manet has expressed his pleasure at Vietnam's investment in rubber plantations in Cambodia. The President announced that he supports and supports all Vietnamese investment in Cambodia.
The Prime Minister made the remarks while allowing Mr. Chin Cong Kha, Chairman of the Board of the Vietnam Rubber Industry Coalition (VRG) and his colleagues to pay a courtesy call on the afternoon of December 12, 2023 in Hanoi, Vietnam.
During the meeting, Mr. Chin Kong Kha thanked the President for taking the time to allow him and his colleagues to pay a courtesy call. Mr. Chin Kongkha briefed the President on the business activities of companies investing in rubber plantations in Cambodia, as well as their contribution to the construction of infrastructure, including schools, pagodas, health centers, roads and local community development, as well as human resource training. On rubber industry expertise as well.
Mr. Chin Kong Kha thanked the Royal Government of Cambodia as well as the relevant ministries and institutions and authorities for facilitating the company's business operations in the past until the company has grown and been able to contribute to economic development. Cambodia.
Hun Manet welcomed the presence of VRG management and thanked the company for its investment in Cambodia as well as the import of new technologies in the agro-industrial sector that have helped to improve product quality and capacity. Human resources in this field.
He also expressed support for the company's direction to expand investment in Cambodia and stated that the Royal Government will continue to provide the necessary protection.
He confirmed to the company that the Royal Government of Cambodia is not only focused on attracting new investment, but also always pays attention to all existing investment projects in Cambodia.
He also highlighted the priority policy of the Royal Government of Cambodia in promoting the agricultural sector through the establishment of mechanisms for the establishment of agricultural communities and cultivation, which ensures the quantity and quality of exports in the form of raw materials. , Semi-finished products and finished products to the international market.
