Takeo Provincial Administration's Bak Dai Gate Office Rejects Posting of Pressure on Rice Traders to Pay
(Takeo): The Takeo Provincial Administration's Border Checkpoint Office recently announced its rejection of social media posts and some websites that published false information that officials at the Bak Dai Gate were stepping on it. Traders by requiring Vietnamese traders to pay the authorities from 300,000 riel to 500,000 riel per boat.
The Bak Dai Border Gate Inspection Office added that the authorities of the Bak Dai Border Gate Inspection Office had never met with Vietnamese rice traders or stopped rice boats from buying rice from Cambodian farmers in Angkor Borei district. Broken arm once.
In the past, all border guards, especially the director of the gate inspection office, have always instructed the relevant authorities to make every effort to facilitate all rice transporters to Vietnam smoothly and quickly.
The report that the director of the Bak Dai border checkpoint and other authorities forced Vietnamese rice traders to pay 300,000 to 400,000 riel per boat is untrue and baseless allegations. Precisely because all the rice traders have never met with the director of the gate inspection office and the gate authority, and for the transportation of agricultural products, there are no customs duties, export taxes or other fees.
