Ministry of Social Affairs Prepares for the 4th ASEAN Partnership Conference 2023 in Siem Reap
(Siem Reap): Mr. Suong Menglong, Secretary of State and Chairman of the Working Group on International Cooperation, representing Mr. Chea Somethy, Minister of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation (MoSVY), on December 12, 2023, presided over the opening ceremony of the ASEAN Summit. The 4th 2023 Partnership at Borey Angkor Resort and Spa in Siem Reap.
The opening ceremony of the ASEAN Conference was also attended by representatives of the Ministry of Women's Affairs, representatives of the ASEAN Commission on the Promotion and Protection of the Rights of Women and Children (ACWC), representatives of the ASEAN Committee on Women (ACW) of ASEAN Member States, development partners and A total of 120 civil society organizations with direct and online participation.
According to Mr. Suong Menglong, the 4th ASEAN Partnership Conference 2023 aims to strengthen cooperation between all ASEAN Member States and development partners, UN agencies, international organizations and NGOs. Civil society working together to promote the rights of women and children in the ASEAN region to achieve the ASEAN Goals and Sustainable Development Goals 2030 "without leaving any women and children behind."
