(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Economy and Finance and the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and Development of the United Kingdom have signed a Memorandum of Understanding to promote the development of infrastructure projects, identification of funding sources and mobilization of private sector projects, as well as facilitation. To prepare for the development of infrastructure projects in Cambodia.
Through this Memorandum of Understanding, the Royal Government of the United Kingdom aims to provide technical support and investment promotion to Cambodia through the UK Investment Partnership Framework by mobilizing specialized resources from the private sector and linking to other sources of funding. Regional and international to meet Cambodia's infrastructure needs.
Mr. Meas Sok Sen San highlighted the importance of the Royal Government's Pentagon Strategy - Phase 1, which focuses on five key pillars: growth, employment, equity, efficiency, and sustainability in participating in public infrastructure development and progress. Achieve the vision of Cambodia 2050.
On this basis, the Ministry of Economy and Finance, in collaboration with the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and Development of the United Kingdom, is committed to further strengthening cooperation between the two countries and promoting UK investment in infrastructure development in Cambodia.
