(Phnom Penh): This morning, December 12, 2023, the Phnom Penh Capital Administration organized a ceremony at Wat Phnom Historical Resort under the chairmanship of Mr. Im Ron Hassan, Deputy Governor of Phnom Penh, representing Mr. Khuong Sreng, Governor of Phnom Penh and Mr. Sim Kimsan, Deputy Director of National Authority. Fight against AIDS and Mr. Ngy Mean Heng, Director of Phnom Penh Health Department.
Ngy Mean Heng, Director of the Phnom Penh Municipal Health Department, reminded of the support provided to people living with HIV, reminded of the tragedy of those who died of HIV / AIDS, and reminded people across the country to remember the dangers of HIV infection for both. Together we can eliminate the spread of HIV and contribute to the development of humanity. To this day, HIV and AIDS remain a threat to public health.
The occasion also called on LGBT people, especially gay men, to pay more attention to sexual issues and prevention to reduce the spread of HIV / AIDS because of the rate of HIV infection. About 60% are gay.
Mr. Ngy Mean Heng said that according to the 2022 summary data of the National Center for AIDS, Dermatology and STIs and the United Nations AIDS in Cambodia, the total number of people living with HIV in Phnom Penh. There were about 20,952 people, of which 23,893 were receiving HIV services.
Mr. Som Kimsan, Deputy Director of the National AIDS Authority, said that according to the survey conducted by the HACC Health Coordination Committee for the first 11 months of 2023, the working group of the committee has surveyed and educated people about HIV / AIDS. More than 40,000 people, and about 30,000, have volunteered for a retest, which has been positive for more than 800 people.
Mr. Im Ron Hassan, Deputy Governor of Phnom Penh and Vice Chairman of the Phnom Penh AIDS Committee, on behalf of Mr. Khuong Sreng, Governor of Phnom Penh, said that through the message of Samdech Kittiprittbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, President of the Cambodian Red Cross, sent important messages. To our compatriots, especially our youth, including:
* First, be committed to preventing the spread and ending of AIDS by 2025 by adhering to the principles of equality and environment.
* Second: We must practice peer-to-peer education to stay away from drugs, sexual immorality, which is a high risk of HIV / STIs, and to strive to learn to maintain good health and eat good nutrition. The old saying goes, love yourself to love food
* Third: Compatriots who are suspected of being exposed to HIV must seek counseling and testing for HIV as soon as possible, receive health care and use antiretroviral drugs properly, regularly and consistently.
* Fourth: Pregnant women should check and take care of their pregnancy with a midwife or doctor at least 4 times before giving birth and get HIV / syphilis and liver infection prevention services from health services.
* Fifth: Please, all compatriots, encourage and do not discriminate or stigmatize people living with HIV and AIDS.
* Sixth: Please call for men who have sex with men, transgender people, women who serve in entertainment venues, adults, etc. Must participate in the implementation of measures to prevent the transmission of HIV properly for personal health and to prevent new infections and lead to the end of HIV / AIDS by 2025 successfully.
