(VOVworld) - Minister of Commerce Cham Nimmol and Minister of Industry, Science, Technology and Innovation Hem Vandy met with Minister of Industry and Trade Nguyen Hong Dien of the Socialist Republic of Vietnam to discuss solidarity. And a partnership on trade and industry cooperation between Cambodia and Vietnam.
The meeting between the Minister of Commerce and the Ministry of Industry of Cambodia and the Minister of Industry and Trade of Vietnam on Tuesday morning, December 12, 2023, took place on the occasion that Mrs. Cham Nimmol and Mr. Hem Vandy accompanied the President. PM pays official visit to Socialist Republic of Vietnam
On that occasion, the two sides exchanged views on how to further strengthen trade and industry cooperation, including: Strengthening cooperation on trade facilitation to reduce trade barriers. In order to promote the growth of Cambodian-Vietnamese trade, especially technical cooperation on production in the processing industry.
The two sides recommended that the technical working groups of the three ministries examine the feasibility study of legal documents in order to be able to further strengthen cooperation in various fields under the jurisdiction of the three ministries.
At the same time, the two sides reaffirmed their commitment to strengthen and promote trade and industrial cooperation for the mutual economic benefit of the two peoples and nations.
