Mr. Voeung Dinh Fe also congratulated Samdech Thipady on his election as the Vice President of the Cambodian People's Party (CPP) at the 44th Central Committee Meeting of the 5th Mandate. The Speaker of the National Assembly of Vietnam also congratulated the Cambodian People's Party for its overwhelming support, as reflected in the recent results of the 7th National Assembly election in July 2023.
During the meeting, Mr. Vung Dinh Fei also recalled the good memories he received from attending the 43rd ASEAN Inter-Parliamentary Assembly (AIPA) hosted by the National Assembly of Cambodia, as well as the opportunity to pay a courtesy call on Samdech. Techo Hun Sen in November 2022 ago.
In response, President Hun Manet thanked the President of the National Assembly of Vietnam for his warm welcome. He highlighted the long-standing and traditional relationship between the two countries during the past 56 years of diplomatic ties.
The President also conveyed a message of greetings from National Assembly President Khuon Sodary to the President of the National Assembly of Vietnam and thanked the leadership of the National Assembly of Vietnam for their support to the National Assembly of Cambodia.
France, Germany and Italy support EU sanctions on Hamas
(Brussels): France, Germany and Italy have called on the European Union to impose special sanctions on Hamas as the bloc's foreign ministers meet on Monday to consider possible next steps. In resolving the crisis in the Middle East. This is according to the release by the AFP news agency on December 11, 2023.
Possible measures discussed at the meeting include a financial crackdown on Hamas and a travel ban on Israeli settlers responsible for the West Bank violence.
"This means that Europe will be more committed to fighting Hamas' infrastructure and financial support, as well as the internationalization of the group without a chance," the letter said. "In return for representing the Palestinian people."
The head of state of Vietnam emphasized this during a meeting with President Hun Manet on the afternoon of December 11, 2023 in Hanoi, Vietnam.
During the meeting, Mr. Vann Thuong warmly welcomed the first official visit on behalf of Prime Minister Hun Manet and a high-level delegation of the Royal Government of Cambodia in Vietnam.
The Vietnamese Head of State also congratulated the President on his election as the Vice President of the Cambodian People's Party (CPP) at the 44th Central Committee Meeting of the Cambodian People's Party (CPP). The results strongly demonstrate the party's confidence in the leadership capacity of the president.
Mr. Vann Thuong also expressed his satisfaction with the official visit of a high-level delegation of the Royal Government of Cambodia to Vietnam. The visit clearly reflects the continued spirit of strengthening the Cambodia-Vietnam bilateral relationship in the spirit of friendship and good solidarity between the two countries and peoples.
Mr. Vann Thuong also expressed his belief that under the leadership of the Prime Minister and the next generation of leaders full of energy, Cambodia will continue its development even stronger.
Samdech Hun Sen thanked for the warm welcome from the President of Vietnam. He stressed that Vietnam is the first country in ASEAN to pay an official visit as Prime Minister to promote closer bilateral cooperation between the two countries.
The Vietnamese President praised and supported the outcome of the talks between the Prime Ministers of Cambodia and Vietnam. The Vietnamese Head of State sent a message of greetings to the King and Queen Mother of Cambodia, as well as to Samdech Techo and other Cambodian leaders.
The Vietnamese Head of State also stated that he was always looking forward to welcoming the King of Cambodia on his upcoming state visit to Vietnam. UN peacekeeping mission in Mali officially ends after 10 years
(Mali): A UN peacekeeping mission in Mali has officially ended its decade-long deployment in the country, a spokesman announced on Monday. Ordered to withdraw from the country's military leaders. This is according to the release by the AFP news agency on December 11, 2023.
The withdrawal of the UN peacekeeping mission MINUSMA has raised concerns that fighting between the army and armed groups to control territory will intensify.
