Deputy PM Sar Sokha orders more security for upcoming elections as hostilities continue to provoke riots
(Phnom Penh): Deputy Prime Minister Sar Sokha, Minister of Interior and Chairman of the Permanent Security Command for National and Sub-National Elections (NCPC), has ordered all competent forces to remain focused. Take care to protect the upcoming election firmly, while the enemy group continues to nurture attempts to provoke unrest and interfere in the internal affairs of Cambodia.
Dr. Sar Sokha emphasized that for the upcoming election, the Royal Government of the 7th legislature, which is the new legislature, does not want any problems to occur, especially regarding external interference in Cambodia's internal affairs. There is an intention to try to cause chaos during the election, so focus on security work and be on the lookout for suspects.
In response to the important events ahead, Deputy Prime Minister Sar Sokha, Minister of Interior, Chairman of the Permanent Security Command for National and Sub-National Elections (NCPC), issued the following instructions:
* First, the Capital-Provincial Administrative Unity Command must enhance its role and responsibility in leading and coordinating forces under the Capital-Provincial Electoral Security Mechanism and providing security services at all stages of the election process.
At the same time, we must continue to pay attention to managing the security situation in our localities, including further promoting the policy of safe villages, communes and sangkats in order to strengthen security, order and order. In a better society.
* Second, all relevant competent forces, which are election security agents, must be neutral and respect the election law, election regulations and ethics as election security agents, and must facilitate the provision of Services to all targets and targets to be protected in a transparent and non-discriminatory manner.
* Fifth: Continue to pay attention to monitor and take measures to prevent and coordinate the phase of the election campaign because it is a stage of political struggle, especially related to expression.
* Sixth: The election phase, as well as the counting of ballots, this stage is also important, so the Unity Command at all levels and all security forces must raise a high vigilance and be responsible for the defense and cooperate. Good with the National Election Committee at all levels, especially the head of the polling station to count the ballots to better manage each polling station.
In that, the election security agents who personally protect each polling station must strictly abide by the election law, regulations and appropriate procedures for the election. At the same time, protection must continue to ensure the absolute security of the program as well as a large number of tasks such as ballot delivery, ballot counting, as well as accurate records of ballots at designated locations.
