In the first 11 months of 2023, Cambodia exported 20,494 million US dollars worth of goods to international markets, up 1.2 percent from 20,243 million US dollars in the same period in 2022. . This is according to data from the General Department of Customs and Excise of Cambodia.
According to the report of the General Department of Customs and Excise of Cambodia, from January to November 2023, the volume of Cambodia's trade with the international community amounted to 42.5 billion US dollars, of which Cambodia exported 20494 million. The dollar rose 1.2 percent while imports amounted to $ 22,006 million, down 5.4 percent.
Cambodia's exports include garments and accessories made from fabrics, machinery and electrical equipment, garments and accessories made from double needles, rubber and rubber products, and other agricultural products. Secretary-General of the Communist Party of Vietnam: The visit of Samdech Manet will further strengthen the bilateral relations between Cambodia and Vietnam.
