Philippines summons Chinese ambassador over latest clashes in South China Sea
The Philippines on Monday summoned the Chinese ambassador and determined the possibility of expulsion after a Philippine boat and a Chinese ship collided in a disputed reef in the South China Sea. This is according to the release by the AFP news agency on Monday, December 11, 2023.
(Phnom Penh): Before World War I, the United Kingdom was considered the "immortal sun" due to the policy of expanding the colony, which is stronger than the French Empire and the German Empire. Do you know which countries and territories were once under this European colony?
Britain, like other European powers, has been striving to expand its colonial policy since the 16th century. The colonial politics of this superpower has always been more victorious than any other superpower.
For Britain, it was decided to conduct military operations to occupy the colonies from many countries, including:
* Asia and the Pacific
In the Pacific, this mighty empire also colonized Australia and New Zealand.
* Americas
On this black continent, Britain invaded the kingdoms of Egypt, Nigeria, East Africa, and South Africa. In addition to the above countries and territories, the United Kingdom also colonized many other small islands around the world.
Their colonial policy was to achieve four main goals, including:
1: Collect raw materials from the colony to be used in industry in their country.
2. When their industrial plants produce finished products, they sell those products in the markets in those colonies.
Third, strengthen military bases on existing colonies to continue to invade new territories under colonization.
Fourth: Strengthen its prestige to trade or want to control more important areas in the world.
By 1914, the territory under British rule was a quarter of the world's land area and a quarter of the world's population.
