Ms. M. Rachana, Undersecretary of State and spokesperson for the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, told reporters on December 11, 2023 that the road cleared by the authorities is on the border between the park and private land. Not in the conservation land.
She explained that the clearing of this road is to prevent wildfires that have occurred frequently every year, and this clearing is not only able to prevent wildfires, it also provides another way to The people living in this area traveled through it appropriately and easily.
She said she did not understand why the Wild Life Alliance gave an interview accusing the government, the Ministry of Agriculture and the authorities of clearing the land for personal gain or developing any project that violated and forgot the natural resources that the government had. And is working to protect. The Ministry completely rejects this claim.
"What we do is to protect our natural resources, to make it easier for our people living in this area, so we have done nothing wrong and what we do is to serve the national interest," she added. And the people. "Therefore, we will continue to do so."
Mr. Nhek Rattanak Pich, Director of Phnom Tamao Protected Wildlife Park and Botanical Garden, also explained that Phnom Tamao Protected Wildlife Park and Botanical Garden, which the King issued a Royal Decree to protect 2,25,000 hectares More than 20 kilometers long, surrounded by railways, both new and old.
He said the clearing site was on an old railway line, with authorities clearing it to make it easier for residents to travel and prevent wildfires from entering the park.
