Deputy Prime Minister Sar Sokha and Chairman of the NEC chaired a meeting to announce the sub-decree on the establishment of the NCDD and the decision on the establishment of the NCDD Secretariat.
Sub-Decree on the Establishment of the Permanent Security Command for National and Sub-National Elections (NCPCS), signed by Prime Minister Hun Manet on September 20, 2023, was established to Directs the protection of the annual voter registration and registration and the national, sub-national elections of all legislatures.
Separately, the Decision on the Establishment of the Secretariat of the Permanent Security Command for National and Sub-National Elections (NCPC) was established by Deputy Prime Minister Sar Sokha, Minister of Interior on November 17, 2023. General Sar Thet, the National Police Commissioner, is the chairman, accompanied by six deputies and several other members.
* Monitor the implementation of the law of the Electoral Security Structure Mechanism and the Election Security Agency in accordance with the inter-institutional plan between the Ministry of Interior, the Ministry of National Defense and the National Election Committee.
Disseminate plans, action plans, regulations and instructions on electoral security protection to relevant ministries, institutions and units, especially electoral security structure mechanisms and electoral security agencies, as well as local authorities at all levels for information and cooperation.
Gather regular information on the electoral security situation from the ministries, sub-national administrative institutions and relevant units, the mechanism of electoral security structure, and report to the President of the CEC and the Royal Government for review and timely measures.
* Monitor all incidents or events related to the security situation of the election process and information from all sources that affect the security environment of the election process in order to clarify, react, and neutralize the influence of information that pollutes the election security environment. In severe cases, seek advice from the President of the CSC to take legal action.
* Organize the meeting or meeting of the NCDD by making an invitation to all the components and stakeholders to participate in accordance with the principle of the NCDD chairman.
* Propose a budget for the training of skills for election security agents, a budget for the supply of fuel for the means of use or the purchase of necessary equipment for election security, to submit to the President of the National Election Commission for review and request for approval from the Royal Government
