The Prime Minister of Vietnam congratulated Prime Minister Hun Manet on the morning of December 11, 2023 during a two-day official visit from December 11 to 12. 2023 in the Socialist Republic of Vietnam.
During the meeting, Mr. Pham Minh Chinh welcomed the first official visit on behalf of Prime Minister Hun Manet and a high-level delegation of the Royal Government of Cambodia in the Socialist Republic of Vietnam. Congratulations on the success of the Extraordinary General Assembly of the Cambodian People's Party.
At the same time, the Prime Minister emphasized that through the visit of President Hun Manet on this occasion, the Cambodian-Vietnamese bilateral relations will grow stronger and stronger in line with the spirit of good neighborliness, traditional friendship, all-round cooperation and stability. Long lasting.
He also expressed confidence that under the honorable leadership of the Prime Minister, the Cambodian fleet will be further developed towards achieving the vision of Cambodia 2030 and 2050.
In response, Prime Minister Hun Manet expressed his pleasure at the bilateral working meeting and thanked the Vietnamese Prime Minister for his warm welcome on his first official visit as Prime Minister of Cambodia. The Kingdom of Cambodia in the Socialist Republic of Vietnam on this occasion.
At the same time, Samdech Thipadei also brought a message from Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Chairman of the Supreme Council of the King of the Kingdom of Cambodia to the Prime Minister of Vietnam.
NEC Releases Results of Meeting to Review and Decide on Registration of Political Parties and Candidates for the 5th Mandate Senate Election
(Phnom Penh): The National Election Committee (NEC) has released the results of the meeting to review and decide on the application for registration of political parties and the list of candidates for the 5th legislative election in 2024.
The meeting was chaired by Mr. Prach Chan, Chairman of the NEC, on the morning of Monday, December 11, 2023 at the meeting hall of the NEC.
After reviewing the documents and listening to the report of the specialized unit, the NEC meeting decided as follows:
First, officially recognize the registration application of the Khmer Will Party, which has 8 regions and the list of candidates for the 5th legislative election in 2024.
2. Officially recognize the application for registration of the National Forces Party, which has 8 regions and the list of candidates for the 5th Senate election in 2024.
3: Issue a letter of notification to FUNCINPEC to meet the required conditions. The content of the letter states that the shortcomings that the party needs to fill are as follows:
Declaration on the bank account in which the political party has deposited various income, including contributions from any source in a bank in the Kingdom of Cambodia recognized by the National Bank of Cambodia. * Deposit Receipt 15,000,000 Riels issued by the General Department of the National Treasury.
4: In various agendas, after listening to the report of the specialized unit, the NEC meeting decided that the Department of Voter Data Management and Voter List to implement the 9 final decisions of the 6 commune councils of Kampong Speu province. Decided to keep 1 name in the complaint and decided to delete 8 names in the first voter list in 2023.
5: Agreed on the image of the educational video spot for 1 story to be published in the 5th legislative election for the Senate in 2024.
According to the election calendar, the 5th Senate election will be held on Sunday, February 25, 2024.
A spokesman for the UN General Assembly said a special meeting of the General Assembly was proposed on Tuesday afternoon by representatives of Egypt and Mauritania, who are chairing the Arab League and heads of cooperation. Islam. According to diplomatic sources, the UN General Assembly may vote on a ceasefire resolution during Tuesday's meeting.
The draft resolution is expected to be similar to the UN Security Council resolution vetoed by the United States last Friday, expressing grave concern over the devastating humanitarian situation on the Gaza Strip. And calls for an immediate humanitarian ceasefire and the immediate and unconditional release of all remaining hostages.
