Beijing and Phnom Penh jointly form official media to provide information on how to attract more tourists
This statement was made during a courtesy call between Mr. Khuong Sreng, Governor of the Phnom Penh Municipal Council, and Mr. Lu Yan, Vice Chairman of the Beijing Municipal Committee of the People's Political Consultative Conference of the People's Republic of China. In the morning of December 11, 2023 at Phnom Penh Capital Hall.
Mr. Khuong Sreng reminded that Phnom Penh is a ghost city, but after the liberation of the country by Samdech Techo Hun Sen and the Cambodian People's Party, this city has developed. The Phnom Penh Capital Administration has well managed both security and infrastructure development. However, despite such progress, challenges still require the Phnom Penh authorities to address, especially traffic congestion and solid waste.
He said that Phnom Penh used to have only 300,000 people, but now, with the growth, Phnom Penh has increased to more than 3 million people in and out of Phnom Penh every day.
Mr. Khuong Sreng stated, "It is likely that China and Cambodia are a steel-friendly relationship, and the latter is a diamond friendship." Please, Chinese friends, help spread good news, real news from Cambodia to attract Chinese tourists to visit Cambodia. "Through the sisterhood between Beijing and Phnom Penh, Chinese tourists will increase."
The governor of Phnom Penh stated that Cambodia and China, especially Beijing and Phnom Penh, will form an official media account to provide information to each other in order to attract more tourists.
At the same time, Mr. Khuong Sreng asked Beijing to provide scholarships to Cambodian students to study in Beijing, a city with good human resource training, and asked Mr. Luo Yan to discuss with the Governor of Beijing. These two problems.
