UN chief says UN Security Council "disabled" over Gaza war resolution
Guterres said in a speech to the Doha Forum in Qatar that the council was "crippled by the geographical divisions that were destroying the solution to the war between Israel and Hamas."
"The authority and credibility of this institution has been severely damaged by its slow response to the conflict," he said. The statement comes two days after the United States used its veto to block a resolution calling for a ceasefire in Gaza.
The UN Secretary-General has used Article 99 of the UN Charter, which is rarely used to convene the Security Council, in what the head of the international community sees as "a potential threat." "To maintain international peace and security."
