However, the prolongation of the global economic crisis for the past three years has made Cambodians more vulnerable and declining in income. These problems make the possibility of monthly repayment of people owed to the bank more difficult, if not resolved, may cause the banking sector to fall into crisis like any other sector.
Dr. Ky Sereyvath, an economist at the Royal Academy of Cambodia, said that despite the economic crisis, people were unable to repay their loans, but debtors could not afford to repay the bank because the bank needed it. Profits to make themselves sustainable in business and to pay interest to depositors and to sources of capital from abroad.
He said that working together to solve the problem is the most important strategy to keep the banking sector strong and maintain business stability.
He explained that if people face problems and lose their income completely, they must report to the banking and financial institutions, and the banking institutions should inform their agents to understand if in the conditions where people can not afford to pay. Report to the National Bank and find a solution, otherwise the people who are in debt will easily fall into poverty.
He added that the banking and financial institutions and the National Bank need to do a thorough study on this issue to delay or suspend payments for a while, or the government needs to help create jobs and create jobs for them.
As for those who have lost their jobs or occupations, they can return to study the vocational skills that the Royal Government has been developing a strategy to provide training to 1 million skilled people. When people are able to find work and earn money, they will be able to repay their debts.
Also, for those who have lost some income, should apply for a loan to help reduce the amount of monthly repayments to the bank.
