(Dubai): Dr. Eang Sophalleth, Minister of the Environment, made a national statement on behalf of Cambodian Prime Minister Hun Manet at the 28th Conference (COP28) to demonstrate Cambodia's high commitment to international efforts. To contribute to solving the problem of climate change this morning, December 9, 2023.
In front of leaders from 197 countries around the world, the Minister urged the members of COP28 to increase unprecedented global cooperation in response to climate change by ensuring the well-being of communities. And the health of our planet.
Dr. Eang Sophalleth emphasized Cambodia's commitment to join the UNFCCC signatories as follows:
1: To keep the temperature rise at 1.5 degrees Celsius, Cambodia is committed to launching a long-term carbon neutral strategy by 2050.
