(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Justice on December 08, 2023 issued a press release in response to criticism on social media of the Kampong Chhnang Provincial Court's decision on the criminal group of victims who have been cracked down on in the past.
In a press release obtained by Fresh News, a spokesman for the Ministry of Justice stated that after receiving the above information, in order to have a clear and comprehensive basis on this case, the Ministry of Justice has assigned an inspection team to conduct an immediate investigation. At Kampong Chhnang Provincial Court on December 4, 2023 and got clear results around this case.
According to the Ministry of Justice, the Kampong Chhnang Provincial Court has accepted the case of drug offense No. 742 dated 14 September 2022 by the Kampong Chhnang Provincial Prosecutor's Office and has also expanded the anti-money laundering investigation.
Based on the above, the Ministry of Justice considers that the decision of the Kampong Chhnang Provincial Court is correct and strict, with the sentence of imprisonment and a fine up to the maximum sentence prescribed by law.
In order to ensure the correct implementation of the law, especially in relation to the above-mentioned confiscated items, the Ministry of Justice has decided to appeal to the Prosecutor General of the Phnom Penh Court of Appeal to appeal against Criminal Judgment No. 55. "C" dated October 19, 2023 of the Kampong Chhnang Provincial Court in accordance with the law.
