Philippines accuses Chinese coastguards of using water cannons on their boats near disputed South China Sea
The Philippines on Saturday accused the Chinese Coast Guard of using water cannons to disrupt three Manila government boats carrying food and supplies for Filipino fishermen. Near a Chinese-controlled reef in the South China Sea. This is according to a release by the AFP news agency.
In a statement, the Philippine Armed Forces in charge of Western Philippine Maritime Affairs said Chinese Coast Guard ships used water cannons to disrupt government boats carrying fuel and food to Philippine fishing boats. The incident took place near the Scarborough Shoal, a disputed area between Beijing and Manila.
(Koh Kong): The ecotourism community of Phny Meas commune, Kirisakor district, on December 9, 2023, held a community inauguration ceremony to promote tourism and reduce local poverty.
