Mr. Ly Vanna said that he made an effort to gather community members who participated in organizing water transport services, visiting natural canals and hosting national and international tourists.
The community has contributed to the establishment of a tourist port, a lobster repair shop, a toilet, and a car park, which is the result of the unity of the spirit, the physical strength, the mental strength and the budget until it comes into being. Fruitful to the operation of the ecotourism community in Phny Meas commune and continue to do more.
At present, the community does not have all the services to serve tourists at present, but in the future, he will continue to do his best to improve the tourism sector to contribute to reducing the poverty of the people and develop. In addition, for eco-tourism in Phieu Meas commune and for the local people to have a continuous job.
He said that in the community of 29 members, there are 19 boats for tourists to travel along the canal, and the beach is beautiful, there are tamarind trees along the canal for hundreds of kilometers.
Mr. Ly Vithavann, Deputy Director of the Koh Kong Provincial Department of Tourism, said that the Koh Kong Provincial Department of Tourism and he, who was invited to attend the event, were very pleased that the Phny Meas Ecotourism Community was established to promote tourism and Reduce the living standards of local poor families so that they can have jobs and income for their families.
He added that the inauguration ceremony of Phny Meas commune eco-tourism community in order to provide tourism services in the community area with quality standards and order in the management of each section.
Business owners have come together to form a tourism community with relationships between the private sector, tour operators, travel agencies, tour guides, tour operators, hotels, guesthouses, lodges, restaurants, restaurants, as well as community-based tourism resorts as a driving force for strengthening. Tourism and the national economic income to contribute to reducing poverty in the community.
Mr. Chea Bunthoeun, Deputy Governor of Kirisakor District, said that on behalf of the district authorities, I would like to support and encourage you, the committee, community associations and business owners. All the services that came to attend the inauguration of this office, he was very happy that you have united the spirit, materials and budget to contribute.
He said that the development of the community to become a tourist attraction, hospitality and shopping and accommodation supply, which is a need of national and international tourists.
