(Preah Vihear): A man was sent to the hospital on January 16 by Mr. Hor Bun Hour, Governor of Rovieng District, Preah Vihear Province, after he was injured by a gas stove fire for several days and could not go. Hospitalized.
Hor Bun Hour, Governor of Rovieng District, said on the evening of December 8, 2023 that the man who suffered from a gas stove fire was 18-year-old Moeun Sothearang, a resident of O Po Village, Romney Commune, Rovieng District, Preah Vihear Province. He said that the case of a man with a gas stove fire occurred on November 24, 2023, because the victim turned off the gas stove (gas canister) to cook and set himself on fire.
After the incident, the victim did not go to the hospital for treatment because the family was poor and treated at home. Due to the unresolved injuries, the neighbors reported this to Mr. Hor Bun Hour, the governor of Rieng district.
Immediately after receiving the information, the district governor led a team to inspect the house, handed over some money and sent him to be treated at the 16 Makara Hospital in Preah Vihear province for the medical expenses he would cover.
Ministry of Health warns again about prevention of seasonal flu and Kovid 19 (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Health has issued a proclamation on prevention of seasonal flu and communicable diseases. Kovid-19, in particular, calls on all citizens to remain vigilant against Kovid 19.
According to the Ministry of Health, there has recently been an increase in the incidence of Kovid-19 in some ASEAN countries. In addition, the infectious disease monitoring system of the Department of Infectious Diseases of the Ministry of Health has confirmed the frequent detection of Kovid-19 among patients who come to receive medical services at the hospital, as reported in the statement. Introduce reminders on the official reporting system of the Ministry of Health.
The following are measures to prevent the spread of influenza and Kovid-19:
Always apply contagious measures, such as wearing a mask in case of respiratory health problems and washing your hands frequently with soap or alcohol or hand gel.
Cover mouth and nose when coughing or sneezing with elbows, masks, scarves, towels or toilet paper and throw in a sealed bin.
If you have symptoms of fever, cough, headache, runny nose, difficulty breathing, please seek advice at a health center or hospital in a timely manner.
Call on people to continue to be vaccinated against Kovid-19 in all doses, both basic and booster doses, at hospitals or health centers to strengthen their respective immune systems appropriately to prevent Kovid-19 infection.
For more information, please contact the Ministry of Health's hotline number 115 for free. Prosecutor General Chea Leang Leads a Cambodian Delegation to the 13th ASEAN-China Attorney General Meeting in Vietnam
(Hanoi): Ms. Chea Leang, Prosecutor General of the Supreme Court Prosecutor General, led a Cambodian delegation to the 13th ASEAN-China Prosecutor General's Conference to be held from 5 to 8 December 2023 in Hanoi. Socialist Republic of Vietnam under the theme of strengthening cooperation in preventing and combating high-tech crime and transnational crime.
The ASEAN-China Attorney-General's Conference is a regional forum of attorneys-general, where the Attorney-General and the Chiefs of Delegation from ASEAN and China share experiences in counter-terrorism, financing, terrorism and drug trafficking. Addiction to illegal cross-border smuggling, corruption, technology crimes and organized crime.
Beginning on December 6, 2023, the Attorney General, Attorney General and Heads of Delegations from ASEAN and China (including Hong Kong and Macao Special Administrative Region) began to intervene and make key remarks. On the topic of technology crime and transnational crime, based on the legal basis, work experience and the challenges it has faced in cracking down on and preventing this type of crime in the past.
After concluding discussions, exchanging opinions and experiences in actively suppressing and preventing transnational technology and transnational crime, the 13th ASEAN-China Attorney General's Meeting unanimously signed a joint declaration. Content decided:
1. Committed to enhancing cooperation in the fight against transnational crime, including high-tech crime, based on the principles of equality, trust and mutual benefit in accordance with national and international law.
2. Make full use of all international cooperation channels, including legal mutual assistance in the field of crime, direct cooperation between the prosecution or the network of cooperation between prosecutors and prosecutors in accelerating prevention and Fight cybercrime and transnational crime.
3. Continue to commit and implement capacity building, experience sharing, including training sessions, workshops, roundtable discussions and expert exchanges.
4. Improving the quality and efficiency of the official website of the ASEAN-China Attorney General's Conference and regularly sharing legal documents and guidance on the functions and operations of the prosecutors of all countries, as well as sending prosecutors to study at the grassroots level. ASEAN-China Prosecutor Training, located in Nanning, Guangxi Province, China.
