Mr. Nuon Danhel called on the people living on both sides of the 14 roads to cooperate with the technical staff of the department in taking care not to be overweight, which will cause the road to collapse or damage, not to pour the village soil higher than the road that leads to flooding or Crossing the road leads to the road being blocked and not being used for a long time. Preah Vihear Provincial Governor Calls on Citizens to Promote and Prevent HIV Transmission
Appeal of the Governor of Preah Vihear Province on the occasion of attending the groundbreaking ceremony for the construction of an antiretroviral treatment facility for HIV / AIDS patients at Choam Ksan Referral Hospital in Choam Ksan Village, Choam Ksan Commune, Choam Ksan District, Preah Vihear Province this morning. December 08, 2023
Mr. Kim Rithy urged people, especially young people, to adopt peer education methods to stay away from drugs, sexual immorality, which is a high risk of HIV and other sexually transmitted diseases.
In case of suspected HIV infection, seek counseling and testing for HIV as soon as possible in order to receive health care and to take antiretroviral drugs regularly and consistently. In addition, participate in encouraging and not discriminating or stigmatizing people living with HIV and AIDS.
Dr. Kuong Lo, Director of Preah Vihear Provincial Health Department, said that the HIV / AIDS treatment building, which is currently 7 meters by 16 meters in size, is made of cypress cement, which will start construction on December 08, 2023. The construction will be completed on February 23, 2024 at a cost of $ 29,254 under the Global Fund through the National Center for AIDS, Dermatology and Sexually Transmitted Infections.
Ministry of Justice issues statement regarding the conviction of drug criminals in Kampong Chhnang province
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Justice on December 08, 2023 issued a press release in response to the criticism on social media in the case of the Kampong Chhnang Provincial Court's decision on the criminal group of victims who have been cracked down in the past. .
This statement was made by Ms. Chea Serey at the 10th Annual Macroeconomic Conference on Climate Risks and the Transition to a Green Economy on December 8, 2023, with the participation of Duke Kith Meng, President of the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce.
"Cambodia is a low-carbon country, but it is vulnerable to climate change, especially through agriculture," she said.
According to a World Bank report released in late October, Cambodia is being hit hardest by climate change as droughts and floods become more frequent and severe, with an estimated $ 100 million in rice losses. United States Due to the drought caused by El Nino in 2019, while facing this problem, the Royal Government of Cambodia has been actively involved in preventing and managing the consequences of climate change.
Ms. Chea Serey said that this issue could also contribute to increasing social inequality and putting vulnerable families and people below the poverty line. The floods of September 2022 affected 14 provinces and affected 45,000 families.
According to Chea Serey, in order to reduce global warming to below 2 degrees Celsius and ideally to 1.5 degrees Celsius, in line with the goals of the Paris Agreement 2018, the world needs to reduce greenhouse gas emissions. At least 45% by 2030 compared to 2019 and towards carbon neutrality by 2050, that is, eliminate carbon emissions or all carbon emissions into the atmosphere must be absorbed to zero.
Dr. Chea Serey is very pleased and honored to warmly welcome the signing ceremony of the Memorandum of Understanding between the United Nations Economic and Social Commission for Asia and the Pacific and the National Bank of Cambodia.
Dr. Chea Serey emphasized that in our recent collaboration between NBC and UNESCAP, the launch report was made to take stock of the current sustainable financial and market environment in Cambodia. Among the recommendations in the report, a national sustainable financial roadmap should be developed and the MoA is the start of this new initiative.
Through the MoA, we will develop a roadmap that integrates multilateral stakeholder integration, strategic approaches to accelerate the development of a sustainable financial system. The roadmap will include a clear plan for consolidating financial needs, resource gaps and options in line with national climate goals for sustainable development. It will also show future projects and investment pipelines that are eligible for financing.
Dr. Chea Serey is confident that with the cooperation and support of UNESCAP, we will be able to provide the right legal framework, support infrastructure, incentives and clear guidelines to ensure that the financial sector can play a better role as a financial intermediary. Effectively between private capital and sustainable activities in Cambodia.
In addition, Dr. Chea Serey is optimistic that the plans we are developing now are not limited to the banking and financial industries alone. It is designed to provide a framework that enables all stakeholders to actively participate and reap the benefits of their execution.
Taking this opportunity, Dr. Chea Serey would like to take this opportunity to request the cooperation and cooperation of various organizations such as ministries, institutions, regulators, public institutions, financial organizations, the private sector and development partners to jointly fight climate change.
Dr. Chea Serey would like to thank UNESCAP for your continued support of the National Bank of Cambodia, especially the technical assistance and capacity building of our staff. Dr. Chea Serey looks forward to the successful implementation of our MoA and to deepen our cooperation.
US Embassy in Iraq hit by rocket but no casualties
The spokesman said the attack was believed to have been carried out by Iranian allied militias in Iraq. However, no group immediately claimed responsibility.
An explosion was heard near the US embassy in the Iraqi capital at around 4 a.m. Friday.
This is the first rocket attack targeting the embassy since Iran's allied Shiite militia launched an offensive against US forces in Iraq and neighboring Syria in mid-October.
Armed groups operating under the banner of Islamic State militants in Iraq have linked more than 70 such attacks to Washington's support for Israel in its deadly offensive in Gaza.
"We reiterate our call on the Iraqi government, as we have repeatedly called on the United States to do everything in its power to protect its diplomatic staff and allies," an embassy spokesman said.
In addition to diplomats in Iraq, the United States has about 2,500 troops in the country to provide military advice and help local forces try to curb the recovery of Islamic State in 2014. Occupy large territories of both countries before being suppressed.
