Japanese Ambassador to Cambodia holds closing party to mark 70th anniversary of Japan-Cambodia friendship
(Phnom Penh): Cambodia and Japan first established official diplomatic relations in 1953, and 70 years later, in 2023, the two countries have upgraded their bilateral relations to the level of "comprehensive strategic partnership". The highest level of relations between the two countries in Asia.
In fact, on December 08, 2023, the Embassy of Japan in Cambodia organized a closing party to mark the 70th anniversary of Japan-Cambodia friendship with the participation of Deputy Prime Minister Sok Chenda Sophea, Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation. Members of the Supreme Personal Adviser to the King, the President of the Constitutional Council, as well as leaders, civil servants and many other distinguished guests at the residence of the Ambassador of Japan.
The 70th anniversary of Japan-Cambodia friendship was celebrated with more than 70 events in Cambodia. These events are held throughout the year and many people attend these events. Through such events, Cambodia and Japan can promote mutual understanding and, as a result, the relationship between the two countries is closer than ever.
Mr. Ou Natsu-Assushi stated that relations between Japan and Cambodia will definitely not end with the successful completion of the celebration of the 70th anniversary of the establishment of diplomatic relations. Cambodia and Japan need to build on this year's achievements and further develop bilateral relations over the next 10 years and beyond.
Deputy Prime Minister Sok Chenda Sophea said that the 70th anniversary of the establishment of diplomatic relations between Cambodia and Japan (1953 to 2023). This year 2023 is really special for both countries.
"We are not only celebrating the 70th anniversary, but we are also enhancing our relationship from a strategic partnership to a strategic management partnership," said the Cambodian Foreign Minister. "Our two countries have been cooperating closely to organize many projects in Cambodia and Japan throughout the year, such as this anniversary."
