(Phnom Penh): Dr. Eang Sophalleth, Minister of Environment, led a Cambodian delegation to the 28th United Nations Conference on Climate Change (COP28) in Dubai, United Arab Emirates on the afternoon of December 8, 2023.
Dr. Eang Sophalleth is scheduled to speak on behalf of the Prime Minister of Cambodia, Hun Manet, at the Conference (COP28) from Cambodia, which is committed to playing a key role in international efforts to address climate change.
The Minister will address leaders from around the world urging COP28 to embark on an unprecedented global partnership for climate resilience, ensuring the well-being of our communities and the health of our planet.
"Even though Cambodia is a low emitter, we are aware of our vulnerability to the negative effects of climate change." This was added by Dr. Eang Sophalleth on the occasion before attending the meeting.
