(Phnom Penh): In the first nine months of 2023, the Royal Government signed a new concessional loan agreement with development partners totaling $ 1 billion. This is according to the Cambodian Public Debt Statistics Bulletin issued by the Ministry of Economy and Finance.
According to the Ministry of Economy, "From the first quarter to the third quarter of 2023, the Royal Government has signed new concessional loan agreements with development partners totaling $ 1 billion, equivalent to 762.52 million SDR. "About 45% of the ceilings allowed by law (1,700 million SDR), of which about 45% are bilateral and 55% are multilateral."
According to the Ministry of Economy, compared to the same period last year, the total number of new concessional loan agreements from the first quarter to the third quarter of 2023 decreased by about 17%. Overall, these loans are all highly concessional, with an average of 43% of gift items.
The Ministry of Economy and Finance has stated that the purpose of these new credit agreements is to meet the financing needs of the Royal Government's priority areas in order to contribute to sustaining long-term growth and increasing economic productivity or productivity.
According to the Ministry of Economy and Finance, compared to the same period last year, total debt repayments from the first quarter to the third quarter of 2023 increased by about 8%.
