Please be informed that the former Deacon of Siam Silcha Charnavisoth, a Buddhist devotee of the birth mother of General Nop Ratana, passed away on December 7, 2023 at 3:33 AM at the age of 90. National Bank of Cambodia Holds 10th Annual Macroeconomic Conference
(Phnom Penh): On December 8, 2023, the National Bank of Cambodia organized the 10th Annual Macroeconomic Conference on "Climate Risks and the Transition to a Green Economy" to contribute to research on key development inputs. National economy.
She said that in 2023, the National Bank of Cambodia has selected topics related to climate change and the process towards Cambodia's green economy, the decision to set this topic because the national, regional and international community has been focusing. Pay more attention and urge all stakeholders to integrate this issue into the implementation of their policies and activities.
In particular, Cambodia has also played a more active role in contributing to climate change mitigation and is committed to setting policies towards a green economy. Currently, global temperatures have risen by about 1.2 degrees Celsius since before the Industrial Revolution (1850-1900), and could reach 2.7 degrees by 2100 without further effort.
It should be noted that in general, the effects of climate change affect the livelihoods of people in agriculture directly and indirectly.
"Food represents more than 43% of the baskets of goods and services that households in Cambodia use on a regular basis, so the impact of climate change on agriculture could lead to food insecurity and rising prices that affect livelihoods," she said. Living of the people as a whole. This could also contribute to increasing social inequality and putting vulnerable families and people below the poverty line.
She added that at the same time, the National Bank of Cambodia has been actively involved in the preparation process and initiatives of sustainable financial promotion, including: 1: Supporting the establishment of sustainable financial policies of the Association. Banks in Cambodia for all banking and financial institutions to participate.
2. Establish a framework for cooperation between the National Bank of Cambodia, the Ministry of Environment and the Banking Association of Cambodia to share information and develop initiatives for climate change mitigation activities. Sustainability and hedging from climate change for banking and financial institutions and stakeholders.
In addition, the National Bank of Cambodia also participates in the international framework through initiatives and discussions with institutions such as the Central Bank Network and the Supervision Authority for the Green Financial System, the Green Financial Environment Working Group, the Partnership for Economic Activities. UN Green and ASEAN Working Group on Sustainable Banking and Finance Networking
The National Bank of Cambodia has also partnered with organizations such as UNESCAP, the Alliance for Financial Environment (AFI), the International Finance Corporation (IFC) to strengthen green financing participation, and partially invested in international reserves on bonds. Green will become a member of the Advisory Committee for the Green Fund for Southeast Asia in 2022.
As a follow-up, the National Bank of Cambodia will implement more important initiatives aimed at establishing the necessary support mechanisms and ecosystems to promote sustainable financing and essential action to mitigate climate change risks. Those tasks include:
1. Creating a sustainable financial guide map. 2. Creating a cyclical system for sustainable finance. 3. Establish a sustainable financial reporting mechanism for transparency and accountability. 4. Build capacity and knowledge of the banking and financial sector and stakeholders. Climate change of banking and financial institutions.
