As of the beginning of December 2023, the Royal Library of Luang Prabang has distributed 80,240 copies of the book "Historical Witnesses on the Royal Journey to the Liberation Front of the Cambodian National United Front" to the public.
In early 2024, the "Royal Luang Prabang Library" will continue to distribute this book at the request of the public, especially Cambodians living in remote rural areas.
The book "Historical Witnesses on the Journey to the Liberation Front of the Cambodian National United Front" is the original text of Queen Norodom Monineath Sihanouk, the Queen Mother of Cambodia, in French and has been translated into English without modification. Reflected on the royal knowledge, opinions and views of Luong Mey himself.
The book "Historical Witnesses on the Royal Journey to the Liberation Front of the Cambodian National United Front" describes the Royal Journey of King Norodom Sihanouk to the Liberation Front of the Cambodian National United Front in 1973, departing from Beijing to Hanoi. And continue along the Ho Chi Minh Trail and parts of Laos to Cambodia.
During the 39 days of the royal journey, Luong Mae wrote a diary every day and showed his gentleness and dignity, despite the dangerous and tumultuous situation.
