(Siem Reap): Samdech Kittisongkhab Dr. Men Sam An, Personal Adviser to the King and Lok Chumteav Dr. Pech Chanmony Hun Manet, held a prayer service on the morning of December 7, 2023 and counted 131 monks. Multiply Angkor in the third year.
Also present at the ceremony were Ms. Pheung Sakona, Minister of Culture and Fine Arts and Chairman of the Board of APSARA Authority, Governor of Siem Reap, monks, leaders, civil servants and hundreds of staff of APSARA Authority.
Ms. Phoeung Sakona said that the Angkor Commemoration Event was held for two main purposes: to celebrate the 31st anniversary of the inscription of Angkor on the World Heritage List on December 14, 1992, as well as to commemorate To the ancestors of all the previous kings who built the temples, leaving a lot of heritage, art and culture to serve the social and economic benefits of this generation and the future.
The ceremony is also dedicated to Cambodian ancestors, Cambodian dignitaries of all generations, national and international experts who have sacrificed their physical and mental strength for life to protect and preserve our national cultural heritage.
On that occasion, Lok Chumteav Pech Chanmony Hun Manet also highlighted the merits of the ancient ancestors who built temples, built history, etc. in accordance with the Khmer slogan that always says to drink water to remember the source.
She added that this event commemorates Angkor is an expression of national pride, civilization, culture and the long history of an ancient Khmer nation.
