Former Minority Police and More Than 100 New Police Officers Gather to Celebrate 28th Anniversary
(Phnom Penh): The leaders of former low-level criminal police officers and more than 100 new police friends who served from 1995-2023 on December 7, 2023 gathered to celebrate the 28th anniversary to commemorate and Strengthen the relationship between former and current officials.
The rally was also attended by Lt. Gen. Song Ly, Deputy National Police Commissioner, Lt. Gen. Young Sing Mao, Deputy Director of the Economic Crimes Department, and Mr. Ream Sarin, as well as former criminal police officers and other police officers.
Col. Duch Duong Serey Makara stated that the purpose of organizing this event was to commemorate and strengthen the bonds of solidarity in the Phnom Penh Municipal Police Commission's Office of Minor Criminal Police between the younger generation and the older generation, some of whom entered. Some retirees move to work in different units and get along with each other and support as much as possible to those who face various difficulties.
Colonel Duch Duong Serey Makara said that the event was organized for the former and new police officers, who had been separated for more than 28 years, to meet together with memories and happiness.
On that occasion, on behalf of the low-level criminal police officers who served from 1995-2023, Colonel Duch Duong Serey Makara also expressed his deep gratitude for the ceremony that provided some financial support to the joint police officers. A number of retired professions are also set aside for various needs.
(Phnom Penh): At the handing over of vocational certificates to young people at the Vocational and Vocational Training Center of Mith Samlanh on December 7, Mr. Heng Sour, Minister of Labor and Vocational Training, praised and mentioned that the 105 young trainees The successful graduate will now become a family hero through technical and professional skills.
The Minister pointed out that the choice of vocational and technical education of all young people is the right choice that makes all young trainees have specific skills in life and have their own income, family life and personal life, because the skills soon Work using short-term.
Minister: "Uncle, I would like to commend you for going through a lot of hardships and hardships, but overcoming to study for a career and having more work is a source of pride for your family, society and your own, and I believe that "You are the heroes of the family through skill and decent work."
Please note that Mith Samlanh Organization has trained on 8 majors such as haircut, cosmetics, maintenance and repair of electrical equipment, motorcycle repair, installation of steel frame, Khmer cooking, shopping services.
Please be informed that the inauguration ceremony and the groundbreaking ceremony were attended by Mr. Oueno Atusaki, Ambassador of Japan to Cambodia, Mr. Sanu Ika Sumasa, President of the Japan International Cooperation Agency in Cambodia, Mr. Vy Samnang, Governor of Kampong Speu .
Minister Tho Chetha expressed his deep gratitude to the Royal Government of Japan for its support and continued assistance to Cambodia to develop in all areas, especially the development of water resources.
The Minister also thanked the Ministry of Economy and Finance, relevant institutions, local authorities and all citizens who actively participated in making the implementation of the project as planned.
The Minister said that the Royal Government of Cambodia has focused on giving high priority to the water resources sector in response to the current trends of global warming and climate change, which has made the water problem worse. Serious and clearly indicating the water crisis that may occur in the near future.
The Minister stated that the rehabilitation and rehabilitation of irrigation and drainage systems, the establishment and strengthening of water user farmers' communities and the provision of agricultural extension services to farmers in the project area have increased the amount of rice production and people's income. Farmers are increasing year by year and their livelihoods are improving, in line with the National Poverty Reduction Policy and the first phase of the Pentagon Strategy.
The Minister said that since 1993, Japan, through the Embassy of Japan in Cambodia and JICA, has supported the management and development of water resources and meteorology, focusing on the construction of water works to ensure water supply. Adequate and timely irrigation for farmers' production work and capacity building of officials of the Ministry of Water Resources and Meteorology at both national and sub-national levels.
On that occasion, the Minister requested the local authorities as well as farmers living in the project area to continue to work closely with the Department of Water Resources and Meteorology to manage and maintain the irrigation system built effectively and efficiently. Sustainable to ensure adequate water supply for all types of agricultural crops.
Please be informed that the project of rehabilitation and rehabilitation of irrigation system and drainage system west of Tonle Sap in Kampong Chhnang, Pursat and Battambang provinces started on March 28, 2016 and was completed on the 31st. By December 2020, it will be able to supply irrigation water to a total of 13,393 hectares of farmland.
Separately, the project of rehabilitation and rehabilitation of irrigation and drainage system southwest of Phnom Penh in Kampong Speu, Kandal and Takeo provinces began construction on June 13, 2023 and is scheduled to be completed on June 26, 2026. This will supply irrigation water to a total of 23,831 hectares of farmland, benefiting 7,925 families, equivalent to 44,157 people, and increase rice yields from 2.20 tons to 3.80 tons / hectare.
