In front of the former Foreign Minister of Singapore, Samdech Techo also described some plans related to state management to the successor. Samdech Techo confirmed that this arrangement is an arrangement for a long time.
Regarding economic issues, Samdech Techo said that there are two issues that Cambodia is continuing to pay attention to: first, food security and second, energy security. In terms of food security, Cambodia has become a country that produces its own food for consumption and a country that has some food left for export.
Regarding energy security, although Cambodia is not an oil-producing country, Cambodia can control it. So far, Cambodia has used about 62% of renewable energy, and Cambodia has stopped producing coal-fired power.
