Director of Takeo Provincial Department of Agriculture asks farmers to cooperate with agricultural extension officers to get new technologies
(Takeo): Mr. Nhim Sron, Director of Takeo Provincial Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, requested farmers to cooperate with agricultural extension officers to acquire new technologies as well as private companies' participation in agricultural development to help Farmers make a profit.
The proposal was made on the occasion that the Takeo Provincial Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, in collaboration with Kbal Krabey Fertilizer and Yitak Group, organized a smart rice show in line with climate change in Cambodia, demonstrating the use of tractors. A bunch of rows on a farmer named Mak in Rovieng village, Thlok commune, Traing district, Takeo province.
The Director of Takeo Provincial Department of Agriculture expressed his support for the participation of the private sector, especially Kbal Krabey Fertilizer Company, which cooperated with the Provincial Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries to conduct experimental rice farming demonstrations of smart farming methods for profit and exploration. Economic efficiency.
He added that this is in line with the policy of the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries to reduce production costs to a low level and achieve high yields for the main purpose of improving the agricultural sector and improving quality yields. Including profits.
Mr. Nhim Sron said that the problem is that farmers continue to farm according to the practice of using too many seeds, using impure seeds, using the wrong fertilizers, and the cost of production.
He also said that the provincial Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries has collaborated with private companies and farmers with large farmland to show local farmers how to understand smart farming. High production costs and high yields.
Mr. Chao Rathoun, Representative of Kbal Krabey Fertilizer Company, confirmed that the company has cooperated with Prey Veng Provincial Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries to organize 3 demonstration plots in 3 districts in Prey Veng province and recently Continue to show rice in 3 more places in 3 districts, including: Traing district, Kirivong district and Borey Chulsar district in Takeo province.
The company representative stated that this smart demonstration farming aims to show the farmers who are engaged in farming to compare the economic efficiency of using the cultivator in rows.
He said that the use of tillers in rows uses 80 kg of seeds per hectare, compared to the traditional sowing of farmers generally spend 300 to 400 kg per hectare. Another related to the use of fertilizers is to make the rice get a better yield than the traditional fertilizer application by using a machine to make the rice get enough fertilizer.
He added that the use of tractors to plant in rows saves both time and labor, with one hectare of rice taking only one hour and more labor than sowing rice by hand, which requires a lot of labor and takes a long time. Therefore, using a sowing machine in rows saves time, effort and higher yields than manual sowing.
