Cambodia officially launches sub-national roadmap on blindness management and prevention to reduce blindness to 0.35% by 2030
(Phnom Penh): On December 7, 2023, Cambodia officially launched the road map for sub-national level on blind management and prevention 2021-2030 to reduce blindness to 0. .35% in 2030. The ceremony was presided over by Professor Chheang Ra, Minister of Health.
"This roadmap is a continuation of the need to continue to increase the quality, expand the scope of eye health services throughout Cambodia to bring people closer to the grassroots to reduce blindness," he added. 0.35% in 2030 as stated in the National Strategic Plan on the Management and Prevention of Blindness 2021-2030 of the Ministry of Health.
On that occasion, the Minister also praised and congratulated the National Eye Health Program for the achievements that Cambodia has achieved, both in providing eye health services to people in the community and the success of reducing blindness on stage. International. He also thanked all health officials, ministries, relevant authorities at all levels for their efforts to provide health care, eye care to the people.
At the same time, the Minister gave recommendations on the management and prevention of blindness, including:
Continue the mechanism and implementation of existing activities and roadmaps for the sub-national level on the management and prevention of blindness, which are officially launched today, ensuring that it responds to the needs of the people in the community.
* Promote community involvement in the prevention of blindness and vision impairment that can be avoided, especially among the most vulnerable populations such as premature babies, schoolchildren, women, the disabled, people over the age of 50 Years and all age groups with impaired vision.
* Modernize and expand the visual field with digital innovation and quality.
* Promote the implementation of quality improvement projects, expand the scope of eye health services closer to the community, especially the establishment and strengthening of vision centers, the integration of primary eye care at health centers and health posts.
* Health officials at all levels should adhere to the code of ethics in providing services to local people.
* Strengthen cooperation with existing partners and expand with new partners.
Before concluding, the Minister encouraged all civil servants and health workers to know how to help each other, cooperate, unite and make more efforts to develop hospitals, eye health centers, eye care centers in the health sector. Better to achieve global health coverage.
