Deputy Prime Minister and President of the National Anti-Drug Authority affirmed that raising awareness of the effects of drugs and the tricks of criminals requires the reform of some ineffective education outreach mechanisms by using new mechanisms. How to make the general public more interested, especially among young people who are vulnerable.
Deputy Prime Minister Neth Savoeun said, "I see the first priority of our education outreach, this time the first educational outreach is very important for our people to understand, so please cooperate." "This word is to reform education, to make education quality General Secretariat, Department of Skills, to study the plan, content, methods and methods, and to find something new, find something popular, easy for people to follow."
Deputy Prime Minister Neth Savoeun added that outreach should seek out influential people of public interest to speak to them about the effects of drugs such as singers, actors, monks, writers and poets. And songs. He assigned this task to Senior Minister Prum Sokha to work well with the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports, the Ministry of Culture and Fine Arts, the Artists and Writers Association.
He also believes that when the authorities go to read speeches to explain or summon people for education, the effectiveness is still limited, that is, can take a show or a concert with a famous song list or comedy list can take time. A little more to spread the message about the effects of drug use to the masses is more effective. In addition, also cooperate with the media in the country.
In addition to education, law enforcement is also considered by Deputy Prime Minister Neth Savoeun as an important task to monitor the performance of all units and to summarize and compile the tricks of the perpetrators, tricks. Production processing, smuggling, transit trafficking, newly developed trading tricks to facilitate the competent authorities to monitor, prevent and prevent crackdowns.
At the same time, Deputy Prime Minister Neth Savoeun urged to increase bilateral, regional and international cooperation to seek assistance on skills training and exchange of experiences to increase the capacity of law enforcement officers.
For treatment and rehabilitation, the capacity for drug rehabilitation sites must be clearly defined in collaboration with the Ministry of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation, and the private sector should be given the opportunity to participate. Also, determine the number of people in care and those who leave the center to facilitate follow-up.
The President of the National Authority for Combating Drugs also recommended further strengthening the management of chemicals to control the import, use and distribution, but make sure there is a clear mechanism to avoid disturbing the relevant ministries. Allow the import of chemicals.
