(Phnom Penh): Dr. Hiv Sovann, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Economy and Finance, Dr. Chhim Sareth, Royal Government Delegate in charge of the Director General of the General Department of Public Procurement, on December 7, 2023, presided over a seminar on Dissemination of the Law on Public procurement and legal documents related to three new public procurement.
The event was also attended by representatives of ministries, institutions, public enterprises, public institutions, administrative, capital, province, municipality, district, Khan, capital-provincial departments, representatives of units under the Ministry of Economy and Finance.
In addition, there is a need to strengthen and improve the mechanism for receiving and resolving procurement complaints independently, establishing a sanction regime and harmonizing the rules, regulations and procedures of public procurement in accordance with According to the basic principles of international procurement and excellence to increase competition with transparency and efficiency.
In this direction, the Royal Government has assigned the Ministry of Economy and Finance to prepare, improve and supplement the Public Procurement Law 2012. As a result, the Law on Public Procurement was signed into law by His Majesty the King by Royal Kram No. NS / RKAM / 0523/005 dated 16 May 2023.
The new Public Procurement Law sets out a number of key contents and principles, including:
The direction of the public procurement reform, in which the Ministry of Economy and Finance acts as a regulator, with the General Department of Public Procurement acting as a staff, and highlights some of the key roles of the regulator.
* Providing favorable treatment for the implementation of each procurement method in order to encourage local bidders, especially small and medium enterprises to participate in public procurement.
* The implementation of sustainable procurement is to contribute to the Royal Government's sustainable development policy, which must promote the use of resources, minimize pollution, the impact of human activities on the environment and the use of energy. More efficient
Expanding the scope of electronic procurement (e-GP) in line with the evolving trends of digitalization * Strengthening mechanisms for receiving and resolving procurement complaints.
Dr. Hiv Sovann emphasized that although the new Public Procurement Law has been signed by the King, all legal documents related to the implementation of the Public Procurement Law 2012 and related to public procurement Which is still in force and will remain in force until a new legal standard is replaced in accordance with the provisions of the new Public Procurement Law.
In addition to the preparation of the new Public Procurement Law, which was signed by the King, the Ministry of Economy and Finance has been revising and revising the legal documents related to public procurement, including Three prakas were approved and disseminated by the Ministry of Economy and Finance today, including:
Proclamation No. 831 MEF.PrK Alsa dated 10 November 2023 on the Examination and Approval of Procurement Plan of Capital, Provincial and Municipal Departments and Municipalities
Proclamation No. 832 MEF.PrK Alsa dated 10 November 2023 on Increasing the Amount of Decision-Making in Public Procurement and
Proclamation No. 833 MEF.PrK.Lsa dated 10 November 2023 on Determining the Amount of Procurement Method.
