Samdech Prime Minister Hun Manet issues a decision to establish an inter-ministerial working group to lead the preparation of the National Report on Human Rights in Cambodia to the United Nations (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): Lead the preparation of the National Report on Human Rights in Cambodia to the United Nations (UN).
According to the decision received by Fresh News on December 7, 2023, the inter-ministerial working group is headed by Senior Minister Keo Remy, Chairman of the Cambodian Human Rights Committee, accompanied by 41 Vice-Chairmen and members. Figure.
The above inter-ministerial working group has the following tasks:
* Review and comment to the Royal Government on draft UN reports, such as the report of the Office of the United Nations High Commissioner for Human Rights in Cambodia, the report of the Special Representative of the Secretary-General of the United Nations, and your report. Other representatives of the UN treaty entities submitted to the Royal Government
Perform other duties related to human rights issues as assigned by the Head of the Royal Government.
The following is the decision of Samdech Hun Sen: The Minister of Environment encourages and encourages people to plant palm trees, which are the national representatives of Cambodia.
(Phnom Penh): Dr. Eang Sophalleth, Minister of Environment, encourages Cambodians to plant the national tree, the palm tree, by distributing more than 300,000 palm seedlings per year for free, in addition to planting October 10, 2023 Campaign of the Ministry of Environment on the distribution of more than 1 million seedlings every year to the people of Cambodia to plant and restore more than 60% of the forest by 2050.
The Minister made his remarks at the closing ceremony of the workshop on "Labor Inspection 2023 and Strategic Action Plan for the Management of Protected Areas 2024-2028" on December 6, 2023 at the Ministry.
The encouragement of the people to plant the national plant is done in order to promote the value of the Khmer national culture associated with the Khmer plant to show national and international tourists about the valuable heritage from the past and modernization in planting. The national thing is brown to benefit all Cambodians.
Brown has many benefits for the daily lives of Cambodians. Palm sugar from palm juice squeezed from palm flowers is a type of food that provides energy to help health. Palm leaves can be used for roofing, palm trees for boats and houses, etc. In addition, there are many materials made from the plant is brown.
The Minister emphasized that the arrangement of palm planting sites must be creative to make it easier to harvest, that is, we plant in rows with a spacing of 4 meters, one tree can be transferred to harvest from other trees. Is able to help people earn better income. In addition, the aesthetics of planting help to attract foreign tourists, help people's livelihoods linked to national cultural traditions.
