(Phnom Penh): In the context of leaking information about the discovery of a lot of frozen meat imported illegally, Mr. Hong So Hour, the Royal Government delegate in charge of the Director General of the Stock Exchange of Cambodia, urged business owners to follow the principle "Business right."
According to the Trinity, the right to a business, which means to make a living or to make a good living, refers to businesses that deviate from the five occupations: arms trafficking, human trafficking, animal trafficking, drug trafficking, alcohol trafficking. .
But because this type of business has often evolved since the time of the Buddha, we can define business right: living without hurting others, wanting to maximize profits, and not worrying about pain. Catching or endangering the health or well-being of others.
"Although we can not stop eating meat completely, we can reduce it and improve our health," he added. "Of course, we can not completely ban alcohol, but we can push it to a level that does not harm the health and harm others."
Applying these principles can reduce some of the profits or increase some of the costs, but can be transformed into a brand that can easily attract loyal customers to ensure long-term business growth.
