At the same time, the Secretary of State stressed the importance of the Minister's contribution to the current lecture, which is a noble activity to help promote and strengthen the fifth generation leadership and innovation training process. High quality, effective and beneficial to the motherland under the wise leadership of Samdech Moha Bovathibodi Hun Manet, Prime Minister of Cambodia.
In addition, the Minister informed more about building digital citizens in human resource development through scholarship programs, setting up community technology centers, digital skills development programs, promoting digital capture, creating programs related to digital skills, creating digital nurseries. Various.
The Minister also informed about the digital revolution in ministries and institutions, the establishment of digital revolution units, the organization of the Royal Government and sub-national networks, equipment and systems, the organization of data centers, the development of digital development planning in each ministry and Action planning;
At the same time, senior trainees of the Royal School of Administration paid a study visit to the Telecommunications and Post Regulators of Cambodia related to the process of providing public services to the people.
(Phnom Penh): Honorary Legal Doctor, Senior Minister Om Yentieng, Head of the Anti-Corruption Unit, said that since the day Cambodia became a member of the United Nations Convention against Corruption (UNCAC) ACU, Cambodia has participated in overseeing the implementation of anti-corruption work. Corruption in five countries: Marta, Palau, Saudi Arabia, Kiribati, while currently monitoring the anti-corruption process in Lebanon.
This statement was made by Senior Minister Om Yentieng on the occasion that he and the leaders of the Anti-Corruption Unit held a joint press conference to highlight the achievements of the ACU and to celebrate the International Day and the 9th National Anti-Corruption Day. In the afternoon of December 5, 2023 yesterday.
According to Senior Minister Om Yentieng, Cambodia became a member of the United Nations Convention against Corruption (UNCAC) in 2007, four years after the establishment of the Convention. Open the door for the United Nations to review the implementation of anti-corruption work on a regular basis.
Senior Minister Om Yentieng said that this participation on behalf of the United Nations Convention on the Rights of Persons and Associations of Cambodia is constitutional, criminal and other laws, all of which are consistent. In addition, Cambodia has institutions to work on the fight against corruption.
The ACU President affirmed that in the fight against corruption, Cambodia is not alone, but Cambodia is working with other countries in the world.
In addition, Senior Minister Om Yentieng said that December 9, 2023 will be the 20th anniversary of the United Nations Convention against Corruption (UNCAC), which will be held under the theme "Global Unity. "Let's fight corruption for the development of peace and security."
According to Mr. Seng Kheang, Deputy Director of the Anti-Corruption Unit and an expert on the United Nations, he visited the implementation of the United Nations (UNCAC) and said that through the implementation of the UNCAC, Cambodia has achieved great success. Comprehensive in the implementation of all chapters of the United Nations Convention (UNCAC) that Cambodia has fulfilled its obligations to answer questions and reports submitted to the United Nations.
It should be noted that the International Day Against Corruption 9 December came after the United Nations General Assembly (UN) adopted this convention in 2003, with the participation of UN member countries, including Cambodia. The convention covers a total of 189 countries by 2021.
