Articles and pictures by Cambodia-China Friendship Radio Analysis: What is lacking in global climate governance is not just a verbal promise, but also a practical one.
Passing through these data, it is easy for you to understand why China's contribution can get the attention of the parties at the 28th General Assembly of the Parties to the Framework Convention. The United Nations Framework Convention on Climate Change (COP28) is underway in Dubai, United Arab Emirates.
Nowadays, everyone on the planet may have a personal impression that extreme weather events are so frequent that climate change has become a real crisis. The World Meteorological Organization (WMO) has released a report on the opening day of the COP28 General Assembly, declaring 2023 the hottest year in human history on record.
In the face of tough tests, the COP28 General Assembly is expected to hold its first global consolidation through the implementation of the "Paris Agreement" to bridge the gap as well as urge all to take action. More efficient in terms of reducing fossil fuels and greenhouse gas emissions, and working to keep temperatures within 1.5 degrees Celsius.
