Senior officials of the Ministry of Commerce urge stakeholders to promote Cambodia's cashew potential to serve local, regional and global markets
(Kampong Thom): Mr. Kem Sithon, Permanent Secretary of State of the Ministry of Commerce, on December 6, 2023, urged stakeholders to promote the potential of Cambodia's cashew to serve local, regional and global markets.
Such a promotion was made at the Cashew Forum under the theme "Together to Promote the Potential of Cambodian Cashew" in Kampong Thom on December 6, 2023.
The event was attended by leaders of the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, the Ministry of Industry, Science, Technology and Innovation, the Ambassador of the European Union to Cambodia, as well as leaders, government officials and many citizens.
He added that the Cashew Forum is an important forum that brings together all stakeholders in the cashew sector and provides opportunities for the private sector to participate in the display of cashew products, processing equipment and business matching, and discussions to share experiences on issues. Challenges and successes, etc. These are direct contributions to enhancing the reputation and potential of Cambodian cashews.
He added that with a focus on cultivation, processing and export, and a vision to develop cashew production and market environmentally competitive, ensuring sustainability, economic diversification and aiming to transform Cambodia into As a producer as well as a supplier of cashew products to serve the local, regional and global markets.
At the same time, Mr. Kem Sithon shared some views as follows:
1: Request for cooperation and continued support from relevant development partners, especially the EU and Gl2, as well as the private sector involved in continuing to organize such forums on a regular basis every year to participate in the implementation of action plans set out in In the National Policy on Cashew 2022-2027.
2. Encourage the Cambodian Cashew Federation The Cambodian Cashew Association strengthens its role and further cooperation to jointly develop the Cambodian cashew sector.
4: Request the Cambodian Cashew Federation, the Cambodian Cashew Association and the relevant private sector to continue to support and organize such programs on a regular basis, as well as to participate in more business meetings to connect the network between the members of the Federation and the Association and build friendship. Partner with local, regional and international entrepreneurs strategically and in depth.
5. Request the stakeholders in the cashew production chain to continue to cooperate closely with the ministries / institutions / and sub-national administrations to jointly address concerns and challenges in the cashew sector.
6. The Ministry of Commerce will continue to work closely with relevant ministries, institutions, sub-national administrations, the private sector and development partners to promote the implementation of the national policy on cashews in accordance with the action plan.
Meanwhile, Mr. Nguon Rattanak, Governor of Kampong Thom Province, said that Kampong Thom Province has more than 145,000 hectares of agro-industrial crops such as cashews, 53,000 hectares of cassava, 9,000 hectares of mango, turmeric, 141 hectares of pepper and 75 hectares of tamarind. .
