(Preah Sihanouk): The Royal Government delegation in charge of the Director of Fisheries Administration of the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, Mr. Pum Sotha and Mr. Kouch Chamroeun, Governor of Preah Sihanouk Province met to understand the difficulties and challenges of fishermen in the sea in the afternoon. December 05, 2023.
During the meeting, the provincial governor and the director of the Fisheries Administration allowed the fishermen to describe some difficulties and problems to check and solve the proposed fishermen based on the principles and all legal forms.
After tackling the problem, the director of the Fisheries Administration said that currently both freshwater and saltwater fish species are becoming increasingly scarce, so the Royal Government as well as the Ministry of Agriculture have taken measures to crack down on illegal fishing for fisheries. Recurrence.
After the crackdown on fishery products, some of which are now endangered, have been revived after major fishing offenses were prevented, he said. In the daily business, which makes the fishery worse from day to day.
With the attention of the Ministry of Agriculture and new rules that will be issued in the near future so that fishermen have a better understanding of what gear is allowed, which is not allowed to be used in the fishing area. Allow any location that does not allow conservation and encourage fishermen to register their boats.
At the same time, Mr. Kouch Chamroeun said that from now on, if there are competent officials to extort money from fishermen, please contact him personally and will take measures to find justice for people who face problems on the border. The sea. He continued that the people are the eyes and noses of the authorities, so if there is any crime, please report to the authorities to take measures to solve in time.
The provincial governor emphasized that in Kampong Som Bay, fishing with large trawlers is not allowed for people who have small boats to do business or leave this place. As a fishing destination, tourists are encouraged to go fishing outside the bay. Regarding legal issues, the provincial governor also said that there must be measures for professional officers to participate in solving people's problems, not to oppress the people.
