Phnom Penh Capital Administration announces the temporary avoidance of all types of vehicles in the Extraordinary General Assembly of the Cambodian People's Party
(Phnom Penh): The Phnom Penh Capital Administration would like to inform all the people in Phnom Penh that on December 9th and 10th, 2023 at 07:00, the Central Committee of the Cambodian People's Party will organize Extraordinary General Assembly of the Cambodian People's Party at the 7 Makara Palace in Sangkat Tonle Bassac, Khan Chamkar Mon, Phnom Penh, chaired by Samdech Techo Hun Sen, President of the Cambodian People's Party.
In order for the above program to run smoothly, to maintain security, safety, order and public order, as well as to avoid traffic jams, the Phnom Penh Capital Administration will avoid traffic for all types of vehicles on Norodom Boulevard (from the traffic light to the bridge). Aerial at the head of the road and the area around the venue) on December 9 and 10, 2023 from 05:00 in the morning until the end of each day.
Therefore, all citizens are kindly requested to understand, tolerate and avoid traveling through the above road sections on the dates as kindly informed. After the temporary ban, the Phnom Penh Capital Administration will reopen to normal traffic.
Receiving this announcement, Phnom Penh Municipal Police, Phnom Penh Gendarmerie Command, Khan Chamkar Mon Administration, Department of Public Works and Transport of Phnom Penh and relevant authorities at all levels must disseminate widely and assign high efficiency.
