(Kampong Chhnang): A young woman has had a breast ulcer for 14 years and is being treated for cancer because of her worsening condition and living in a poor family without access to treatment. Due to her poor family, she could not afford to pay for medical treatment.
Due to the poor living conditions of her family, she and her family requested the leaders and the Minister of Health to help pay for the treatment at the Khmer-Soviet Friendship Hospital in order to be treated and to continue their studies.
Chea Thida, a 20-year-old former 12th grade student, is the youngest of 12 siblings living in Andong Chrey village, Andong Snay commune, Rolea Bier district, Kampong Chhnang province. Years ago.
In connection with the above request, with the guidance of Mr. Sun Sovannarith, Governor of Kampong Chhnang Province, on the afternoon of December 4, 2023, a group of party youth activists took her to Kampong Chhnang Provincial Referral Hospital to request a team of technicians. Cancer lesions help diagnose and assess her condition.
On the afternoon of December 5, 2023, Dr. Yeap Kong, a cancer specialist, examined her wounds and performed an ultrasound examination, and confirmed that the condition of the patient's chest ulcers was generally in good condition. . The doctor also advised her to continue to treat this ulcer at the Khmer-Soviet Hospital, which specializes in oncology, to see Dr. Ear Phearum at the C surgery building, where he has a specific specialty to examine and treat this ulcer.
After receiving the advice of the above professional doctors, Ms. Chea Thida and her family respectfully requested the Minister of Health and His Excellency Lok Chumteav, the leaders, to support the medical expenses at the Khmer-Soviet Friendship Hospital for her. Thanks to give her the opportunity to continue her education for the future of her and her family.
In relation to this case, Mr. Sun Sovannarith, Governor of Kampong Chhnang Province, this morning, December 6, 2023, he donated 1 million Riels to Ms. Chea Thida to cover her travel expenses and stay in the public hospital in Phnom Penh, if there is a shortage, you will continue to support more.
