(Phnom Penh): In a congratulatory message on the National and International Day Against Corruption on December 9, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, His Excellency Hun Manet, presented the five priorities of the Royal Government of the seventh mandate in promoting governance reform. With a focus on promoting and strengthening cleanliness in public administration.
Samdech stated that since the Triangle-Rectangular Strategy and now is the first phase of the Pentagon Strategy, on behalf of the new government of the 7th mandate, Samdech would like to continue the exemplary example of Samdech Techo Hun Sen to promote the reform and strengthening of governance by focusing on Promote and strengthen cleanliness in public administration, and the Royal Government would like to focus on the following five tasks:
First, the preparation and implementation of professional ethics and codes of conduct in public functions, as well as the promotion of strict adherence to the principles of inequality, function and conflict of interest in the performance of public officials.
Second, to strengthen the effectiveness of inspections and audits, as well as to establish the framework and rules of the inspection and audit system to ensure the harmonization of inspection and audit functions in public administration.
Third, strengthening the mechanism for managing and providing public services, providing incentives based on philanthropy, and taking strict legal action in the performance of roles and responsibilities to increase the trust and efficiency of public services.
Fourth, to continue to strengthen and expand education, prevention and control, as well as to strictly enforce the law to crack down on corruption.
Fifth, strengthening cooperation between the Anti-Corruption Unit and public institutions, especially through focal mechanisms, both education and prevention, to prepare for the implementation, monitoring, monitoring and evaluation of the implementation of strategic plans and promote cleanliness in By public institutions.
The Royal Government would also like to commend all the efforts made by the National Anti-Corruption Council and the Anti-Corruption Unit to fulfill their national and international duties in the past by bringing the trust, support and participation of many ministries and institutions. Sub-national and general masses are also strong.
