US official to visit Taiwan to explain new chip exports
(Taipei) - Taiwan's economy minister said on Monday that US officials are scheduled to visit Taiwan to explain to companies in detail new measures to curb the export of high-end chips, mainly to Taiwan. On China. According to Reuters.
The government of President Joe Biden in October said it planned to stop exports to China of artificial intelligence chips designed by Nvidia and others as part of measures to try to stop Beijing. From the acquisition of US technology in order to strengthen its military.
"We think they (the United States) came to Taiwan to explain things to companies to find out face-to-face what US law enforcement thinks, talking directly to the details," he said. "Taiwan needs."
