Business meeting between Cambodian Chamber of Commerce and Dubai Chamber of Commerce
(Phnom Penh): On the morning of December 5, 2023, at the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce, Duke Kith Meng, President of the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce and Chairman of the ASEAN-Cambodia Business Advisory Council, led senior members and the International Chamber of Commerce in Cambodia. Representatives of a number of key companies met with Marwan AlMarri, Regional Director for Asia of the Dubai Chamber of Commerce, and some colleagues from Vietnam.
The purpose of this meeting is to find business partners to invest in Cambodia from the Dubai Chamber of Commerce, especially to share their business and investment environment activities and other business information to the members of the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce to understand the business environment and investment. In Cambodia as well.
In response, the Dubai Chamber of Commerce accepted the request and will continue to maintain effective relations between the two chambers of commerce.
SME Bank to provide low interest rate loans and ease collateral for cashew processing enterprises in Cambodia
(Phnom Penh): The Cambodian Cashew Federation and the Small and Medium Enterprise Bank of Cambodia (SME Bank) have signed a Memorandum of Understanding (MoU) to facilitate lending to cashew processing enterprises in Cambodia to promote better cashew processing in Cambodia. Exported in accordance with government policy.
Through the signing of this Memorandum of Understanding, business owners who are members of the Cambodian Cashew Federation can apply for a business financing scheme with favorable conditions from the Bank of Small and Medium Enterprises of Cambodia to expand their business.
Mr. An Dara, President of the Cashew Federation of Cambodia, said that the Royal Government is currently paying close attention to the cultivation and processing of cashews by setting out a national policy to promote cashew processing to 25% of the cashew. Million tons in 2027 and 50% of 1 million tons in 2032.
Through this policy, the Royal Government has encouraged and encouraged the Cashew Federation to cooperate with government institutions and development partners to promote more cashew processing to promote the export of processed cashew nuts to foreign markets.
He said that the market for processed cashew nuts in Cambodia is wide, especially in the United States, Europe, Japan, China, etc., which is an opportunity for Cambodia to penetrate those markets. However, Cambodia's processing is currently limited and some of the non-standard processing can be exported.
He said that the main problem of cashew processing enterprises in Cambodia is the lack of capital to buy fresh cashew nuts to dry and store for processing.
According to An Dara, there are currently about 25 cashew processing companies in Cambodia, of which only about 10 are capable of processing standard cashew nuts for export to international markets.
Dr. Lim Oun, Director General of the Bank for Small and Medium Enterprises of Cambodia, stated that this cooperation is a strategic goal that the Bank has set to support the growth of the cashew sector in Cambodia.
"The Bank strongly believes that the signing of this Memorandum of Understanding is part of addressing the business expansion challenges for all cashew actors, including processors and exporters, as well as "The height of the cashew processing industry in Cambodia to be even better."
