(Phnom Penh): The Cambodian Human Rights Committee (CPP) has issued a press release on the outcome of a working meeting between Senior Minister Keo Remy, President of the Cambodian Human Rights Committee (CCHR) and UN Special Rapporteur Vitith Montaboun. In charge of the human rights situation in Cambodia on the morning of December 5, 2023.
The purpose of this meeting was to discuss the progress of the human rights situation in Cambodia and the establishment of a national human rights body in Cambodia.
Senior Minister Keo Remy said that Cambodia remains committed to maintaining peace, which is fundamental to guaranteeing human rights, especially the right to life.
In addition, he stated that in the seventh mandate, the Royal Government has continued to promote economic, social and cultural rights through six priorities in the first phase of the Pentagon Strategy led by Samdech Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia through six priorities. In the first phase of the Pentagon strategy.
Mr. Vitit Montaboun expressed his appreciation for Cambodia for its positive progress in the field of human rights, especially the drafting of the Law on the Establishment of National Human Rights Institutions, and thanked the Cambodian Human Rights Committee for organizing the event. This meeting has a friendly atmosphere, understanding and brings proud results.
