In addition, the first CLV-DTA Parliamentary Summit aims to strengthen cooperation between our three bordering countries, not only highlighting the strategic importance of cooperation in all areas of the region, but also It has also contributed to ASEAN connectivity and the strengthening of the ASEAN Community, especially in bridging the development gap in the region, promoting the well-being and well-being of our people.
* Third: Of course, within the framework of cooperation in the field of national security, our three Ministries of Defense have achieved many achievements in participating in security cooperation along the border, building solidarity. Good Neighborhood, Strengthening Traditional Friendship and Strengthening Sustainable Cooperation to Ensure a Future of Peace, Stability and Prosperity
* Fifth: At the same time, we still have meetings to discuss through the existing mechanisms of the three countries, we together with the strengthening of cooperation in the fight against human trafficking, drug crime, transnational crime. Forest crime, transnational crime, as well as facilitating the people of our three countries to travel across the border have yielded fruitful results.
The three armies of our three countries continue to work together to enhance defense cooperation in politics, security, order and order along the border, and to further improve diplomatic and military relations in accordance with our existing protocol. The necessary requirements for our cooperation to reach a higher and deeper level in line with the aspirations of all our people in the future.
Non-traditional security challenges such as climate change and cybercrime are exacerbated, making development efforts difficult. In addition, disasters caused by climate change and other traditional and non-traditional security challenges remain a concern for all of us.
* Eighth: In response to the above-mentioned challenges, the Armed Forces of the three countries need to strengthen their cooperation to be able to solve these problems most effectively.
The Royal Government of the Ministry of National Defense of the Kingdom of Cambodia has emphasized its position on "Unity for Cooperation" and not "Unity for Confrontation," so the three countries must strive to strengthen regional relations. Diplomacy, military, friendship, brotherhood as countries, villages, fences together.
* Ninth: We must prioritize the value of peace above all else. Therefore, in the current context, we need to enhance cooperation in the fields of technology, technology and science, increase technology knowledge, human resource development, strengthening all-round cooperation between the three Ministries of Defense is important and necessary for traditional communication. Unity, understanding, trust are common interests and sustainable development.
At the same time, we need to strengthen the implementation of the existing structural protocol, we create each annual plan is necessary to promote cooperation in the field of defense and other areas to grow to another level. .
* Eleventh: This meeting reflects the joint commitment to strengthen and expand the good relations, friendship, solidarity in good cooperation between the three countries to be stronger, closer and more effective for the benefit of The people of our three countries.
Twelfth: Finally, I would like to wish the 1st CLV-DTA Parliamentary Summit on Strengthening the Role and Duties of the National Assembly in Promoting Comprehensive Cooperation between Cambodia, Laos and Vietnam. Achieve more brilliant success.
During the meeting, the two sides exchanged views on enhancing ASEAN-China relations and exploring ways to further strengthen cooperation between ASEAN and China, including Anhui Province, in areas such as trade, investment, digital economy and exchanges. People and people and so on.
On that occasion, the two sides exchanged views on the initiatives and projects of the ASEAN-Korea Center for the Promotion of ASEAN-Republic of Korea Cooperation, as the 35th Anniversary of the ASEAN-Korea Dialogue Partnership is approaching. 2024.
On Tuesday morning, the ASEAN Secretary-General also attended the launch of the handbook on "Environmental, Social and Governance Practices in ASEAN and Korea: The Road to Sustainability".
In a keynote address to the National Assembly, President Khuon Sodary said that the CLV Summit is a historic event with the vision of enhancing parliamentary mechanisms, strengthening cooperation and enhancing the three countries' strategic partnership. More comprehensive and in-depth, reflecting the common values of peacekeeping, promoting prosperity and sustainable development, and resilience.
The National Assembly said that the CLV Development Triangle was established in 1999, which was initiated by Samdech Techo Hun Sen as a compass to guide the transformation of the border area into a development and harmonization zone of people-to-people connections. The people of the three countries are on the road to peace, peace and prosperity together.
The National Assembly President stressed that the strengthening of parliamentary mechanisms to participate in the development of the CLV is a testament to the strategic goals based on mutual respect and trust to promote political, cultural and economic cooperation. And security, which so far has brought many benefits to the people of the three countries.
The development triangle of the three countries consists of 13 provinces, Vietnam has 5 provinces, Laos has 4 provinces and the Kingdom of Cambodia has 4 provinces, namely Ratanakkiri, Mondulkiri, Kratie and Stung Treng. The development triangle of the three countries is a region with great potential for natural resources and biodiversity.
At the same time, the President of the National Assembly proposed to promote digital commerce, increase the capacity and resilience of small and medium enterprises (MSMEs), science, technology and innovation (STI). These connections are an important element in the action plan for CLV economic connectivity towards 2030.
