Phnom Penh Capital Hall Holds a Dissemination Workshop on Women's Empowerment and Leadership
(Phnom Penh): In accordance with the first phase of the Pentagon strategy of the Royal Government of the 7th mandate under the highest leadership of Samdech Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, "Human capital development" in public administration has been prioritized. To transform public administration into a highly capable and intelligent entity in line with the trends of digital evolution and the need to provide public services to the people.
At the same time, building human resources, especially among women, is an indispensable factor in promoting gender equality and empowering women in order to ensure full participation in leadership and decision-making. On this basis, Cambodia has adhered to the "principle of matriarchy" since the inception of the first state, which means that we adhere to a culture of respect and value for "women" in leading families, communities and society as a whole.
These are the words of Mr. Keut Chhe, Deputy Governor of Phnom Penh, representing Mr. Khuong Sreng, Governor of Phnom Penh while presiding over the opening ceremony of the dissemination workshop on "Women's Empowerment and Leadership" on Tuesday morning. December 2023.
The deputy governor said that the woman after having a family, she already has the reception and control of the family and the leadership in the family, just do not use the right to lead and manage in the outside society. Mr. Keut Chhe said that the man asked to cancel the words "women can not lead." Men should understand that women are more complex than men in both body and household chores as family supervisors.
In connection with the training of women empowerment and leadership, Mr. Keut Chhe advised the Human Resources Unit that men should also be invited to participate, as men are more involved in roles or domestic violence in order to Men understand the role of leadership in the family and society, without which men would not be successful.
