The Nepalese army, known as the Gurkhas, is serving in the British as well as Indian armies after India gained independence in 1947 under an agreement between the three countries. However, the Himalayan country does not have such an agreement with Russia, which has been at war with Ukraine since February 2022.
The Nepalese government said in a statement on Monday night that six of its citizens who had served in the Russian military had been killed, but did not provide further details. The statement added that the Nepalese government had asked the Russian government to send their bodies back to their homeland and provide compensation to their families.
