In 2023, the Royal Government of Cambodia has introduced the "National Policy on Cashew 2022-2027", which has become an effective driving force for strengthening and promoting the productivity of cashew production, seed processing and export.
Seeing this opportunity, Mr. Try Veng's VCP Thanh Dan on November 20, 2023 signed a business cooperation agreement with Thanh Dan Vietnam, which has many years of experience to bring processing machinery and technology. Recently came to the Cambodian market.
Mr. Try Veng said that the agreement was made to expand the market for cashew processing machinery and equipment to Cambodia, which is in need of machinery and processing technology, while the Royal Government of Cambodia has made great efforts to promote the policy. Cashews.
Please be informed that this Memorandum of Understanding will be held on the morning of December 6, 2023 in Kampong Thom province in the cashew forum under the theme "We together promote the potential of Cambodian cashews" under the chairmanship of three ministers, including: Minister Minister of Commerce, Minister of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries and Minister of Industry, Science, Technology and Innovation.
He strongly hopes that the introduction of new technologies and collaborative companies leading the supply of cashew processing machinery will enable Cambodia to seize opportunities, share global markets and contribute to the technical skills of Cambodian children.
Cashew is a strategic crop that the Royal Government has been paying attention to and promoting the largest export in the world, or can be said to be "the emperor" to export all cashew in the future.
In the first 10 months of 2023, Cambodia exported more than 610,000 tons of raw cashew nuts, earning 831 million US dollars, a decrease of nearly 16.7% compared to the same period in 2022. This is according to data from the Cambodian Cashew Association. The average price of dried cashew nuts is $ 1,658 per ton, according to the Cambodian Cashew Association. Siem Reap Provincial Council Holds a Meeting to Elect Chairman-Deputy Chairman of Siem Reap Provincial People's Office
(Siem Reap): On the afternoon of December 4, 2023, Mr. An Khun, Chairman of Siem Reap Provincial Council, chaired a meeting to elect the Chairman-Deputy Chairman of the Provincial People's Office with the participation of Ms. Councilors. Provinces and Ladies and Gentlemen, Members of the Election Commission, Chairman, Deputy Chairman of the Provincial People's Office and Deputy Director of Provincial Administration, Deputy Director of Human Resources and Administration.
Mr. An Khun, Chairman of the Provincial Council, said that the election of the Chairman-Deputy Chairman of the People's Office has already been organized through a series of meetings to promote the election of representatives of national civil society organizations. In addition, the National Civil Society Organization participates in the election of the Chairman and Deputy Chairman of the Citizens' Office in accordance with the Instruction No. 024 of the Ministry of Interior.
Mr. An Khun continued that the selection of the Chairman-Deputy Chairman of the People's Office is the core work of the Office, which plays an important role in receiving complaints, facilitating the settlement of extrajudicial complaints related to the provision of public services to the people, as well as Also manages sub-national administrations.
The Chairman of the Provincial Council also instructed the members of the Election Commission of the People's Office to be accurate, clear and fair in accordance with her decision to vote for the person who has Sufficient capacity to fulfill its role effectively.
After the election, Mr. Neth Phalkun was elected as the Director of the Siem Reap Provincial People's Office and Ms. Sim Sovannary as the Deputy Director of the Provincial People's Office. After the election and the announcement of the results, Mr. An Khun also instructed the Provincial Council Secretariat to prepare a letter of request to the Ministry of Interior for a formal announcement in accordance with legal procedures.
Chinese economic and trade delegation visits Cambodia to seek investment
(Phnom Penh): An economic and trade delegation of the Ji Lin Trade Promotion Council of China, along with the leaders of several major Chinese companies, visited Cambodia to seek investment.
After arriving in Cambodia, the delegation met with Deputy Prime Minister Sun Chanthol, First Vice President of the Council for the Development of Cambodia on December 4, 2023. The meeting was held at the request of the Ji Lin Provincial Trade Promotion Council to learn about investment policies and regulations in Cambodia. The two sides discussed investment projects in the fields of health, energy, fuel and herbal medicine.
Deputy Prime Minister Sun Chanthol requested all companies wishing to invest in various sectors in Cambodia to apply for investment projects with their detailed study to the Council for the Development of Cambodia for further implementation.
On that occasion, the Deputy Prime Minister also informed about the mission of the Council for the Development of Cambodia in facilitating investment project proposals with relevant ministries and institutions to companies to encourage investors to increase investment in Cambodia.
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Kao Muy Thong, Deputy Secretary General of the Council for Agricultural and Rural Development, said that nutrition is at the heart of the sustainable development goals of families, communities and the nation.
On the morning of December 5, Mr. Kao Muy Thong stated that nutrition is at the heart of the United Nations Sustainable Development Goals and the Millennium Development Goals for achieving this. To achieve the above goals, each country needs to strengthen cooperation, create innovative ideas based on research findings and interventions to reduce malnutrition in all its forms.
On the occasion, he added that based on the research of nutritionists, all forms of malnutrition and overweight problems are interrelated and can occur individually, it can occur in families in the community. And in the whole country. Malnutrition affects the health of people more than the effects of high blood pressure, smoking and air pollution.
He said that for Cambodia, the Council for Agricultural and Rural Development, as a staff of the Royal Government in coordinating the food security and nutrition sector, has led the development of a national strategy on food security and nutrition, a roadmap on food systems for sustainable development in Cambodia. Cambodia 2030 and other legal documents we need to improve food security and nutrition in Cambodia.
Mr. Kao Muy Thong stated that the workshop on nutrition-conscious food system is a forum for stakeholders in the food system to share and exchange information about ongoing projects or projects in the future and also as a network. Promote a nutritional system in the Lower Mekong Delta of Cambodia.
He added that the Nutrition Consideration Workshop is a platform for stakeholders in the food system to share information about ongoing projects or projects in the future, as well as a network to improve the system. Nutritionally Conscious Food in the Lower Mekong Delta of Cambodia.
