(Phnom Penh): On Tuesday, December 5, 2023, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, Samdech Moha Bovathibodi Hun Manet, officially announced the implementation of national policies related to national programs. Social assistance is the last of the six priority policies announced to be implemented in 2023.
The new Royal Government has started its journey by giving high consideration to the health and livelihood of the people. In response to this, the Royal Government, led by Samdech Mani Hun Manet, has set out six priority policies that need to be implemented urgently in 2023. Five priority policies have already been implemented in a row, while the priority policy related to the National Social Assistance Program is the latest program to be implemented.
Building a comprehensive, integrated and automated social protection system is important in supporting the well-being of the people, especially in times of emergency or crisis, in line with the National Social Protection Policy Framework 2016-2025, the Royal Government has implemented. Some social assistance programs to provide support to pregnant women, young children and people with disabilities in target communities.
In addition, in response to emergencies, the Royal Government has launched special social assistance programs, including cash assistance programs for poor and vulnerable families during the fight against Kovid-19 (ongoing), cash assistance programs. Following the closure of large-scale (closed) and cash assistance programs for vulnerable families severely affected by floods and inflationary pressures (also closed).
In this regard, the Royal Government will focus on the institutionalization of the National Social Assistance Program, which is comprehensive, integrated and automated to increase the capacity of the social protection system in response to crises or emergencies through the preparation of a number of key documents. 2 as follows:
- Cash support program for pregnant women and children under 2 years old - Scholarship program for poor primary and secondary students - Cash support program for the disabled - Cash support program for the elderly (60 years and older)
At the same time, the National Social Assistance Program in the Family Package also provides basic support for all equitable families and takes into account family members living with HIV / AIDS, adhering to the principles of moderation and equity and avoiding falls. Significantly lower income for families who have received allowances in the past.
Under the framework of the National Social Assistance Program in the family package will be a support when the program to provide cash to poor and vulnerable families during the fight against Kovid-19 ended with a gradual departure for three months from January. 2024, the official implementation of the National Social Assistance Program framework in the family package will start from April 2024 onwards.
The National Social Assistance Program in the family package will benefit about 700,000 equitable families, equivalent to 2.8 million people, and is planned to spend about 674.5 billion riels (165 million US dollars) in 2024.
2: Guidelines for the Social Security Response Framework "Draft Social Protection Framework for Emergency Response" is designed with the aim of institutionalizing the social protection system to be prepared for future emergencies and crises. . This framework identifies the types of emergencies that the social protection system can respond to, including: (1) natural disasters, (2) public health crises, and (3) macroeconomic and financial crises.
The choice of tools, measures, social protection policies in response to emergencies limited within this framework are as follows:
At the same time, the framework also identifies the main action plans and the roles of the participating ministries and institutions.
The above two documents, "Guidelines on the Social Protection Framework for Emergency Response" and "Guidelines on the Framework of the National Social Assistance Program in the Family Package" were submitted to the National Social Security Council meeting on the 5th of this month. July 2023, with the full approval of the content and submitted to the Plenary Meeting of the Council of Ministers and approved by the Royal Government on September 20, 2023.
It should be noted that in this 7th legislature, in addition to the introduction of the Pentagon Strategy - the first phase, which is the core policy, the Royal Government led by Samdech Moha Bovat Hun Sen has also launched six priority political programs to respond immediately. And the livelihood and health of the people.
The first program was officially launched on October 24, 2023, the second program was officially implemented on November 14, 2023, and the fourth program was implemented on October 24, 2023. Officially, on October 10, 2023, and the 5th and 6th programs will be officially implemented on November 20, 2023. Tomorrow morning, Samdech Manipadei Hun Manet announced the implementation of the national policy related to the National Social Assistance Program.
