(Phnom Penh): Mr. Neth Pheaktra, Minister of Information, on the morning of December 4, 2023, inspected the work of officials stationed at the OWSO. The Ministry of Information organized the launch of the OWSO on December 1, 2023, with officials from the five General Departments on duty to receive documents and provide public services.
The Ministry of Information has designated a specific location in front of the Ministry of Information building and has officers stationed at the OWSO to provide timely customer service as scheduled.
Through a joint prakas on the provision of public services by the Ministry of Information, the Ministry of Economy and Finance decided to allow the Ministry of Information to implement the collection of revenue from public service fees for the benefit of the national budget.
This public service package details the service fee, service period and validity for each type of public service as stated in the appendix attached to this joint prakas.
The Ministry of Information shall post to the public, especially at the service point, the service standards, including: price list, documents and procedures for the provision of services related to the above revenue collection. The Ministry of Information shall set up a place to receive complaints that may occur eventually, especially in the event of non-compliance with service standards or excessive fees or delays.
The Ministry of Information has the duty to collect revenue, be responsible for the revenue collected and pay the revenue to the national budget, including registering the accounts on revenue operations and recording the revenue in the sub-account section of the budget content, as well as making labels. Income statement.
The division of responsibilities for the management of revenue collection from the provision of public services between the Central Administration of the Ministry of Information and the Capital and Provincial Information Departments shall be determined by a Prakas of the Minister of Information.
The Ministry of Information shall send a copy of this declaration to the Ministry of Economy and Finance for information and to monitor revenue performance.
All revenue collection from public service fees as stated in the table in the Annex attached to this Joint Prakas shall use the payment receipt provided by the Ministry of Economy and Finance in accordance with the Prakas dated 17 March 2011 on Introduce payment receipts and circulars on the management of payment receipts of the Ministry of Economy and Finance.
The Ministry of Information shall make a report on the implementation of monthly and annual revenue to be submitted to the Ministry of Economy and Finance before the 10th of the following month for the monthly report and before the 15th of January of the following year for the annual report. Years.
