As of September 2023, 1,162 electric vehicles have been registered in Cambodia
(Phnom Penh): A senior official of the Ministry of Public Works and Transport said that as of September 2023, there were about 1,162 electric vehicles registered in Cambodia, including 573 cars, 387 tricycles and motorcycles. There are 202 units.
Mr. Pov Maly, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Public Works and Transport, said that compared to the registration of electric vehicles in 2022 and 2021, there is a significant increase, with 2062 electric vehicles registered in 2022 and 2021. There were 63 units, an increase of about 951%.
He pointed out that the growth of the use of electric vehicles in Cambodia, with the participation of the private sector with the Royal Government to promote the electric vehicle sector in Cambodia and because people are aware of the benefits of using electric vehicles are more profitable. Compared with the use of internal combustion vehicles.
As for maintenance, electric cars are less expensive compared to using fuel-efficient vehicles (internal combustion engines), with a difference of 20,000 to 30,000 points, especially without having to worry about changing the engine oil. Damage to the electrical system, water system in the machine and so on.
The Royal Government, through the Ministry of Public Works and Transport, has been working hard to increase support infrastructure, such as the establishment of more charging stations in the capitals and provinces, currently with 18 locations and 23 charging stations to charge. Convenience for people to use electric vehicles, which we strive to expand more in remote provinces, as well as on major national roads.
