The eight recommendations were given by the President on December 4, 2023, when he presided over the celebration of the 25th Cambodian Day of Persons with Disabilities and the 41st International Day of Persons with Disabilities at the Koh Pich Theater.
According to the Prime Minister, the eight recommendations include:
* First, to increase investment in people with disabilities and continue to build more resources for people with disabilities, including innovative and vibrant curricula, to ensure that people with disabilities can live in Cambodian society with equity and competitive opportunities. Both in countries, regions and globally.
* Third: All ministries, institutions, relevant partner organizations and the private sector must start adjusting or arranging facilities for people with disabilities in public and private places in accordance with the Law on the Promotion of the Rights of Persons with Disabilities and the technical standards of physical infrastructure to make it easier for people. Have a disability.
* Fourth: All Ministries, Institutions and the private sector must encourage people with disabilities who have the qualifications and ability to fulfill their responsibilities in positions with the right to work without discrimination, including working as civil servants. Workers, apprentices or interns.
* Fifth: Encourage the participation of the private sector, civil society, factories, enterprises and all institutions to implement responsibly and by awakening the obligation to recruit people with disabilities to continue to work as others. It is stated in the Law on the Protection and Promotion of the Rights of Persons with Disabilities.
* Sixth, the Ministry of Information must guide all public and private radio and television stations, as well as all media outlets, to increase the broadcast time by providing sign language translation so that people with disabilities can receive information in a timely manner. Time.
Seventh, the Ministry of Public Works and Transport and the Ministry of Health will cooperate with the Ministry of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation to make it easier for people with disabilities to obtain a driver's license in accordance with the capabilities and technical characteristics of vehicles.
* Eighth: All ministries and institutions as well as competent authorities at all levels, relevant partner organizations and the private sector continue to strengthen the implementation of existing laws and regulations and continue to participate in additional initiatives on the protection and promotion of the rights of persons with disabilities. .
