(Phnom Penh): On the morning of Monday, December 4, 2023, Cambodian Prime Minister Hun Manet presided over a celebration of the Day of Persons with Disabilities. The 25th Cambodia and the 41st International Day of Persons with Disabilities held at the Koh Pich Theater.
The 25th Cambodian Day of Persons with Disabilities and the 41st International Day of Persons with Disabilities 2023 will be organized under the theme "Innovative Solutions for a Comfortable and Equitable Society".
The organization of this day is a celebration of the recent achievements in the field of disability, which shows the strong will and attention of the governments of each country as a signatory to the Convention on the Rights of Persons with Disabilities to continue to promote the welfare and promotion. All persons with disabilities have no discrimination on the basis of color, religion, status or political affiliation.
