Third, all ministries, institutions, relevant partner organizations and the private sector must start adjusting or arranging facilities for people with disabilities in public and private places in accordance with the Law on the Promotion of the Rights of Persons with Disabilities and the technical standards of physical infrastructure to make it easier for the rich. Disability.
Fourth, all ministries, public institutions and the private sector must encourage people with disabilities who have the qualifications and ability to fulfill their duties and responsibilities in positions with the right to work without discrimination, including working as civil servants, workers. Employees, apprentices or interns, etc.
Fifth, to encourage the participation of the private sector, civil society, factories, enterprises and all institutions to implement responsibly and by raising the obligation to recruit people with disabilities to continue to work as others have. Provided in the Law on the Protection and Promotion of the Rights of Persons with Disabilities.
