Speaking on the occasion of presiding over the closing ceremony of the Sea Festival in Kep, Samdech Hun Sen said that without peace, there would be no visit to Kep.
He said that yesterday, when he rode to Kep province by helicopter through Phnom Vly, which is a very important former battlefield. The helicopter pilot for Samdech, also a veteran of the war, told Samdech that he had been here twice to drop bombs because the area was occupied by the Khmer Rouge.
The Prime Minister said that here are all plantations, turning from a battlefield into a development site. Three foreigners were captured by the Khmer Rouge here near the railway line and killed. Nor can escape.
This commemoration of Samdech Thipadei Hun Manet was made on the evening of December 3, 2023, on the occasion of Samdech presiding over the closing ceremony of the 10th Sea Festival in Kep Province.
"My experience, I actually studied abroad, I met some people in 2002, when I first went to England, when I arrived at the airport, my passport was left by the immigration police for about 15 minutes, I wonder. "I asked him if there was a problem because my visa was not a problem, he just said he had never seen a Cambodian passport. You were the first person to hold a Cambodian passport to study in England."
On that occasion, Samdech Hun Sen also reminded that after the British police found out that Samdech was Cambodian, the British police immediately asked Samdech whether Cambodia was over the war or not. According to Samdech, at that time, the British police also considered wanting to visit Cambodia.
Samdech Hun Manet added that during his two years of studying in the United Kingdom, the situation in Cambodia changed from 1998 to 2002, when Cambodia ended the civil war. During 2004, when Samdech met with other British immigration police officers, he confirmed that his family had visited Cambodia, saying that Cambodia was very safe and that he would visit Cambodia himself.
Samdech Hun Sen said that now Cambodian fame is better known to foreigners through the image of Angkor Wat and the promotion through tourists who visit Cambodia and return, they advertise what Cambodia Available to their relatives in their hometown. Samdech considers good propaganda from Cambodia by foreign tourists is very important for the potential of Cambodia's tourism sector.
This statement was made by Samdech Hun Sen Manet during the closing ceremony of the 10th Sea Festival (Round 3) in Kep Province on the night of December 3, 2023.
On that occasion, Samdech Thipdey said that the four provinces bordering Cambodia, if combined, are not large, but we have the potential of beaches, islands, natural resources, potential as ports, potential for multi-purpose tourism and so on.
He added that the master plan for the development of the four provinces bordering Cambodia is to ensure the value of long-term development. Mutually for the benefit of Cambodia, not to compete with each other, which leads to the loss of common interests.
"This plan is to ensure clear development so that the four provinces do not compete with each other, but to make the four provinces support each other so that our coastline can go," he said. "As a province that gathers forces to promote the potential of Cambodia's seaside as a total force, this is what we need to do."
"If any province has any potential, it is important to focus on development investment and develop a master plan to support that development," he said.
For Kep, Hun Manet stated that it is a province with potential for eco-tourism and some other tourism products, so it is necessary to consider to ensure long-term value rather than short-term value because it has developed experience. But fail.
