The response of the spokesperson of the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports at this time after receiving some information that is different from the parents of students, especially regarding the requirement to pay some money to support the work. This reform.
Ms. Kim Sethany responded to the full content as follows:
"Cambodia needs education reform in line with scientific education policy to step into global integration. A new program has been developed in this direction to achieve this goal. The spirit of the new generation program and the Ministry's commitment to design reforms in the education sector (The spirit of the new generation program is the main commitment of the Royal Government in education reform).
The New Generation School Program is a program that creates a new development model in the public education system that will lead to the establishment of high-investment public schools, linked to new standards, accountability and good governance, as well as standards. Professions for study in the 21st century.
All teachers working here are competitively selected and have a selection committee from ministries and programs. The employment contract is made once a year and is subject to end-of-year evaluation by the new generation school board. All teachers must be trained in new teaching techniques and pedagogy before teaching.
Teachers are strictly prohibited from inactive activities and contrary to the professional ethics of teachers, such as selling copies, doing business in schools and some other activities. Teaching both theory and practice Students study throughout the day, students are required to participate in extracurricular and individual and group research activities, mainstreaming the use of ICT in all forms of learning and teaching.
The new generation school program is being implemented in 11 schools covering from primary to secondary level (grades 1 to 12) with 7 secondary schools and 4 primary schools in 5 provinces (Phnom Penh, Kandal province). Kampong Speu, Kampong Cham and Svay Rieng provinces) with a total of 10,122 students, 4,710 girls. "This is the beginning of a long mission and it will be successful with the participation of all of us."
