Senior National Bank official urges banking users to pay close attention to personal information security
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Heng Bo Makara, First Deputy Director General of the Audit Department of the National Bank of Cambodia, urged users of banking services, including digital banking, to pay close attention to the security of their network account information. Personal society.
This proposal was made on the occasion of Mr. Heng Bo Makara's participation in the Economic and Business Forum focusing on the topic of digital banking organized by ACLEDA Business Institute on December 2, 2023.
Mr. Heng Bo Makara stated, "I urge users of banking services, including digital banking, to pay close attention to the security of personal social media account information."
In addition, Mr. Heng Bo Makara also advised to understand the use of digital financial services and to be very careful before transferring money through mobile applications or accounts or through agents by verifying phone numbers, account numbers and Recipient identities, etc. to be accurate and clear.
According to the First Deputy Director General of the Audit Department of the National Bank of Cambodia, financial literacy and digital finance are an important task to ensure the full participation of the people in the digital society. By a sustainable environment.
Dr. Phon Narin, Director of ACLEDA Business Institute, said that this economic forum is a co-curricular program in which the institute focuses on linking curricula to related industries, including: The digital banking sector.
Dr. Phon Narin added that this economic forum is also an opportunity for students to learn from experts in related fields, as well as the opportunity to network with potential partners and employers, etc. -.
Please be informed that the purpose of this economic and business forum is to:
* Raise awareness of the latest trends and developments in digital banking * Identify the risks and opportunities that digital banking may face for operators and consumers * Facilitate discussions and collaborations between experts from the expert banking sector Technology and Regulators * Recommend for policymakers and regulators how to support the safe and accurate growth of digital banking.
The launch of QR Code cross-border payments will boost digital payments, promote the use of the national currency in the market in a convenient, fast, affordable, secure way and boost economic growth, tourism and cross-border trade. Cambodia and the Socialist Republic of Vietnam.
The cross-border payment system between Cambodia and Vietnam, which was announced today, allows Cambodians with a riel bank account to use the mobile banking application for Vietnamese dong payment transactions by scanning the VietQR Code. Traders or shops in Vietnam.
In addition, the National Bank of Cambodia and the State Bank of Vietnam held a bilateral meeting aimed at strengthening ties and cooperation between the two central banks.
