Samdech Thipadei Hun Manet instructs the coastal provincial authorities to take care of security at tourist sites so as not to become a haven for drugs, human trafficking and transnational crime (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): Samdech Thipadei Hun Manet, Director The Cambodian Minister instructed all local authorities in coastal provinces to take care of security at tourist sites without becoming a haven for drugs, human trafficking and transnational crime.
This statement was made on the occasion of Samdech presiding over the closing ceremony of the 10th Sea Festival in Kep province on the afternoon of December 3, 2023, which went smoothly under the happy crowd.
In this ceremony, Samdech made some recommendations to the coastal provincial authorities to promote Cambodia's tourism sector, including the fifth point is to maintain security for tourists.
"Local authorities, especially in the tourist area, must continue to pay close attention to maintaining security and order for tourists. In this regard, I would like to encourage the strengthening of security at all tourist destinations," he said. "And do not allow these tourist destinations, including coastal areas, to become a haven for drug users, human trafficking and transnational crime."
Samdech Hun Sen also called on tour operators to join the clean city, clean resort, good service, good hospitality and clean environment.
