(Phnom Penh): A well-known agricultural businessman in Cambodia, Duke Mong Reththy, said that together to prevent the import and stop eating of low quality frozen meat will help the livestock business in Cambodia and health. Consumers.
Tycoon Mong Reththy noted that the livestock sector in Cambodia in the last 10 years has grown rapidly, from family farming to modern commercial farming as developed countries in the world. . Unfortunately, the livestock sector in Cambodia has been experiencing a serious crisis in 2023, causing farmers to lose.
He said the main impact on the livestock business was not the Kovid 19 disease or the Ukraine war or the Israeli-Palestinian war, but the importation of a number of unusually low-quality frozen meat for sale. In the small and large market in Cambodia.
He added that in the context of free trade in the region, Cambodia can not close the import of frozen meat. However, he urged the importation of other meats to be legal, respect quality standards and ensure food safety for people across the country.
He called on stakeholders from the private sector, the public sector and students to continue to help spread the word about the properties of frozen meat to the public to gain a greater understanding of frozen meat safety for citizens' health and the impact of Import frozen meat to the livestock sector in Cambodia. When people know and understand, people have to think carefully before buying meat to eat or eat at any restaurant.
At the same time, he called on entrepreneurs in the field of animal husbandry to cooperate more closely, share information with each other, improve the proper application of techniques to ensure the balance of production and marketing in the context of regional competitive markets.
At the same time, he expressed his appreciation to Cambodian entrepreneurs as well as some foreign entrepreneurs who have come to invest in animal husbandry in Cambodia, although this year was not profitable and have worked hard in the field of policy. Meet and discuss with the relevant ministries and institutions to seek support and seek the right to implement the law to help the animal husbandry sector and ensure social welfare.
It should be informed that recently, frozen meat, including pork, chicken, fish, etc., has been smuggled into Cambodia by corrupt traders. The prices of those substandard frozen meat are lower than those of domestic livestock, which affects the livestock business in Cambodia.
At the 19th Royal Government and Private Sector Forum on November 13, Samdech Prime Minister Hun Manet, Prime Minister of Cambodia, instructed relevant officials to strictly strengthen the import of food, especially frozen pork, fish, chicken and eggs. Quality affects the health of consumers.
