The South Korean Defense Ministry said that through the successful launch of the reconnaissance satellite, the South Korean military has ensured its own independent reconnaissance and reconnaissance capabilities, and it will help provide superiority for Seoul. In a spy competition with North Korea. In the past, South Korea has relied heavily on the United States for satellite reconnaissance activities.
