Mr. Le Van Thuy expressed his deep gratitude to the President of the National Assembly for taking the opportunity to pay a courtesy call during his visit to Vietnam. Mr. Le Van Thuy congratulated the National Assembly President who was elected by the National Assembly of Cambodia as the President of the National Assembly in the 7th legislature.
National Assembly President Khuon Sodary congratulates the results of the meeting of the Cambodia-Vietnam Friendship Association and the Vietnam-Cambodia Friendship Association in Tay Ninh province on November 12, discussing and evaluating the progress of implementation. Memorandum of Understanding between the two associations for one year, with proud results.
The National Assembly President praised the Association's mission on diplomatic cooperation and connectivity between the two countries through building trust and mutual understanding to strengthen solidarity, friendship and cooperation between the people and the people. The people, the government and the government, especially in the fields of economy, society, tourism, trade, culture, science and cooperation, are the borders of the two countries, the border of peace and development.
The National Assembly stressed that the friendship between the two countries, Cambodia and Vietnam, has played an important role in promoting social and cultural exchanges, as well as promoting economic cooperation and building a trusting partnership. Today marks the 45th anniversary of the birth of the "United Front for National Salvation of Cambodia, now called the United Front for the Development of Motherland Cambodia" (Video inside)
The "Cambodian United Front for National Salvation" was organized based on the pure national spirit of the Cambodian people, the unity of all nationalities throughout the country, mobilizing all social forces regardless of political affiliation, religion, caste, workers, farmers, intellectuals, monks, ethnic nationalities and the people. Cambodians living abroad as well.
December 2, 1978 is the day that the "United Front for the National Salvation of Cambodia" was established in Cheung Khlou village, 2 Thnou commune, Sroul Snoul, Kratie province, with mutual support and spirit between friendly countries and the "Front" "Cambodian National Salvation Unity" is further strengthened solidarity, friendship and closer cooperation.
After the day of liberation on January 7, 1979, the General Assembly of the "United Front for National Salvation of Cambodia" changed its name to "Front for the Defense of the Motherland of Cambodia". On April 26-27, 2006, the 5th General Assembly of the Front changed its name to "United Front for the Development of Motherland Cambodia" to this day.
The Front is a comprehensive organization of Cambodian people, both inside and outside the country, regardless of religion, caste, political affiliation, mobilizing all forces, patriotism, peace, democracy and freedom, volunteering to build and develop the country to achieve poverty reduction for prosperity. Harmony and happiness to the people of Cambodia.
The Front takes care to protect the rights, freedoms and legitimate interests of the people by respecting the Constitution and the laws in force of the State, and gathers opinions and suggestions from the people to submit proposals to the competent institutions for review and resolution.
The Front participates in building and strengthening the relationship of solidarity, friendship and good cooperation between the people of Cambodia and the people of countries in the region and the world.
From a country devastated by the flames of war for more than 40 years, under the right leadership and with a long-term vision of the Royal Government, by overcoming countless obstacles and difficulties, The country has achieved great and important achievements in history and is moving forward vigorously on the path of full peace, political stability, social order and development in all fields.
Starting from the resistance movement and all kinds of sacrifices, even life more than 40 years ago made the people free from suffering, free from slaughter, returned with full freedom to live, work and earn a living. Gradually promoted from year to year under the roof of this hard-earned peace.
In order to strengthen the leadership structure and act more effectively in the 6th General Assembly on November 15, 2023, the Front decided to elect Samdech Ponhea Chakrei Heng Samrin as the Honorary Chairman of the National Council of the Solidarity Front, Samdech His Excellency Hun Manp was the honorary presidency, Samdech Kittisangkhab Dr. Men Sam An was the chairman and Hun Many was the vice chairman of the National Front Council.
The 45th anniversary of the founding of the National Liberation Movement, engraved in the hearts of the Cambodian people, will never be forgotten. Many programs have been created to commemorate the heroic heroism of this national liberation movement.
The United Front for the National Salvation of Cambodia, now known as the National Council of the United Front for the Development of Motherland Cambodia, was established on December 2, 1978 and issued its 11b statement in the Snuol Liberation Area, Snuol District, Kratie Province.
* The Kampuchean United Front for National Salvation was formed by the great unity of the people, both inside and outside the country, including Samdech Akka Moha Ponhea Chakrei Heng Samrin, Samdech Akka Moha Thamma Pothisal Chea Sim, Samdech Akka Moha Padei Techo Hun Sen and patriotic heroes. Many others are leaders. The reasons for the United Front for National Salvation are:
* During the 1975-1978 genocidal regime of Pol Pot, the situation in the country plunged into a catastrophic catastrophe. At that time, Pol Pot's assassins pushed the country upside down in a way that no one could have imagined.
Under the banner of the Absolute Revolution, they began to purge Cambodian society, exterminating the city, forcing millions of market people to leave their homes and property to live in the miserable and mountainous countryside. To work hard.
* Trampling and destroying culture, civilization, abolishing religious freedom, forcing men and women to marry dozens of couples without religious sentiments.
* They have destroyed Buddhist temples, the nation's longest-running religion, destroyed temples, shrines, Bible schools, ordinances of Buddhism and Islam.
* Almost completely closed human resource development, closed schools from primary to higher education. School-age children are not educated and are forced into the mobile unit to work like adults.
The 11 b statement of the United Front for National Salvation of Cambodia is as follows:
3. Build and strengthen the national army to protect the motherland, protect the life and property of the people, and protect the independence, sovereignty and territorial integrity.
5. Implement the independent economic path in each phase, rebuild the devastated territory, repair the new economy, the economy serves the interests on the basis of agricultural expansion and industry. Eliminate coercion, eradicate rice harvest, people's property, open banks, distribute banknotes, repair and expand the exchange of all goods, open domestic trade, abolish forced labor.
7. Eliminate the culture of reaction and build a new culture with national character and people's views. Eliminate ignorance, expand all levels of education and professional skills. Preserve and protect the antiquities, national heritage, parks, pagodas that were destroyed by Pol Pot.
8. Congratulate and facilitate the officers, soldiers in the armed forces, cadres, staff who abandoned the Pol Pot regime and returned to live with the people. Punish the stubborn master and favor the faithful and correct in time, as well as praise the accomplices.
9. Implement foreign paths, peace, friendship and non-alignment with all countries, without adhering to the socio-political regime on the basis of peace, respect for independence, sovereignty and territorial integrity, not interfering in internal affairs, equally and beneficially. Come and go.
Based on the essential principles of the United Front for National Salvation of Cambodia, we have successfully implemented the principle of national unification. All classes, regardless of political affiliation, caste, religion.
The Thai Minister of Defense said this during a courtesy call with Samdech Techo Hun Sen at the January 7 Palace on the afternoon of December 1, 2023.
After being appointed Minister of Defense of Thailand, Mr. Sothin Klangseng chose Cambodia as his first country to visit, as did his Prime Minister.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen commended the Thai Minister of Defense for choosing Cambodia as the first country in his visit and delegation, as well as the visit of the Thai Prime Minister last September, which showed his concern. Of Thailand for friendly relations and cooperation with Cambodia.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen expressed hope that the visit of the Thai Defense Ministry delegation at this time will further strengthen the relationship between the two countries, especially between the two armies.
The Minister praised the good relations between the two countries, which have been smooth and strong, with the two countries using existing mechanisms in the past, such as the JBC mechanism, to gradually strengthen relations.
The Minister deeply appreciated and respected Samdech Techo for leading the politics, bringing peace to the country and building the country, growing politically and economically, and the people living happily, prospering and prospering. And the smooth transition to the next generation, which shows the strength to continue to lead from the previous generation and hope that Cambodia will grow rapidly.
The Thai Minister of Defense thanked Samdech Techo after listening to meaningful speeches as a model of leadership that he can learn to organize leadership in his country.
The Minister considered the experience of Samdech Techo important not only in Cambodia but also in the world forum as well as in the ASEAN forum.
