ASEAN Secretary-General Delivers Keynote Address at Sustainable Financial Forum and Launch of ASEAN Green Investment Principles and Meets with Leaders
JAKARTA: On the morning of Friday, December 1, 2023, in Jakarta, Republic of Indonesia, Dr. Kao Kim Hourn, Secretary-General of ASEAN, gave a keynote address at the ASEAN Financial Sustainability Forum and Launch of the ASEAN Green Investment Principles.
On that occasion, the ASEAN Secretary-General stressed the importance of promoting sustainable finance in the region and highlighted some key ASEAN initiatives.
On Friday morning, Dr. Kao Kim Hourn received HE An Kwang-Il, Ambassador of the Democratic People's Republic of Korea to say goodbye and discuss work. On that occasion, the two sides exchanged views on ways to enhance relations between ASEAN and the Democratic People's Republic of Korea.
On Friday afternoon, the Secretary-General of ASEAN received Ms. Candith Mashego-Dlamini, Deputy Minister of International Relations and Cooperation of the Republic of South Africa, for a courtesy call and discussion. The two sides discussed ways and means to make the ASEAN-South Africa Dialogue Partnership more meaningful and to further strengthen mutually beneficial cooperation.
On Friday evening, Dr. Kao Kim Hourn, Secretary-General of ASEAN, delivered a congratulatory speech at the 5th ASEAN-Korea Day Party hosted by the Mission of the Republic of Korea to ASEAN.
The ASEAN Secretary-General highlighted the dialogue partnership between ASEAN and Korea over the past 34 years and thanked the Republic of Korea for its support for ASEAN community building efforts.
Dr. Kao Kim Hourn also reaffirmed his commitment to work closely with the Republic of Korea to enhance relations, while the two sides will establish a comprehensive strategic partnership in 2024, coinciding with the 35th anniversary of the partnership. ASEAN-ROK Dialogue Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen Sends 6 Key Messages to Compatriots, Especially Youth to End AIDS Together by 2025
The six key messages of Samdech Kittipritthbandit are as follows:
1: Commit to participating in preventing the spread and ending of AIDS by 2025 by adhering to the principles of equality and environment.
2. Practice peer-to-peer methods to stay away from drugs, sexual promiscuity, which is a high risk of HIV / STIs, and to strive to learn to maintain health, eat good nutrition, as the old saying goes. Say, "Love Yourself for Love"
3: Compatriots who are suspected of being exposed to HIV must seek counseling and testing for HIV as soon as possible, receive health care and use antiretroviral drugs properly, regularly and consistently.
4: Pregnant women should check and care for pregnancy with a midwife or doctor at least 4 times before giving birth and receive services to prevent HIV / syphilis and liver from health services.
5: Please all compatriots to encourage and not discriminate or stigmatize people living with HIV and AIDS.
6: Please call on men who have sex with men, transgender people, women who serve in entertainment venues, adults, etc. Must participate in the implementation of appropriate measures to prevent the transmission of HIV for personal health and to prevent new transmission and end HIV / AIDS by 2025 successfully.
On this significant occasion, "I would like to join the Royal Government of Cambodia, which in the past under the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen and now continues to be led by Samdech Moha Bovathipati Hun Manet, who has always been determined to lead the movement to join the national movement. "Only to prevent the spread of HIV and AIDS to be successful and recognized by the national and international community, especially from the United Nations."
