The "Drawing Game" was inscribed on the Intangible Cultural Heritage of Humanity on December 2, 2015 in Winduk, Namibia.
Draw is a popular game that Cambodians play in various ceremonies to show their solidarity as a team to win the game in a fun way.
The tug-of-war is linked to Khmer tradition and culture, and we can see historically valuable evidence through the carvings on the temples that tell the story of the churning of the sea of milk.
