Crackdown on detention in Chroy Changvar district, 13 suspects arrested (12 Bangladeshis) and 2 Chinese nationals released
(Phnom Penh): On the night of November 30, 2023, the police force of Chroy Changvar Administration Post, in cooperation with the Military Police of Chroy Changvar District, cracked down on the case of detention at 131G, Keo Chenda Street, Group 8, Village 3, Sangkat Chroy Changvar, Khan Chroy Changvar.
According to local police reports, for the operation, police detained 13 suspects (12 Bangladeshis and one Cambodian) and released two Chinese nationals.
According to the local police report, after receiving the emergency number from the National Police General Commission that there was a case of detention at the above point and the victim called the military number 1291, the Chroy Changvar Administrative Police Force cooperated with the force. Military police arrived at the scene immediately, surrounded the scene until the actual crackdown, arrested 13 suspects and freed two victims.
All 13 suspects and two victims are currently being held at the Chroy Changvar Military District for further questioning. Minister of Information Presides Over a Meeting to Celebrate the 45th Anniversary of the Birth of the United Front for the Development of Motherland Cambodia, December 2, 1978-December 2, 2023
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Neth Pheaktra, Minister of Information and Chairman of the Front Committee of the Ministry of Information, together with the leaders of civil servants, celebrated the 45th anniversary of the birth of the United Front for the Development of Motherland Cambodia from December 2, 1978 to December 2, 2023. Held on the afternoon of December 1, 2023 at Chaktomuk Mongkul Hall, Ministry of Information.
Mith Tinh celebrates the anniversary of the birth of the United Front for the Development of the Motherland of Cambodia on December 2, a day to commemorate the first day of solidarity between the patriotic forces working to liberate Cambodia after the Khmer Rouge regime of Pol Pot.
The 2 December Front not only saved the lives of the people from the catastrophe of the Black Shirt regime, but also helped to rebuild and develop the motherland of Cambodia to a new face until peace, national unity and development like Today.
Along with the inauguration of the 2 December Front, the people gathered on the outskirts of the city, which had just been liberated from the genocidal regime of Pol Pot, in order to ensure their livelihood by cultivating agricultural products.
Minister Neth Pheaktra recalled the history of the creation of December 2 If there were no December 2, there would be no January 7, December 2 and January 7 are the foundations that led Cambodia out of the genocidal regime. The Khmer Rouge and we can build a nation together for development and peace to this day.
The leadership of the Ministry of Information would like to express our deep gratitude to the leadership of the Cambodian People's Party, Samdech Akka Moha Pothisal Chea Sim, Samdech Akka Moha Ponhea Chakrei Heng Samrin and Samdech Akka Moha Sena Padei Techo Hun Sen, as well as all the female warriors who Strive for the liberation of the nation and pay tribute to those who sacrificed their lives for the cause of national liberation and the cause of national defense and development.
On that occasion, the Minister of Information asked the people, youth and all civil servants of the Ministry of Information to always remember the spirit of December 2, which is a great national unity force in liberating the country from the Khmer Rouge regime. All of this is the basis of a historical lesson for us to lead the country and protect the peace that Cambodia has.
Starting from the base of 2 December, which brings peace to Cambodia, which until now, from 1998 to 2023 for 25 years and will continue to protect for a long time for the next generation. Opportunity to protect and develop the nation is growing stronger.
Behind the peace and development that the nation and the people of Cambodia have today is full of all the sacrifices of the youth and the previous generation! In the past, Cambodia has gone through countless tragedies, millions of Cambodians have lost their lives and they are fighting for the revival of their nation and people! The sacrifices of previous generations have borne fruit today!
The Cambodian people know exactly where Cambodia is currently coming from and exactly where Cambodia is going to move forward in order to maintain the developed peace that the Cambodian people are enjoying. The next generation of Cambodians will always remember the sacrifices of the previous generation and remember the true history of the sacrifices of the Cambodian ancestors.
National Assembly President Khuon Sodary Asks Vietnam to Boost Tourists and Attract More Investors to Cambodia
(VOVworld) - National Assembly President Khuon Sodary has asked the President of the Socialist Republic of Vietnam to encourage more Vietnamese tourists and investors to visit and invest in Cambodia.
National Assembly President Khuon Sodary said that the trade volume between the two countries has reached 10 billion US dollars, which is a proud size. As for tourism, the Vietnamese population is high among foreign tourists visiting Cambodia, but due to the 19-year-old disease, the number of Vietnamese tourists has declined. He hopes that after the Kovid 19 crisis, Vietnamese people will return to Cambodia and investment will increase.
At the same time, the National Assembly President also asked the Vietnamese side to promote and accelerate the connection between the two countries as soon as possible.
Mr. Vu Van Thuong praised the visit of the National Assembly President to Vietnam on this occasion, which not only strengthened the cooperation between the two parliaments, but also played an important role in enhancing relations. And deepen, long-term and sustainable cooperation in all fields between the two countries.
He welcomed the remarks made by the National Assembly President and stressed that Vietnam hopes to import more agricultural products from Cambodia and increase Cambodia's purchases of industrial products from Vietnam. He stressed that progress between the two countries is inseparable.
Mr. Vu Van Thuong informed the National Assembly that Vietnam is preparing to welcome the upcoming visit of His Excellency Hun Manet to Vietnam. President Hun Manet's presence in Vietnam is believed by the President to have more and in-depth discussions on strengthening friendship and cooperation in all fields, including trade and road connectivity. Also original.
Please be informed that the National Assembly President Khuon Sodary, President of the National Assembly, led a high-level delegation of the National Assembly to pay a three-day visit to Vietnam from November 30 to December 2, 2023 with the aim of strengthening institutional cooperation. The legislature and the executive branch between the two countries should be strengthened.
