Minister Tho Chetha Attends Inter-Ministerial Meeting to Discuss Flood Solutions Mechanism and Identify Priority Areas
(Phnom Penh): At the office of the Ministry of Land Management, Urban Planning and Construction, on the afternoon of Friday, December 4, 2023, Mr. Tho Chetha, Minister of Water Resources and Meteorology, accompanied by leaders and officials. Experts attended an inter-ministerial meeting to discuss flood resolution mechanisms across the country, prioritization of flood-affected areas and mechanisms for resolving the Stung Prek Tnaot flood.
The meeting was chaired by Mr. Say Sam Al, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Land Management, Urban Planning and Construction, and attended by Mr. Peng Por Nea, Minister of Public Works and Transport, Mr. Chhay Rithy Sen, Minister of Rural Development and Mr. Keut Chhe, Deputy Governor of Phnom Penh Capital Hall. And the leadership of each ministry.
To begin with, Minister Tho Chetha addressed the meeting on the general situation of floods across the country last year and the floods in 2023, which caused damage to water infrastructure, road infrastructure and hindered economic activities and the general situation of Stung Prek Tnaot floods, along with the measures taken to reduce floods.
Regarding the delimitation of floodplains in rivers and streams, the Minister said that the Ministry of Water Resources and Meteorology has followed the high-level recommendations of His Excellency Hun Manet, Prime Minister of the Kingdom of Cambodia. 2) flooded areas and receding and 3) flooded areas due to various developments.
The Minister stated that the Ministry has identified floodplains in the Stung Prek Tnaot basin to reduce flooding, which causes damage to infrastructure, property, economic activities and people's lives in Kampong Speu, Kandal, Takeo and south of Phnom Penh. .
Finally, the Minister mentioned the infrastructure measures as a solution to reduce floods 1) Continue to develop the reservoir in the upper part 2) Continue to rehabilitate and build flood defenses in the central part and 3) Continue to rehabilitate and build infrastructure Remove flooding at the bottom, along with non-infrastructure measures, discuss and accept recommendations from relevant institutions.
