The Royal Government issues a sub-decree on the organization and functioning of the General Secretariat of the National Authority for Dispute Resolution
(Phnom Penh): The Prime Minister of Cambodia, Samdech Moha Bovathi Hun Manet, has decided to establish a General Secretariat to operate the work of the National Authority for Dispute Resolution outside the Judiciary.
It should be noted that on November 2, 2023, the King signed the establishment of the National Authority to resolve disputes out of court.
According to the Royal Decree, the National Dispute Resolution Authority is a complementary mechanism to the Dispute Resolution System in the Kingdom of Cambodia, which aims to improve the quality, efficiency and speed of dispute resolution through out-of-court mediation and reduce disputes. Congestion of cases to ensure harmony in society.
