(Phnom Penh): Mr. Keo Rattanak, Minister of Mines and Energy, emphasized that clean electricity, which is energy from hydropower, solar and wind, not only helps the planet's environment, but also contributes to attracting investment to Cambodia. Well.
Unclean electricity or electricity that affects the environment to the planet is being eliminated by the world together. In this sense, products made with unclean electricity will also be under pressure from buyers. They will not support products made with unclean energy as part of a campaign to protect the environment or save the planet. For this reason, producers, before investing in any country, will also check the condition of the power source.
Mr. Keo Rattanak explained, "Investors are under pressure from consumers. For example, when we make clothes, bicycles, shoes for the world market, consumers in Japan, the United States, Central America and other continents want to contribute to global warming. "So they want to buy products that come from clean energy."
Under this trend, Mr. Keo Rattanak claimed that Cambodia's goal of producing 70% clean energy by 2030 will contribute to attracting investors to Cambodia.
"If Cambodia pushes clean energy to 70 percent, this is a new hope," he said. It means attracting investment to produce in Cambodia, because if you go to a country that uses a lot of unclean energy, they do not want to buy difficult marketing. Therefore, only a few years ago, because our energy is already 62 percent clean, so we see that a lot of garment factories are continuing to invest in Cambodia.
It should be noted that by the end of 2022, Cambodia can produce up to 4,495.42 megawatts of electricity. Of that, 62 percent is clean energy from hydropower and solar.
