Of the six priority policies announced by the President at the first session of the Council of Ministers on August 24, 2023, the first is to "expand health care services towards global health coverage." With this in mind, three key measures have been put in place to improve the quality of health care, with a focus on strengthening local primary health care capacity, including:
* First: Strengthening the capacity to provide services at health centers and referral hospitals, focusing on the deployment of all staff with good ethics and proper training, supply of medicines, equipment and medical equipment, infrastructure improvements. And the use of digital information technology / health.
* Second, developing the capacity of national and sub-national health institutions to manage human resources and finance, regulatory work, responding to public health threats and health emergencies, and providing health care services in a more responsive manner. High equity and accountability, as well as improving the efficiency of institutional functions
* Third: Building a strong partnership between the public and private health sectors to ensure that people have access to high quality, safe and effective health care services. The Ministry of Health has implemented these three key measures, achieving remarkable results.
