Progress Report on the Implementation of Key Measures in the Education Sector by the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports During the First Meeting of the Council of Ministers of the 7th Legislature of the National Assembly on August 24, 2023, the Prime Minister of the Kingdom of Cambodia issued four key measures. To strengthen the quality of public educational institutions from kindergarten to secondary school.
The key measures include: First, strengthening school governance, Second: Reviewing and revising curricula and extracurricular activities to strengthen students' knowledge, discipline, ethics and behavior, and Third: Health care. Of students and fourth: state-community partnerships to promote education.
The Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports also reviewed the previous school standards, integrating the four key measures into five "model school standards" for kindergarten through secondary school, focusing on student achievement, teaching and learning. Learn community involvement, school operations and administration, and school accountability.
The Royal Government has established a National Committee to promote the implementation of key measures, chaired by the Prime Minister, accompanied by a composition of 16 Deputy Prime Ministers, Senior Ministers and the Governors of the Capital and Provincial Governors.
It should be noted that the Royal Government of Cambodia has agreed in principle to implement the "Model School Standards" and the "Samdech Moha Bovathibodi Model School Award" as well as the "Clean School Campaign Without Garbage" Nationwide from the 2023-2024 school year in The model school standards will be implemented and strengthened from the new school year onwards.
What is a model school? Model schools are fully functional schools, including:
First, the school is accountable to the community and improves the school in accordance with the model school standards, with the participation of all stakeholders, especially parents or guardians, through the establishment and operation of school management committees and classroom management committees.
Second, the school has autonomy in planning and improving schools and classrooms, as well as providing regular professional development to school management and teachers.
Third, the school implements standardized tests on a regular basis and uses the results of standardized tests to improve teaching and learning, assisting students with learning delays, and provide information to parents or guardians and the community for additional support.
Fourth, schools have the autonomy to implement curricula and extracurricular programs, focusing on youth development programs, traffic law education programs, volunteer work, community work, and moral education.
Fifth, the school pays attention to education, health, hygiene, clean environment, the school is free of litter and considers the nutrition of the students, and sixth, the promotion of the participation of parents or guardians and the community in supporting and developing the school. During the new school year 2023-2024, the Ministry will select 500 potential model schools to receive support and evaluation, expected to meet the standard school standards within two years.
The Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports is committed to the successful implementation of the Samdech's initiative in the next two years, turning at least 500 to 1,000 institutions into model schools, starting with the organization of schools. Learn the model for the announcement at the education conference scheduled to be held in April 2024 for 50 to 100 schools.
