At the same time, in the process of reviewing, discussing and approving the draft National Policy on Intellectual Property 2024-2028, Samdech President Hun Manet stated that this national policy is also in the Royal Government's Pentagon Strategy. Therefore, Samdech requested the Office of the Council of Ministers to provide coordination to make this policy a success.
Please be informed that the draft National Policy on Intellectual Property 2024-2028 has the vision of developing the intellectual property system of the Kingdom of Cambodia to become a driving force in the development of economy, trade, industry, culture, tourism and agriculture in response to the economic and social context of digital and revolution. The fourth generation industry will contribute to achieving the vision of the Kingdom of Cambodia 2050.
This draft policy was drafted through eight meetings of the Secretariat of the National Intellectual Property Management Committee and one consultation meeting with the participation of representatives of the Small and Medium Enterprises Association of Cambodia, the Intellectual Property Association of Cambodia, and the Women Entrepreneurs Association. Cambodia Chamber of Commerce and University of Research Science.
This draft policy has three main objectives, including:
* First, prepare laws and legal documents related to intellectual property in accordance with international standards and strengthen the implementation of intellectual property laws to meet the needs of the economy, society and development.
* Second, strengthen and enhance the capacity of officials and units to implement the intellectual property system to support socio-economic development.
* Third, disseminate and promote public knowledge on the use of intellectual property in the development of small and medium enterprises to promote the economy, trade, science and technology.
