(Phnom Penh): Mr. Keo Rattanak, Minister of Mines and Energy, said that His Excellency Hun Manet, Prime Minister of Cambodia, is highly committed to making Cambodia a model country in producing clean energy, while currently Cambodia has higher clean energy than ASEAN member countries. Other.
Clean energy is renewable energy, such as energy from water, sunlight, and wind. The world is working together to set high energy production goals to help the environment and the planet.
Currently, Cambodia has up to 62 percent clean energy and has ambitions to produce up to 70 percent clean energy by 2030.
To achieve this ambition, at the Closing Ceremony of the Stung Ta Tai Leu Dam in Thmar Bang District, Koh Kong Province, on November 30, 2023, the Prime Minister of Cambodia set out a number of policies, including stopping the construction of coal-fired power plants. , Do not allow the construction of hydropower across the Mekong River, cancel the project of a 700-megawatt coal-fired power plant in Darasakor in Koh Kong province.
The decision by Hun Manet comes as the United Nations convenes a high-level meeting on climate change COP-28 in Dubai.
Mr. Keo Rattanak called the decision of President Hun Manet as a model for the world, while the world is meeting on environmental issues and clean energy production, but Cambodia has already taken action.
Mr. Keo Rattanak emphasized, "When the world wants to do more clean energy, Cambodia is doing it here, this is a message. This commitment shows that Cambodia, under the leadership of Samdech Hun Manet, not only wants enough energy to boost the economy and livelihood of the Cambodian people, but also to contribute responsibly to protect Our earth, too. ”
The Minister of Mines and Energy also said that the creation of clean energy not only helps the environment and the planet, but also helps attract investment to Cambodia.
