The following is the statement of the Coalition of Civil Society Organizations: The Ministry of Inspection and the Bar Association signed an agreement to improve the implementation of the Labor Law, inspect and resolve complaints.
(Phnom Penh): To raise legal awareness and ensure the effectiveness of the inspection work, monitor the implementation of the law in resolving extrajudicial disputes by the victorious policy of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the former Prime Minister, and succeeded by His Excellency Hun Manet. According to the first pentagonal strategy, for the past 100 days, the Ministry of Inspection and the Bar Association of the Kingdom of Cambodia have jointly signed a Memorandum of Understanding.
The signing ceremony of the Memorandum of Understanding between the Ministry of Inspection and the Bar Association of the Kingdom of Cambodia was held on the afternoon of November 30, 2023, presided over by Mr. Huot Hak, Minister of Inspection and Mr. Ly Chantola, President of the Bar Association of the Kingdom of Cambodia. Cambodia at the Ministry of Inspection.
Regarding the Memorandum of Understanding as well as the cooperation between the Ministry of Inspection and the Bar Association of the Kingdom of Cambodia, Mr. Ly Chantola stated that this is an initiative to participate in the work of raising legal awareness, especially understanding on Inspection areas such as receiving complaints and resolving people's complaints.
Mr. Ly Chantola added that through this memorandum, the Bar Association can provide lawyers to help protect the poor who need a lawyer through the Ministry of Inspection. The work of the Bar Association also includes mechanisms for participation in outreach, as well as various training courses related to the field of inspection.
The President of the Bar Association stated that within the framework of the cooperation of the Memorandum of Understanding, the Bar Association provided 5 lawyers to assist in the work related to the mission of the Ministry of Inspection, but if necessary to help resolve disputes, the Bar Association will Add more lawyers. In providing a lawyer to help solve this, there is no fee, it is an offer to help the work of the Ministry of Inspection.
Mr. Ly Chantola said that another important work is internal training for both lawyers and officials of the Ministry of Inspection, we train each other, the Bar Association provides technical assistance in resolving various complaints, and the Ministry of Inspection can share Share experience and knowledge related to the field of inspection.
