The United States on Nov. 30 announced new sanctions against North Korea in connection with Pyongyang's recent launch of a spy satellite, claiming that the launch was a practice. The Ministry of Agriculture will organize agricultural communities so that cashew cultivation can be done at a price acceptable to both farmers and collectors.
(Kratie): The Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries has set out a policy of agricultural communities to ensure that cashew cultivation is at a price acceptable to both farmers and collectors. This was confirmed by Ms. M. Rachana, Undersecretary of State and spokesperson for the Ministry of Agriculture.
This statement was made on the occasion of the Ministry of Agriculture and the European Union organized a four-day study tour of cashew production chain in Cambodia in Kampong Thom, Kratie and Stung Treng provinces from the 29th. November to December 2, 2023.
Ms. M. Rachana stated, "We have set an important policy in this mandate, we are organized as an agricultural community to connect cashew cultivation, both farmers and collectors to the supply of seeds. "Cashew nuts are in proportion and at a price that is acceptable to all."
The spokesman for the Ministry of Agriculture emphasized that in implementing this mechanism, the ministry will bring together farmers who grow crops in a single community and operate as a company.
At the same time, Ms. Rachana also said that the Ministry of Agriculture, the Ministry of Commerce and related institutions are continuing to attract investors to invest in Cambodia after the agricultural community works well, which can ensure the supply of raw materials. As well as processing processed products to investors.
Mr. Toch Bun Hour, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, emphasized that cashew is an industrial crop with high potential for Cambodia and has a good reputation, especially in the market for its quality, taste, size, seeds and traditional organic.
Mr. Toch Bun Hour added that cashews are easy to grow compared to other crops. Cashews need less water for drought-resistant growth, suitable for the climate and topography in Cambodia.
Currently, the provinces that grow the most cashews are Kampong Cham, Tbong Khmum, Kampong Thom, Kratie, Mondulkiri, Ratanakiri, Stung Treng, Preah Vihear, Oddar Meanchey, Siem Reap and Kampong Chhnang. According to the assessment, Cambodia has about 2.38 million hectares of suitable land for cashew cultivation.
Mr. Toch Bun Hour said that although the cashew sub-sector has achieved proud results and developed significantly, the sub-sector still faces some major challenges, such as:
Cambodia is now importing raw cashew nuts to neighboring countries at lower prices than expected. The Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries has examined what benefits Cambodia will receive in exchange for domestic processing for export, increasing value added and creating jobs for local workers.
In addition, Mr. Touch Bun Hour stated that currently Cambodia exports about 90 percent of raw cashew nuts and about 5 percent of domestic processing.
Please be informed that in the first 10 months of 2023, Cambodia exported more than 610,000 tons of raw cashew nuts, earning 831 million US dollars, a decrease of nearly 16.7% compared to the same period in 2022. Ministry of Public Works holds a meeting of the Steering Committee for Decentralization and Deconcentration Reform
