Below is a video of the Candlelight Party activists: National Assembly President Khuon Sodary visits the Socialist Republic of Vietnam
(Phnom Penh) - The National Assembly President of the Kingdom of Cambodia, HE Khuon Sodary, President of the National Assembly of Cambodia, paid a three-day official and friendly visit to the Socialist Republic of Vietnam on Thursday afternoon, November 30, 2023. . The visit will take place from November 30 to December 2, 2023 at the invitation of National Assembly President VUONG Dinh Hue.
The visit is aimed at strengthening the traditional and fraternal ties of cooperation between Cambodia and Vietnam, which are strong and long-lasting in all aspects, both in the legislative and executive branches.
Within the framework of the National Assembly, the two countries, Cambodia and Vietnam, have good relations and cooperation with each other at all levels and always exchange visits with each other at the level of leaders, expert committees, friendship groups and the General Secretariat. In the field of diplomacy, the National Assembly of Cambodia and Vietnam have supported each other in many other inter-parliamentary forums, such as AIPA, IPU, APPF, and APF.
Government Spokesperson: Cambodia is a small country, but its leaders are committed to protecting the environment
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Pen Bona, Spokesman of the Royal Government, noted that the development policy of the country associated with high consideration for the environment, which the Prime Minister announced today, reflects the strong will of the Royal Government in its commitment to development. Sustainable country by paying attention to the impact on the environment.
A spokesman for the Royal Government of Cambodia recalled that from Koh Kong province today, Cambodian Prime Minister Hun Manet announced a clear position that the country's development must take into account three important factors:
First, to promote the national economic growth and improve the living standards of the people, especially the people in the community who benefit from the development first.
Second, pay close attention to the impact, especially the impact on the environment, people and animals.
Third, contribute to the world in preventing climate change.
To reaffirm this strong will, Samdech Thipdey also publicly announced the cessation of the 700-megawatt coal-fired power plant development project in Koh Kong province's Botum Sakor district, instead of the LNG project.
At the same time, the Prime Minister also announced that the Royal Government of Cambodia will not build hydropower on the Mekong River to avoid environmental and ecological impacts along the river.
According to Mr. Pen Bona, although electricity is a necessary need for Cambodia to develop the country, the Royal Government is willing to choose a source of electricity that does not harm the environment. This is an exemplary decision that Cambodia has presented to the world on sustainable development, taking into account the environment and its impacts.
Therefore, it can be said that Cambodia is a small country, but the Cambodian leaders are very willing to develop the country by considering the interests of the people in connection with the consideration of the environment.
Minister of Environment Strengthens Cooperation with Cuba to Promote Cambodia's Environment
The Cuban ambassador said that today's meeting is to strengthen bilateral cooperation between the Ministry of Environment and the Ministry of Institutes and Environment in Cuba to promote the environment.
In response, Dr. Eang Sophalleth, Minister of the Environment, thanked and warmly welcomed the bilateral cooperation between the Ministry and the Cuban Environment Institute for their attention in the field of environment.
Of course, the environment is a global issue that can not be overlooked, so in the first 100 days of the Minister of Environment, he set out a chakra strategy with three priorities: clean, green and sustainable.
In addition, the Minister praised Cuba for its contribution to the development of various sectors in Cambodia, including health, agriculture and other potential sectors. 130 people with disabilities receive consultation and treatment from Techo Santepheap National Hospital
(Phnom Penh): 130 people with visual and physical disabilities received medical treatment from Techo Santepheap National Hospital to celebrate the Day of Persons with Disabilities on December 4, 2023 under the presidency The Most High Samdech Samdech Moha Bovathip Hun Manet, Prime Minister of Cambodia.
On the morning of Thursday, November 30, 2023, at the National Hospital of Techo Santepheap, Ministry of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation, the Ministry of Women's Affairs cooperated with the Ministry of Health for medical examination and treatment. To the visually impaired at the Techo Santepheap National Hospital, 130 people with disabilities came for examination and treatment at the Techo Santepheap National Hospital.
Mr. Chap To brought a message from the Minister of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation, Mr. Chea Somethy, and made a briefing to the ceremony, stating that currently there are a number of people with disabilities. 288,690 people have been identified by commune focal points across the country, and the ministry has produced 222,148 ID cards for people with disabilities.
The Undersecretary of State added that in the past, under the wise and skillful leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, President of the Supreme Council of the King and Samdech Moha Bovathip Hun Manet, Prime Minister of the Kingdom of Cambodia, the people have been blinded. And fitness in Cambodia is really lucky to be destined to receive education, vocational training and high attention, which is the foundation of promoting the rights of people with disabilities in Cambodia.
Ms. Nhem Morakot requested in principle permission from the Minister of Health through Ms. Youk Sambath to give priority to people with disabilities to come to all public hospitals for health check-ups and treatment without discrimination.
The NATO Foreign Ministers' Meeting, which was also attended by the Ukrainian Foreign Ministers, concluded its two-day meeting in Brussels, Belgium, on November 29. The meeting expressed support for Ukraine and the holding of an upcoming summit in Washington, DC.
The NATO foreign ministers' meeting also focused on one point in pushing Ukraine to become a member of NATO. The talks made recommendations on the need for priority reforms in Ukraine, including the fight against corruption, the strengthening of the rule of law, and support for human rights and minority rights.
