About 500 people attended the job forum and immediately applied for job interviews with company representatives and the four factories.
Mr. Nak Sovannary, Governor of Chhouk District, Kampot Province, said that such a forum for recruiting local workers is very valuable because it helps people to have the opportunity to know about employment information in the country, and another can help them. Met with the company in person as well. He added that the forum contributes to reducing unemployment at the local level and helps meet the needs of people in need of employment.
The district governor thanked the NEA of the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training for organizing this forum and requested that this important program be organized more often to help the people, especially the people living in Chhouk district. This is to make it easier to get a decent job in the country.
"This forum is very meaningful for both the company and the people who want to find a job, so that we can easily meet in one place," said Ms. Hai Rang, a recruitment officer at AL Rural Credit Operations. Apply and interview immediately. For AL, we have brought many job opportunities and positions to participate in today's job forum.
Ms. Moeun Sokhon, a resident of Sra Nge village, Boeung Nimol commune, Chhouk district, said that she was very happy that the Ministry of Labor had organized a job forum today. She would like to thank the NEA of the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training for always taking into account the well-being of the people by helping people find jobs locally.
Please be informed that in addition to providing immediate job opportunities at the job forum in Chhouk district, there is also the registration of young people from poor and vulnerable families to attend vocational and technical training courses.
(Koh Kong): Mr. Chhay Rithi Sen, Minister of Rural Development, on the afternoon of November 30, 2023, met with the leaders and civil servants of the Department of Rural Development of Koh Kong Province, urging the leaders and officials to take care of the achievements and Existing works and continue to increase new works with the Royal Government of the 7th mandate.
The Minister stated that in order to contribute to the implementation of the Royal Government's Pentagon Strategy and Vision 2030 and 2050, the Ministry of Rural Development has strived to achieve its vision of improving the quality and values of the people in rural areas, both economically and socially. And culture.
The Minister informed the four priority strategies of the Ministry of Rural Development:
First, to develop the physical and transportation infrastructure that the Ministry has been managing for more than 50,000 kilometers, by striving to upgrade these roads from red gravel roads to paved roads and concrete roads that are resistant to climate change to cause Characteristics for people traveling to receive public services and transportation in all seasons.
Second, improve the living conditions of rural communities through the supply of clean water and household toilets in order to enable people in rural areas to live healthily, change their attitudes, adopt good hygiene, and live in a comfortable environment.
Third, diversify rural economic activities through the training of basic skills and life skills to create additional jobs and occupations other than agriculture in order to increase household economic income in rural areas.
Fourth, to strengthen the institution, that is, to strengthen the capacity of civil servants, to lead with discipline, to have a meeting system to find the strengths and weaknesses in the unit, and to set action plans to meet the needs of the local people.
On that occasion, the Minister instructed the leaders and civil servants of the Provincial Department of Rural Development as follows:
* Maintain the achievements and achievements of the past as a basis and must continue to increase new achievements to contribute to achieving the vision of Cambodia to make people with high middle income in 2030 and high income in 2050.
* The department must strive to fulfill its role as a good and honest staff to the provincial administration and cooperate well with the relevant departments and authorities at all levels to promote better rural development.
* The department shall regularly review the monthly, quarterly, semi-annual meeting schedule to evaluate the work based on the principle of collective opinion.
* Department leaders must encourage civil servants through promotions, ranks, medals or other means.
* Must have good internal unity, do not take sides, take care of civil servants with disabilities, civil servants who are pregnant or have small children.
* The department must establish a group of spokespersons of the department to provide information in order to participate in disseminating the achievements and achievements of the Royal Government as well as the Ministry of Rural Development to the general public.
Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen Donates Money to Poor A-Level Student On Phanit whose Parents Have Disabilities and Livelihoods
(Phnom Penh): The Mother of Humanity Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, President of the Cambodian Red Cross, on November 30, 2023, donated some money to a poor A-level student named On Phanit whose parents have disabilities and living in poverty in the village. Prey Thom, Ang Phnom Touch Commune, Angkor Chey District, Kampot Province.
The donation was made at the CRC headquarters in the presence of Ms. Men Neary Sopheak, First Deputy Secretary General of the Cambodian Red Cross.
On that occasion, Ms. Men Neary Sopheak met and encouraged On Phanit students.
At the same time, he also conveyed the greetings of Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen to On Phanit: "Even though you are poor, your parents are disabled, you have the will and the will to learn. "Parents work hard and study hard until they pass the exam (A)."
She stressed that the Royal Government of the 7th legislature of the National Assembly has set out a pentagonal strategy - the first phase has an angle, focusing on the development of human capital, human resources with high capacity, knowledge, clear skills and good health. Therefore, please, On Phanit, as well as other young people, adhere to morality, virtue, gratitude and continue to strive to learn well to become a good human resource of the nation in the future.
In response, On Phanith students and family representatives would like to express our deepest gratitude to Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen and Samdech Techo Hun Sen for their consideration and encouragement, as well as for providing funds for further study and Pray for the sacred objects in the world by nurturing and caring for both Samdech and his family. May you receive the four blessings of the Buddha: age, class, happiness, and strength.
