OECD warns of declining global economic risks
According to Bloomberg, the Paris-based organization sees economic growth slowing in many countries and will not recover until 2025, when real revenues recover from the crisis. Inflation and central banks will start reducing borrowing costs.
The OECD said risks to the forecast were shifting as geopolitical tensions escalated, uncertain outlook for trade and risks that tight monetary policy could be stronger than expected. Leave it to the company, consumer costs and jobs.
The gloomy outlook stems from the global inflation crisis, the Kovid-19 pandemic and rising energy prices after Russia's attack on Ukraine.
India approves $ 142 billion food aid for 800 million people
The approval comes weeks after Indian Prime Minister Narendra Modi vowed to continue the food subsidy program to protect consumers from rising food prices.
Under the food subsidy program, which began for the first time during an epidemic, about 800 million Indians receive five kilograms of wheat or rice each month. The plan is very popular and widely praised for helping the ruling Bharatiya Janata Party win elections in several states last year.
The Indian government has restricted the export of wheat, rice and sugar to maintain domestic supply of essential foodstuffs. To attract voters, Modi's government has also increased subsidies on cooking gas and fertilizers. The government is also considering other supportive measures, such as increasing the provision of cash to small farmers and low-interest mortgages. According to Bloomberg News.
