(Phnom Penh): Dr. Sar Sokha, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Interior, has instructed the Capital-Provincial Board of Governors to waive the payment of fees and expedite the provision of certain administrative services at the municipal, district, Khan and commune administrations that serve for land registration. To the people.
In a letter from the Ministry of Interior, received by Fresh News on the afternoon of November 30, 2023, stated that the Ministry of Land Management, Urban Planning and Construction has set land registration for people as a priority and must be implemented. Completed throughout the country in order to guarantee land ownership, strengthen the security of land tenure for social harmony, reduce poverty and develop the family economy and society.
First, instruct the Commune / Sangkat Administration within its jurisdiction to prepare and issue an order on the exemption of service fees for the application for land history certificate and heir certificate until the land registration is completed in each commune / sangkat.
Second: Introduce all municipal, district, Khan and commune administrations to pay close attention to providing administrative services that provide land registration to the people quickly and timely.
At the same time, the Capital and Provincial Administration shall assign working groups to support, monitor and evaluate on a regular basis on the implementation of this work, as well as to make specific reports to the General Department of Administration, Ministry of Interior.
This morning, Samdech President Hun Manet chaired a plenary meeting of the Council of Ministers to discuss and cross four agendas.
(Phnom Penh): On the morning of Friday, December 1, 2023, Samdech Moha Bovathibodi Hun Manet, Prime Minister of Cambodia, chaired a plenary meeting of the Council of Ministers to discuss and cross four agendas.
According to Mr. Pen Bona, spokesman for the Royal Government of Cambodia, tomorrow's cabinet meeting has the following agenda:
