Project to expand and improve the quality of National Road 33, achieving 35.99% progress
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Pal Chandara, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Public Works and Transport and Manager of National Road 33 Expansion and Quality Improvement Project, on the afternoon of November 30, 2023, chaired a working group meeting on road construction progress. National No. 33, with the participation of experts from relevant units and technical working groups of China Bridge and Road Corporation (CRBC) and representatives of Guangzhou Wang An Technical Advisory Company.
The purpose of this meeting was to review the progress of the construction work and to check the technical work to ensure that the National Road 33 project is implemented in accordance with the correct quality standards and is completed as planned.
On that occasion, the Secretary of State instructed the company to pay more attention to the work of watering, clearing the pit, keeping the safety at the site by putting up warning signs, traffic signs and safety devices properly to facilitate Travel of the people, especially the location in Kep and the location for the upcoming Sea Festival.
Please be informed that by the end of November 2023, the project to expand and improve the quality of National Road 33 has achieved 35.99% progress.
