Taiwan, a democracy that China claims as one of its provinces, has been complaining for the past four years about regular Chinese patrols and military exercises near the island.
Taiwan will hold a new presidential election on January 13, and the election campaign is fully operational. Relations with China are at the heart of the conflict.
As of Thursday morning, it had spotted J-10 and J-16 fighter jets as well as cruise helicopters operating near central Taiwan and the southwestern part of the island, the Defense Ministry said.
The ministry added that 11 of the planes crossed the Taiwan Strait or nearby areas, working with Chinese warships to carry out "joint combat patrols."
The strait of the Taiwan Strait used to be an unofficial barrier between the two sides, but now Chinese planes regularly fly through the strait. Photo by Reuters Crossing 4 agendas
(Phnom Penh): On the morning of Friday, December 1, 2023, tomorrow, Samdech Moha Bovathibodi Hun Manet, Prime Minister of Cambodia, will chair a plenary meeting of the Council of Ministers to discuss and cross four agendas.
First, a report on the progress of the implementation of key measures in the education sector. Second, a report on the progress of the preparation and implementation of key measures in the health sector. Third: The draft national policy on intellectual property 2024-2028. Fourth: Other issues. Follow the instructions of Samdech Techo Hun Sen! General Kheng Samet and Mr. Mao Thunin inspect the construction site of a house for the family of On Phanit
(Kampot): Following the instructions of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Chairman of the King's Personal Advisory Council, on November 30, 2023, Director General Kheng Samet, Deputy Commissioner of the National Police and Governor of Kampot Province, Mr. Mao Thunin, led the team. Officials and stakeholders inspect the construction site of the house for the family of On Phanit students.
This house is a gift from Samdech Techo Hun Sen to the family of On Phanith, a student who failed the exam and received an A grade from Chea Sim Angkor Chey High School in Prey Thom village, Ang Phnom Touch commune, Angkor Chey district, Kampot province. There are also parents with disabilities.
On that occasion, General Kheng Samet said that after receiving instructions from Samdech Techo Hun Sen to help build a new house for the family of poor students on Phanit yesterday allowed him to lead the team. Lead the relevant team to inspect and study the actual location to prepare to build a new house for the family of this young student in the near future.
Provincial Governor Mao Thunin said that Samdech Techo Hun Sen always cares about the well-being of the poor people, especially the poor students, who always have the support and support for education. Always learn.
In fact, the support for the students of On Phanit now is a show of generosity and high attention to the students who live in poverty, make it difficult for them to study hard to support their family life as well as serve the country. Nation and people of Cambodia.
Ms. Top Makara, the mother of On Phanit students, as well as her husband and children, also expressed their happiness and gratitude to Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Samdech Kittiprittbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen for their generosity. Provide support for your child's education as well as provide a new home, other support to families who are experiencing difficulties.
According to the words of Samdech Techo Hun Sen on November 29, 2023, Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Samdech Kittipritthbandit help support further education and family life, including:
1. Help to get engineering education in college, which is the dream profession of Anphanit students, along with providing transportation as well as monthly stipend to study.
2. Received accommodation at the bodyguard headquarters through General Hing Bun Heang.
3. The two princes sent their personal advisers, Mr. Seng Teang and General Kheng Samet, to help build a new house for the family.
5. Monthly donation of 1 million Riels to the families of On Phanit students to facilitate their lives.
