(Phnom Penh): November 29, 2023 is the 100th day of the inauguration of the Royal Government of the 7th mandate of the National Assembly under the leadership of Samdech Thibodi Hun Manat, Prime Minister of Cambodia.
In the past, the Ministers of Ministries and Institutions have fulfilled their duties according to their respective action plans with energy and high will in accordance with the Royal Decree dated 22 August 2023 on the appointment of the Royal Government of the Kingdom of Cambodia. .
In this seventh mandate, the Ministry of Information under the leadership of Mr. Neth Pheaktra has set the vision for the next five years: to transform the Ministry of Information into a "proactive, public relations institution of the Royal Government." Efficiency and effectiveness ”to manage the information space and information security in Cambodia. The introduction and implementation of this vision is consistent with and supports the Royal Government of Cambodia's Pentagon strategy.
At the same time, the flow of information and work is guaranteed to be revitalized between the leaders of all ministries, general departments and departments in the capital and provinces with a spirit of cooperation, solidarity and high attention.
The following is a press release from the Office of the Spokesperson of the Ministry of Information: The Public Works Department of Preah Vihear Province continues to call on the people who have not yet demolished the construction on the road to be removed while the team is repairing, expanding and constructing the drainage system on National Road 62.
(Preah Vihear): Mr. Samleang Try, Director of Preah Vihear Provincial Department of Public Works and Transport, appealed to the people living on both sides of National Road No. 62 from km 67 + 950 to km 68 + 500 in Phnom Dek village, Romney commune. Rovieng district needs to be demolished while his team is working on the above location.
The Director of Preah Vihear Provincial Department of Public Works stated on November 30, 2023 that the Department will repair and widen the section of National Road No. 62 with 550 meters long DBST pavement, 5 meters wide width and 60 meters long branch road. Install 880 meters of drainage along the road, install 0.8 meters of drainage along the road, 450 meters in length and 17 rugs at the above location.
Mr. Samleang Try added that before the team started repairing, widening the road and installing the drainage system at the above location, the department as well as the Rovieng district authority made a notice to the people living on both sides of the road. Participate in dismantling other structures that have been built in violation of the access road.
While the team was working, the Director of the Public Works Department of Preah Vihear Province also expressed his deep gratitude to some people who participated in the demolition of buildings that encroached on the road.
He would like to appeal once again to a small number of people who have not yet participated in dismantling the structures that encroached on the road, please help to dismantle so that the repair, expansion and installation of sewers at the above location can run easily and quickly. .
Agricultural experts want to see more cashew nut processing in Cambodia for export to international markets
(Phnom Penh): Dr. Thorn Vathana, Director of the Prek Leap National Institute of Agriculture and a Reserve Member of the Royal Academy of Cambodia, would like to see more cashew nuts processed in Cambodia for export to international markets, while the current cashew remnants. There is a market for processing into other products and so on.
Cambodia is a country with great potential for growing cashews, on the other hand, cashews are a very useful crop. Cashews are easy to grow, which allows farmers to grow normally and also grow well.
Dr. Thorn Vathana made this presentation on the morning of November 30, 2023, when he was invited to give a lecture on "Promoting Production and Processing of Seeds." Cashews in Cambodia ”to more than 100 agricultural students.
"Cambodia produces a lot of cashews, but we export less processed cashew nuts, which means we can have the opportunity to produce locally and will export directly to international markets," said Dr. Thorn Vathana.
Currently, the Royal Government has made efforts to promote the production of cashew nuts, especially tax exemptions, to promote financial support by easing interest rates for farmers.
He added that in addition to processing cashew nuts for export to international markets, cashew waste left over from processing can be processed into various products, for example, cashew shells can be processed into oil while these shells are being processed. Sold for $ 100 per ton.
Dr. continued that due to the small size of cashew processing in Cambodia, the amount of waste left on the market for processing into other products is still small, so if the cashew processing in the country. The more that will make the cashew coin processing industry in Cambodia will grow in the future.
"Cashew nuts can be produced as a finished product for the market, which can increase the price of cashew nuts even higher." This is the additional confirmation of Dr. Thorn Vathana.
At the same time, Dr. also encouraged students studying agriculture to consider the topic of graduate research, fertilizer production from cashew nuts or processing cashew nuts to rich or study more markets and so on. .
Please be informed that in the first 10 months of 2023, Cambodia exported more than 610,000 tons of raw cashew nuts, earning 831 million US dollars, a decrease of nearly 16.7% compared to the same period in 2022. This is according to data from the Cambodian Cashew Association.
Cashew is a strategic crop that the Royal Government has been paying attention to and promoting the largest export in the world, or can be said to be "the emperor" to export all the cashew in the future.
The Royal Government has launched the National Cashew Policy 2022-2027, a roadmap that focuses on three major strategic goals: production strategy, processing strategy and sustainable export strategy. And market leader.
This policy will play an important role in achieving the goal of the head of the Royal Government to become the emperor of cashew exports to the international market. And clear implementation time.
