The long-standing land dispute of the people in Prek Pnov district has been resolved and applauded by both parties under the coordination of the Minister of Inspection
(Phnom Penh): A long-standing land dispute in Phsar Lech Village, Sangkat Prek Phnov, Khan Prek Phnov, Phnom Penh has been resolved under the leadership of Mr. Huot Hak, Minister of Inspection in opening a new page of the Ministry of Inspection during the legislature. Seventh National Assembly under the long-term vision of Prime Minister Hun Manet, Prime Minister of Cambodia.
The two sides agreed to accept the size of the land and the length of the plot as decided at the Land Dispute Mediation Meeting on October 31, 2023 and the Technical Meeting for the Settlement of Land Disputes through Cadastral Procedures and completed the formalities. List to the parties on November 22, 2023.
In fact, on November 29, 2023, the Minister of Inspection organized a ceremony to hand over the certificate of ownership of real estate to the two parties to the dispute in Phsar Lech Village, Sangkat Prek Pnov, Khan Prek Pnov, Phnom Penh, with the participation of Deputy Prime Minister Say Sam Al. The Minister of Land Management and Urban Planning and Construction, as well as relevant officials and authorities at all levels of the Ministry.
As a result, both parties agreed as follows:
1: Both parties agreed to end the dispute completely by settlement and made concessions based on the wise win-win strategy of Samdech Techo Hun Sen and accepted the certificate of identification of their respective real estate owners with the utmost pleasure.
2. Both parties stop and end all forms that affect the honor and dignity of each party through all means, including through the media and social media.
3. The Ministry of Inspection will close the investigation into the land dispute between the plaintiffs, Ms. Chi Chantha and Mr. Chi Saravuth, representing Mr. Men Thoeun and the plaintiffs, Dr. Men Den and Ms. Touch Thavy from today.
Please be informed that in the previous mandate under the leadership of Samdech Kittisangha Dr. Men Sam An, former Deputy Prime Minister, Minister of National Assembly-Senate Relations and Inspection, successfully resolved many cases related to land disputes to the people, most of which are disputes. Long-lasting land.
