(Kampong Cham): In the morning of November 30, 2023, in the consultation forum to address the requests and concerns of the people in Village 2, Prek Tanong Commune, Koh Sotin District, Kampong Cham Provincial Council of Authorities received a total of 19 requests, requests and concerns. . Some of which were immediately resolved and some were discussed and resolved in accordance with the administrative procedures.
The forum was chaired by Mr. Khlot Phorn, Chairman of the Provincial Council and Mr. Sasitha, Deputy Governor, with the participation of representatives of relevant departments and units, a total of 431 people.
Mr. Khlot Phorn said that the outreach and consultation forum really provided an opportunity for people to get information and listen to the report summarizing the work achieved by the council and the Board of Governors last year. It is an opportunity for the people to raise questions and suggestions for the council to discuss and respond.
It should be noted that the forum lasted for 2 hours and 40 minutes, with the provincial council authority receiving 6 requests from the people, 10 requests, 2 concerns and 1 conflict, a total of 19. Through the presidency, 8 requests, concerns and disputes were resolved and responded immediately, handed over to the authorities, 1 case and the rest were accepted to discuss and resolve according to the procedures of the administration.
Deputy Governor of Kampong Cham Province Calls on Teachers to Continue the Effective Implementation of Basic Education Principles and Peace Culture Education Content for Students
(Kampong Cham): Mr. Khlot Chenda, Deputy Governor of Kampong Cham Province, called on teachers and officials of the Department of Education, Youth and Sports to continue to implement the principles of basic education and the content of peace culture education to students to be more quality and effective. Build a new generation of progressive youth in all fields.
The Deputy Governor said so on November 30, 2023 during the opening ceremony of the new school year 2023-2024 and the school to thank teachers at Sihanoukville High School, Kampong Cham.
(Phnom Penh): The Chinese Embassy in Cambodia on the morning of November 30, 2023 handed over office equipment including 11 laptops and desktops and other equipment worth a total of 15,000 USD. Chan Veasna, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries and a member of the Central Committee of the Union of Youth Federations of Cambodia, handed over to the unit under the Ministry to use.
Regarding these gifts, the Secretary of State recalled that in 2021, he was sent by Mr. Hun Many, President of the Union of Youth Federations of Cambodia, to attend a training course on senior leadership at Peking University, China, through which he built Closer and more confident relationship with the Chinese Embassy in Cambodia. Upon his return, he received a series of donations from the Chinese Embassy to support the development of Cambodia.
Mr. Kong Chanveasna said that in 2022, he brought donations from the Chinese Embassy, including desktops, laptops and printers to the Hun Many library in Kampong Speu and the Office of the Council of Ministers and bicycles. 300 units for students in Kampong Speu, Sihanoukville and Takeo provinces, totaling approximately US $ 50,000.
Mr. Kong Chanveasna said that in 2023, he brought gifts in office equipment, including laptops, desktop computers and some materials to the unit under the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries and is co-producing some promotional videos to support To the work activities of the Ministry, which amounts to a total of about 50,000 US dollars.
The donations from the Chinese Embassy, especially the laptops, are now very important to help increase the productivity and efficiency of officials who respond to practical needs and in line with the first phase of the Royal Government's Pentagon Strategy. Human resources and the promotion of the use of technology are the two main pillars to contribute to the Cambodian economy to achieve the vision of 2030 and 2050 of Cambodia.
On that occasion, Mr. Kong Chanveasna expressed his deep gratitude to the Chinese Embassy in Cambodia, especially the Ambassador and relevant colleagues who provided these gifts through him to the Ministry, institutions and units of Cambodia to support. To the development in Cambodia.
Mr. Kong Chanveasna added that he will maintain this relationship even stronger for the benefit of the governments and peoples of both Cambodia and China.
(Phnom Penh): The Phnom Penh Capital Council this morning, November 30, 2023, held a forum for dissemination and consultation of the third mandate 2023 in Khan Sen Sok. The ceremony was held in the presence of Mr. Chuob Khon, Member of the Phnom Penh Municipal Council and Mr. Keut Chhe, Deputy Governor of Phnom Penh, representing Mr. Khuong Sreng, Governor of Phnom Penh.
In this forum, the people made a lively request, asking the Phnom Penh Municipal Authority to help solve their worries, such as: request to build a sewer road, to install light poles and cut messy power lines, request to expedite Make land ownership plans for 82 families, solve the problem of garbage that people throw on the road that causes rot and affect health, and ask to help restore the canal to cut branches in Phnom Penh Thmey High School.
Mr. Keut Chhe said that in this forum, people raised 12 oral requests and 54 written requests in the mailbox.
Regarding the proposed request, Mr. Keut Chhe assigned professional officers to solve the problem for the people immediately after the end of this forum, such as rehabilitation of canals, roads, we have put in the project, and some roads ask professional officers to study to check Possibility to include in the priority project the next settlement meeting.
Regarding the garbage problem, Mr. Keut Chhe asked the Sangkat and Khan to cooperate with the garbage collection company to clean up the dumped land and to deploy a permanent force to stop the people who take the garbage and throw it at this location.
At the same time, the Deputy Governor of Phnom Penh requested the people to participate in packing and storing garbage in their respective houses and stop taking garbage and leaving it on the streets, which will affect the environment and affect the health of the people in the village.
Mr. Chuob Khon said that the outreach and consultation forum of the Phnom Penh Capital Council focuses on the direct concerns of the people with security, order, environmental issues and local development issues so that the authorities know and find a mechanism to solve. .
