Minister of Energy Keo Rattanak Highlights the achievements of Cambodia's energy sector in the last 15 years (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): Mr. Keo Rattanak, Minister of Mines and Energy, highlighted this morning, November 30, 2023 The important achievements that the Cambodian energy sector has achieved in the development of the electricity sector in the last 15 years from 2008 to the present.
The highlight of this achievement was the Minister's speech at the Closing Ceremony of the Stung Ta Tai Leu Dam in Thmar Bang District, Koh Kong Province, presided over by His Excellency Hun Manet, Prime Minister of Cambodia.
The main achievements that the Cambodian energy sector has achieved in the actual development of the electricity sector in the 15 years from 2008 to the present are as follows:
1: Development of power supply
Power generation has been continuously developed, with the generation capacity increasing from 150 MW in 1998 to 4,495.42 MW by the end of 2022, an increase of almost 30 times, while the development of transmission and substation systems has started from scratch. By 2008, there were about 3,486 km of transmission network and the number of substations increased to 63, making the national network able to cover all 25 capitals and provinces of Cambodia.
2: Nationwide price agreement, reduction and preference for electricity price
3: Improving the provision of services to electricity consumers
In order for Cambodia to be able to increase the production and use of renewable energy sources towards a carbon neutral society by 2050, the Cambodian energy sector needs to develop energy storage systems to control the fluctuations of renewable energy sources and To store energy for replenishment when the sun or wind is down or not.
In the past, the Ministry of Mines and Energy has tried to include the use of battery storage systems in the last four solar development projects to neutralize the fluctuations of solar energy and is preparing to invest. A large-scale storage battery project with the Asian Development Bank (ADB).
Banlung, Ta Veng and Bor Keo districts of Ratanakkiri province have been declared as districts to end open defecation.
(Rattanakiri): Rattanakiri Provincial Administration celebrates the 14th National Day for the Promotion of Rural Sanitation and recognizes Banlung, Ta Veng and Bor Keo districts as districts to end open defecation.
Speaking at the ceremony, Mr. Chea Thavrith expressed his congratulations and admiration to the authorities at all levels and people throughout Ratanakkiri, especially in Ta Veng, Banlung and Bor Keo districts, which were evaluated by the provincial committee. A thorough examination confirmed that the three cities and districts completed open defecation in November 2023.
On that occasion, Mr. Try Meng expressed his congratulations to the three districts of Ratanakkiri province for stopping the use of defecation.
On the occasion of World AIDS Day, December 1, Deputy Prime Minister Vongsey Visoth provided seven key points to the National AIDS Authority in Cambodia.
Speaking on the occasion, Deputy Prime Minister Vongsey Visoth brought high praise from Samdech and President Dr. to the leadership of civil servants of the National AIDS Authority under the leadership of Senior Minister Ieng Moly. Many great achievements in reducing the spread of HIV and AIDS in Cambodia, especially in the context that Cambodia and the world have experienced the Kovid-19 crisis in the past.
Taking the opportunity to celebrate the World AIDS Day on December 1, 2023, on behalf of Samdech Prime Minister Hun Manet, Prime Minister of Cambodia, Permanent Deputy Prime Minister Vongsey Visoth, please share some views on the eradication of AIDS in Cambodia as follows:
* First. The National AIDS Authority must continue to lead and coordinate with relevant ministries, institutions and partner organizations in formulating a policy to eradicate HIV / AIDS in 2025 and to sustain the AIDS program for 2023-2028 in a timely manner as a basis for strategic planning. Comprehensive and multidisciplinary national response to HIV and AIDS for the sixth time in a sustainable and sustainable national system.
* Second. The National AIDS Authority, ministries, institutions, development partners and all stakeholders must continue to strictly implement the comprehensive and multi-sectoral National Strategic Plan for HIV / AIDS and the AIDS Eradication Policy by 2025 and the Sustainable Aid Program for the year. 2023-2028 To ensure the success and sustainability of the HIV and AIDS response, aiming to end HIV / AIDS by 2025 in Cambodia.
* Third. The National AIDS Authority must cooperate with the Ministry of Health, the Ministry of Economy, the Ministry of Planning and relevant ministries to continue to promote the effective implementation of the six measures related to the response to HIV and AIDS.
* Fifth. The Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports, the Ministry of Information, the Ministry of Women's Affairs and relevant ministries and institutions must work together to promote HIV / AIDS education and develop new digital outreach materials to prevent the spread of HIV in the community .
* Sixth. Capital and provincial governors must continue to strengthen the mechanism of HIV / AIDS committees at the capital, provincial, municipal, district, khan and commune levels throughout the country to take responsibility for responding more effectively to the response to HIV and AIDS at the local level.
