Mr. Tho Chetha inspects the Mekong River Commission's Regional Flood and Drought Management Center in Phnom Penh
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Tho Chetha, Minister of Water Resources and Meteorology and Chairman of the Mekong River Commission 2023, accompanied by the leadership of the National Mekong River Commission of Cambodia, on November 30, 2023, inspected the Flood Management Center and Regional Drought of the Mekong River Commission (MRC).
The Minister thanked for the warm welcome from Mr. Anulak Kitikoun, Executive Director and Secretariat of the Mekong River Commission, together with the leadership and officials of the General Secretariat of the National Mekong Committee of Cambodia, officials of the relevant departments of the Ministry of Water Resources and Many other meteorologists.
The Minister said that the changes in the hydrological regime, floods and droughts in the Mekong River Basin in the past and at present are important points that need to be addressed together by strengthening close monitoring and to be provided. Inform countries along the Mekong River in a timely manner through technological approaches and innovations that better link the Mekong River Commission Secretariat and member countries.
The Minister said that these changes are due to the increase in demand for water, food and energy, the momentum of rapid development and climate change, which has been putting increasing pressure on the resources in the basin and the sustainability of the Mekong River.
The Minister expressed confidence in the increasingly important and proactive role of the Mekong River Commission and the Regional Center for Flood and Drought Management in the context of constant change and emerging challenges to assist member countries. And work with all countries along the Mekong River together to address the risk and impact of floods in each country and in the basin more effectively and in a timely manner.
