The award ceremony took place on November 28, 2023 in Vienna, Austria. This award reflects the recognition of the project's efforts and contributions to promoting gender equality and empowering women in the fisheries sector in Cambodia. The theme of the award is "Making Gender Equality a reality in the industry".
"The project's gender equality approach really creates an environment where everyone can thrive without leaving anyone behind," he acknowledged.
He said that UNIDO is very proud of the project's ongoing efforts to promote the economic role and resilience of women, especially women-led MSMEs.
"Through gender mainstreaming in the project, including gender policy, business support, project management, research and innovation, and project stakeholder capacity building," said Pum Sotha, the Royal Government Delegate in charge of the Fisheries Administration (FiA). It has had a long-term impact on promoting gender equality and empowering women in the fisheries sector in Cambodia. ”
Based on Cambodia's post-harvest fisheries competitiveness initiative, the project supports eight research projects to address relevant issues in the sector, taking into account the needs and barriers of women in expanding their business operations.
It should be noted that of these research projects, 4 were led by female researchers in collaboration with universities and the private sector. In addition to the above support, the project supported a group of 5 women fisheries processors with a total of 141 members, most of whom were women. For the next round of VCIS, the project will select 20 more enterprises, targeting at least 60% women business owners.
