The Ministry of Agriculture and the European Union led a group of journalists to study the cashew production chain in 4 capitals and provinces
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries and the European Union on November 29, 2023 organized a four-day study tour of the Cambodian cashew production chain in Phnom Penh, Kampong Thom province. Kratie and Stung Treng provinces.
The visit coincides with the Cashew Forum organized to highlight the progress and opportunities for investment in Cambodia's cashew sector through an initiative by the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries in collaboration with the Ministry of Commerce and EU-sponsored to highlight Cashew production line in Cambodia.
Through this 3-night, 4-day visit, participating journalists will learn about the cashew production chain from planting, harvesting to processing and market potential.
The visit will also provide an overview of the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries' efforts to promote cashew production in line with the "National Cashew Policy 2022-2027" issued by the Ministry of Commerce to encourage Cambodia became a cashew emperor.
In particular, the European Union, which sponsors the event, aims to demonstrate its commitment to Cambodia's agricultural sector by emphasizing sustainable development and economic diversification.
This press visit will serve as a testament to the joint efforts between Cambodia and the European Union to develop a potential and prosperous cashew industry.
The purpose of the press visit is to: * Provide an in-depth understanding of the Cambodian cashew production chain to the media team, ensuring that they will gain a comprehensive knowledge of the scope, challenges and opportunities of the industry.
* Promote cooperation by creating a collaborative environment where journalists can meet directly with key representatives from the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, the Ministry of Commerce, as well as members of the EU delegation to discuss the current and future situation of the cashew industry.
Promote industry success by highlighting and disseminating success stories in the cashew value chain to the public in Cambodia, highlighting the efforts of the Ministry of Agriculture and the Ministry of Commerce in collaboration with the European Union.
* Provide an opportunity for journalists to hear first-hand the experiences of the cashew community and other stakeholders, including farmers, processors and exporters.
* Improve the quality of advertising content through the production of all forms of information, including audio and video articles related to the cashew community and value chain effectively.
The visit will be a testament to the close cooperation between all stakeholders, such as the Royal Government, business and media representatives, with the potential to enhance the cashew production chain and the EU's contribution to the sector through Clear and accurate means of communication.
The program will also provide accurate, precise and up-to-date information on project activities and interactions between all stakeholders to the public through a wide range of media coverage.
