Bokator is a traditional Khmer martial art that has been deeply rooted in Cambodian society for centuries and continues to survive in Cambodian society to this day.
The carvings on the walls of Angkorian temples are clear evidence of this martial art practice. The training of bokator from one generation to another is to strengthen the wisdom and ability to protect themselves from wild animals and enemies, as well as to protect the society and the motherland.
