The main items used in the Ok Ambok ceremony are: Ambok, ripe bananas, young coconuts, flowers, as well as a number of relics. This ceremony is usually held during the low water season in the lunar month, which is the full moon and full moon, and this ceremony is also associated with the Royal Water Festival.
Today, the Moon Festival and Ok Ambok are practiced by people all over the country every year and are considered one of the major national cultural festivals among many other important festivals.
In connection with this ceremony, the farmers took fresh ripe rice to roast and hit and then took out the husks and offered them to the deity at the time of the full moon to show their gratitude to the deity who gave the rain to the earth. All kinds of crops grow and get a lot of agricultural crops. When Ok Ambok, they wait for the full moon over their heads, then they take Ambok and give it to the rich, old, friends, Ok in happiness.
