A military officer who hit a security guard with a flashlight, causing him to break his head and demand that the victim pay for the flashlight, was sent to court by Por Sen Chey district police
(Phnom Penh): A military officer who hit a security guard with a flashlight caused his head to break and demanded that the victim pay for another flashlight was sent by the Po Sen Chey District Police to the Phnom Penh Municipal Court on November 27, 2023. .
It should be informed that the military officer who caused the violence on the security was arrested by the police force of Post Choam Chao I, Khan Po Sen Chey after the perpetrator violently hit the security guard with a flashlight, causing severe facial injuries at 1 o'clock. Night on November 24, 2023 at the entrance of New World Borey, Trapeang Thleung 4 Village, Sangkat Choam Chao I, Khan Por Senchey, Phnom Penh.
The arrest of the military officer came after beating security guards at the entrance to the New World City, causing disfigurement, insulting and threatening to shoot the local police who went to intervene. Not only that, he hit the victim with a flashlight and even asked the victim to pay for the flashlight, both drunk and called the criminal police to help.
According to the report of the local police, when the police force went to intervene, the person shouted and threatened to shoot at the police. In accordance with the law, the police force arrested and sent to the police station and forwarded to the district police inspectorate for further action. Preah Sihanouk Provincial Administration Takes Measures to Strengthen Security and Suppress Crimes
(Preah Sihanouk): The Preah Sihanouk Provincial Administration has introduced measures to strengthen security mechanisms and crack down on criminal and technological crimes that occur in Preah Sihanouk Province.
This measure was introduced at the meeting of Preah Sihanouk Provincial Administrative Unity Command on November 24, 2023 at Preah Sihanouk Provincial Council Hall, chaired by Mr. Kouch Chamroeun, Governor of Preah Sihanouk Province and Chairman of the Administrative Unity Command. Province.
The meeting decided as follows:
Ensure safety, which is an important foundation for economic, social and tourism development.
* Must conduct a thorough search to find the assets and bank accounts of the suspects who committed the crime to freeze.
* The Provincial Police Commission and the Provincial Gendarmerie Command must conduct an investigation into the source of the weapons for the armed suspects. Where did the weapons come from? Or where to buy? And must destroy any criminal group that uses explosive weapons to pose a risk in Sihanoukville, regardless of race is not exempt.
* The provincial police commission must increase the checkpoints for the strict implementation of the law on road traffic.
* The Provincial Police Commission and the Provincial Police must continue to implement mobile inspection measures on a regular basis.
* Municipal and District Administrative Unity Command must continue to pay attention to inspecting national weapons, explosives and conducting open administration on a regular basis.
* Provincial prisons must be thoroughly and thoroughly controlled in the face of serious criminals who are being held in prisons and must immediately report to the provincial administration at any time of change.
* For the sharing of images of violence and crime information should be considered as a discipline of the forces, must strictly control the sharing of information related to crimes that have not been completely cracked down, absolutely not to leak. Affect the criminal investigation process. The competent authority shall make a press release to the public when the criminal investigation process is closed.
* Provincial Department of Cults and Religions shall organize religious ceremonies to pray for happiness in places where traffic accidents are frequent, to publicize and remind road users to be careful and obey traffic laws to reduce accidents. That could happen eventually.
* Call on the people to cooperate and report information on violence, illegal possession of weapons, drug use and trafficking and other crimes to the competent authorities to take timely action.
The competent forces must conduct an urgent search operation and must maintain the confidentiality of any citizen who has provided information related to those crimes.
The AIDS Health Care Foundation will mark World AIDS Day 2023 early next month.
As the world has grown significantly over the past few decades, the global HIV / AIDS response is facing serious threats, including inadequate funding and high risk rates. Of the 1.3 million new HIV infections each year, about 630,000 die each year, and the response is not given a high enough priority, especially in low-income countries.
According to Dr. Huy Sikheng, Country Program Manager, the fight against HIV / AIDS is not over! We are calling for a united voice with communities living with HIV, high risk groups or people affected by HIV, to call for action in response to HIV.
World AIDS Day, held annually on December 1, provides an opportunity for HIV / AIDS advocates to raise awareness and have a global response to the fight against HIV / AIDS. The stigma and discrimination of people living with HIV hinders access to blood tests and treatment. Urge governments around the world to ensure the resources and political will to fight HIV / AIDS.
A representative of the AIDS Health Care Foundation (AHF), Dr. Nou Vannary, said that on the occasion of the Water Festival, AHF also joined the National AIDS Authority to distribute about 40,000 condoms and a team. Free blood tests for HIV and a mobile team to spread the word about HIV to people and water sports.
The AHF, the world's largest HIV / AIDS Foundation, is currently providing medical care and / or services to more than 1.9 million clients in 45 countries around the world in the United States, Africa. Latin America / Caribbean, Asia / Pacific and Europe.
