There is peace, there is a happy Water Festival now!
(Phnom Penh): Many Cambodians and foreign tourists happily attended the Water Festival in front of the Royal Palace and many other places in Phnom Penh. In the provinces also receive a lot of national and foreign guests.
This large traditional festival is held to commemorate the heroism of the navy, the gods of the Ganges and the earth. But now the Water Festival is also an opportunity to commemorate the merits of peace, because this big and joyful festival could not be celebrated during the war-torn country and during the Khmer Rouge regime. Happiness comes only under the shadow of peace.
In fact, this year's Water Festival can be organized because the Royal Government of the seventh mandate led by Samdech Thipadei Hun Manet ensures the protection of peace, which is rarely found and the achievement of the most difficult efforts of Samdech Techo Hun Sen. While the Cambodian people are happy, hundreds of millions of people in the world do not have such an opportunity, they are suffering from the loss of peace and war is going on in their country.
Taking this opportunity, we look back a little at Cambodia's past: since the March 18, 1970 coup, the country has fallen into the flames of war and slipped into the Killing Fields regime on April 17, 1975. On January 7, 1979, Cambodians had to swim across mountains, rivers, blood, sea, and tears for nearly four years, during which time about 3 million Cambodians lost their lives.
After the day of liberation on January 7, the process of rebuilding the country and seeking peace continued until peace was finally found on December 29, 1998 by the victorious political achievements of Samdech Techo Hun Sen. Therefore, any new leader who maintains peace must be considered as the first and most important achievement before talking about other achievements, because peace is very valuable for Cambodia.
This is the reason why the guarantee of maintaining peace is the first achievement of the Royal Government of the seventh mandate led by Samdech Mani Hun Manet. Because of peace, we can celebrate such a happy Water Festival.
