Expressing intention to import processed agricultural products and food products from Cambodia to sell in this supermarket after the Cambodian business delegation and investors visited the United States from November 7 to 13, 2023 Long Beach, California and has been in direct contact with the owner of this Asian supermarket.
Speaking at a press conference on November 24, 2023, after returning from the United States, Dr. Hor Sereyvath, Chairman of the Board of Directors of IDI and IDC, said that the owner of a supermarket, a wholesale and retail market in the past. Ordered goods from China, Vietnam, Thailand, Bangladesh, India, etc. for sale in its supermarkets, expressed its intention and helped pave the way for Cambodian products to be imported to sell in this market.
He said that the United States is the largest market for imports from Cambodia, accounting for about 40% of Cambodia's total exports, but mostly imported goods such as clothing, leather goods, travel goods, bags, machinery, equipment. Electricity and footwear, but no processed food products have been imported into the US market yet.
He observed that the problem that hinders the export of Cambodian agricultural products to the US market due to the lack of communication between Cambodian producers and US buyers, some producers do not understand the standard of products that can be imported to The United States goes deeper, another issue is the registration of export products.
Through the third visit of a Cambodian business delegation and investor to the United States, the Cambodian business team has learned a lot about the standards of products imported into the United States, as well as an in-depth study of the procedures for exporting processed products to the United States. And IDI will join with other institutions to promote investment to be able to export in the future.
He said that most of the goods sold in this market are imported from Thailand and Vietnam, and that they want Cambodian products to be sold because some of the raw materials produced by Thailand and Vietnam are exported. From Cambodia, this is why the owner of this Asian supermarket wants to help make Cambodian products imported and sold in this supermarket, while the area also has a large number of Cambodians.
He encourages Cambodian producers who intend to produce for export or domestic supply to improve the quality of production to a standard. However, he observed that some companies have met the standard, but many others have not been able to meet the production of quality standards yet.
