Lanterns of the Ministry of Posts and Telecommunications participate in the Royal Water Festival, floating lanterns and worshiping the moon
The meaning of the lantern of the Ministry of Posts and Telecommunications shows the development of the postal sector, telecommunications and digital technology with the following content:
1. The goddess is the king of beasts, representing the Khmer culture and traditions that continue from ancient times to the present, as well as the water element, which is the source of survival and harmony of people across the country.
2. Map of the Kingdom of Cambodia embedded with fiber optic network connected to the whole area The map represents the connection of cable network in all communes throughout the country by 2027 to provide high speed telecommunication and internet services to the people in a convenient environment.
3. The logo of the Ministry of Posts and Telecommunications (at the center of the map) represents the leading institutions in the field of post, telecommunications and digital technology, as well as playing an important role in leading the digital revolution in Cambodia.
4. Mobile antenna towers and satellite images represent the growth of quality mobile services across the country to serve the daily communication of all citizens and highlight the interconnection between Cambodia. And countries in the world.
5. The post office building, mail and planes represent the postal sector in Cambodia, dating back to the 19th century and postal traffic around the world. Currently, the postal sector is being modernized to promote the postal sector to be more efficient and easier to provide services to the people.
6. Post stamps with white doves show gratitude for "peace", the great work of the Father of Peace, Samdech Akka Moha Sena Padei Techo Hun Sen, who has given Cambodia the opportunity to develop in all areas of life. Happiness and brought to our country peace and prosperity, everything as it is today.
7. Smartphones represent the evolution of technological devices that make today's communications more sophisticated and fast.
10. The motto "Digital technology helps make life better" represents the identification of digital technology as an important new catalyst for boosting economic and social productivity as well as work efficiency, as defined in the fifth pillar of the Pentagon Strategy Phase I. Of the Royal Government of the 7th Legislature of the National Assembly under the high leadership of Samdech Moha Bovathibodi Hun Manet, Prime Minister of the Kingdom of Cambodia.
