International Khmer Martial Arts Federation issues joint statement on six outcomes after the General Assembly with 60 member countries in Siem Reap
(Siem Reap): The Khmer International Martial Arts Federation (KIF) issued a joint statement on the outcome of its annual general meeting held at the Borey Angkor Hotel in Siem Reap, Siem Reap province on the evening of November 25, 2023.
The General Assembly of the International Khmer Martial Arts Federation has agreed to issue the following joint statement:
1. The International Khmer Martial Arts Federation and all members of the Khmer Martial Arts Federation have agreed to maintain the continuity of the organization of the Khmer Martial Arts World Championship on a regular basis every year.
2. The International Khmer Martial Arts Federation has been working to strengthen the management mechanism of the 60 member countries and increase the membership to 75 countries in the next five-year term from 2024 to apply for the Olympic Committee. International and relevant international sports organizations.
3. International Khmer Martial Arts Federation calls for support for the "National Movement for the Development of Khmer Martial Arts" to
Achieve the national strategic goal of "integrating international Khmer martial arts into the Olympics."
4. The International Khmer Martial Arts Federation is always open to receive Khmer Martial Arts membership from all countries.
5. The 5th General Assembly and Khmer Martial Arts Championship 2024 will take place
Go to the Kingdom of Cambodia and the Khmer Martial Arts World Championship from 2025 will take place according to the requested member countries. If member countries do not host, Cambodia reserves the right to organize to sustain this important event.
Please be informed that the above annual general meeting of KIF will be held one day before the 4th Khmer International Boxing Championship 2023, which will be held in Siem Reap from 26-28. November 2023, with nearly 70 athletes from 17 countries, including hosts Cambodia, Russia, Mauritius, Japan, Kazakhstan, India, Iran, Australia, Argentina, Cameroon, the Philippines, Indonesia, Thailand, Malaysia and Laos.
For the new members of the Executive Committee of the International Federation of Khmer Martial Arts, the General Assembly also approved 17 candidates, including Mr. Mamara as Chairman and Mr. Vath Chamroeun as Secretary General, as well as leaders and members of the National Coalition. Other nations, such as the French, Japanese, Indians, Iranians, Malaysians, Thais and Filipinos, have also retained and incorporated a number of Cambodian members.
