Expert: Cambodia's actions in promoting solar energy on rooftops promote green development of tourism
(Phnom Penh): Cambodia is one of the fastest growing countries in the world and Cambodia has recently launched the "Principles for Permitting Solar Roofing in Cambodia". This principle can be an important document. Basically, the new regulations are expected to be implemented in early 2024.
Experts believe the new regulations could improve tourism by promoting sustainable change in clean energy and promoting green development in Cambodia.
"New regulations that are expected to be introduced in the near future could pave the way for the use of solar energy, which will reduce electricity costs, strengthen the clean energy supply and reduce carbon emissions," he said. "Also."
CTF and WWF experts believe the new regulations could improve domestic clean energy use and encourage key economic players to install rooftop solar systems. Clear and neutral values that can complement current regulations.
Experts from both institutions also stressed that sustainable energy use through rooftop solar systems could increase revenue for community-based eco-tourism sites across the country, promoting sustainable economic development. When contributing to the conservation of natural resources.
CTF and WWF are partnering in the “Brotherhood, Environment and Environment of Cambodia Tourism Restoration and Promotion” program, a three-year project. The project aims to facilitate tourism in Cambodia by implementing a choice of solar power systems for use in hotels, resorts and eco-tourism community locations.
