Hun Manit and Russian Ambassador pay tribute to eight Russian agricultural experts who died 40 years ago in Chamkar Leu district
(Kampong Cham): Mr. Hun Manit, Director General of the General Department of Intelligence Research and Deputy Commander of the Army Command, presided over a memorial service for eight agricultural experts in the former Soviet Socialist Republic who died last year. 1983: Daun Thi village, Bos Khnour commune, Chamkar Leu district, Kampong Cham province.
The ceremony was held on the morning of November 25, 2023 at Wat Keo Monisetharam, also known as Wat Daunthy, in Daunthy Village, Bos Khnour Commune, Chamkar Leu District, with the participation of Mr. Anatoly Porovit, Ambassador of the Russian Federation to Cambodia, Mr. Dith Ty Na, Minister of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries and Mr. Un Chanda, Governor of Kampong Cham Province, as well as the accompanying delegation and many other people.
The Governor of Kampong Cham Province, Mr. Un Chanda, said that on this occasion, if we all close our eyes to remember the past when the whole country was in the flames of war in the 1970s and 1990s, we really Imagine living under a roof of ammunition full of pain, desolation, deprivation, wife, children, siblings, and relatives in fear, anxiety, and hatred of war.
In fact, as we all remember here, the events of August 1983 were the catastrophic loss of life of eight agricultural technicians. It was an accident, but it really started from the war that was raging in Cambodia, which caused the tragedy, the loss of family, wife, children, parents from the victims in this incident. .
Mr. Un Chanda continued that on behalf of the provincial administration and the younger generation, I would like to express my deepest condolences to the families of the victims, who are agricultural technicians of the eight former Soviet Socialist Republics, and wish them well. Sleep peacefully, such a catastrophe can never happen in the territory of Kampong Cham province, and please pray for the consequences of those who have gone to hell, do not be sad.
Mr. Anatoly Porovit, Ambassador of the Russian Federation to Cambodia, took the opportunity to express his deep gratitude to the Royal Government of Cambodia and the Cambodian people for coming to pay their respects to the agricultural experts of the former Soviet Socialist Republic who lost their lives for friendship.
The ambassador believes that with our joint efforts, we will be able to do everything we can to prevent the tragedy that occurred 40 years ago.
