Dr. Hor Sereyvath continued, "The United States is a major market that is doing business with Cambodia and will continue to be an important export destination for Cambodia." We hope that through the visit in March 2023 and this visit, we will gradually begin to see some potential agricultural and food products on the list of products exported to the United States, which will contribute to increasing production volume and revenue for "Farmers and exporters of Cambodia."
After the visit, some delegates made a clear decision to add additional capital to invest in improving their export capacity, such as diversification of mango and gourd products, establishment of warehousing services, improvement. Cosmetic products and body care and processing of dried fruits, etc.
According to statistics from the Ministry of Commerce, the United States is Cambodia's second largest trading partner with a bilateral trade volume of $ 4.355 billion in the first half of 2023. Cambodia's main products are exported to the United States. These include clothing, leather goods, travel goods, bags, machinery, electrical appliances and footwear. Cambodia imports vehicles, machinery, medical equipment and pharmaceutical products from the United States.
