The Ottawa Convention Review Meeting is held every five years, and Cambodia is the fifth country in the world and the first country in Asia to chair and host this meeting. . The first meeting was held in Kenya in 2004, the second in Colombia in 2009, the third in Mozambique in 2014, the fourth in Norway in 2019 and the fifth in Cambodia in 2024.
As the chair and host of the meeting, Cambodia selected the territory of Siem Reap for the organization and participation of 164 member states and observer states, as well as many other world organizations. The Siem Reap-Angkor Summit is a forum where Cambodia will reaffirm the commitment of the international community to the elimination of anti-personnel mines and review the progress of the implementation of past action plans.
He stated that Cambodia plans to launch three priority projects, including:
1: Promote the globalization of the Convention: Encourage non-States Parties to join or attend meetings or implement aspects of the Convention 2: Strengthen the implementation of Article 5 of the Convention: Demining against people and 3: Assist victims Due to landmines and explosive remnants of war
Samdech Hun Manet also commended Senior Minister Ly Thuch, First Vice President of the Mines Authority, leaders, officials, staff, Mines Authority, development partners, national and international operators, mine action communities and all stakeholders for their efforts and contributions to the country and The Cambodian people have escaped suffering from anti-personnel mines, the legacy of Cambodia's long-running war.
He also thanked the member states of the Ottawa Convention and the international community for their continued support and appreciation for Cambodia's efforts in mine action, as well as for its confidence in the election of Cambodia as chair and host. This important summit.
