(Siem Reap): The 2023 Microfinance Conference ended on 24 November 2023 with the commitment of stakeholders in strengthening the responsible financial environment, customer protection and protection. Clients in difficult times through credit restructuring to develop a sustainable financial sector.
This commitment was made at the 2023 MFI Conference on "Responsible Financial Environment, Sustainability and Sustainability of the Financial Sector in Cambodia" with the participation of policy makers and economists. Business leaders, banking and microfinance leaders, as well as a total of 320 key stakeholders to discuss the latest trends and challenges in the sector.
At the conference, stakeholders mentioned many efforts and initiatives to promote and strengthen a responsible financial environment and customer protection. For the microfinance sector, several initiatives have been made for this task, such as:
1: Credit contract standards and provisions Credit contract standards to be developed to increase transparency and customer protection in the financial sector
2: Code of Conduct for Banking and Financial Institutions, established to promote the efficient operation of the banking and financial sector, trust, accountability and responsibility by setting business operating standards for banking and financial institutions.
3: Community financial security project implemented in 4 provinces with the aim of promoting financial literacy, rights and protection of customers at the local level.
4: Training program for CEOs and shareholders / boards on customer protection designed to examine the roles of the board and senior management to ensure that strong customer protection is incorporated into the business operations of the client. And to maintain sustainability in the institution
5: Regional Workshop on Financial Institution Management Capacity Building, which focuses on management at provincial, district and regional branches of banking and financial institutions;
6. The Responsible Lending Program is designed to enhance the professional ethics of credit officers and credit officers by requiring a certification exam every three years, as well as many other efforts.
7. Credit rules are designed to ensure that customers' borrowing capacity is carefully and accurately assessed to reduce excessive debt and avoid systemic risks.
At the same time, through the conference, the Cambodian Microfinance Association also urged its members to examine the possibility of helping clients through the reorganization of loans on a case-by-case basis in the tourism sector in Siem Reap, the real estate sector. And other affected sectors to customers with financial difficulties with a high sense of responsibility.
This commitment is made in the context that the Royal Government of Cambodia has tightened consumer protection by issuing a joint statement in early 2023 of the Ministry of Interior and the National Bank of Cambodia (NBC) to curb illegal loan activities. Including the strengthening of consumer protection of the Consumer Protection Commission, Competition and Anti-Fraud (CPC) of the Ministry of Commerce.
