(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training calls on young people who have just received the results of the high school diploma exam, despite failing, to turn their attention to the free vocational and technical training of the Royal Government of the seventh mandate.
Mr. Kata On, Secretary of State and spokesman for the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training, said on November 24 that young people and nieces and nephews who have just received the results of the high school diploma exam, despite failing, should turn their attention to the training. Vocational and technical skills that are free to attend, especially young people from poor and vulnerable families will receive an additional monthly stipend of 280,000 riels.
He added that at present, the education system in Cambodia is comprehensive, namely the system of general education and higher education and vocational and technical training. Vocational and technical training was officially launched by the Royal Government on November 14, 2023 by Prime Minister Hun Manet.
"Passing or failing exams is no longer a concern for young people, and all nieces and nephews can check their chances of going to college or attending vocational and technical training courses," he said. Short and get a technical degree that can find a good job as well.
On behalf of the Banteay Meanchey Provincial Drug Control Committee, Mr. Ngor Mengchruon spoke about the active implementation of the fight against drugs in accordance with the plans, regulations and guidelines that have been submitted so far with remarkable results. Mark.
* First, continue to prepare specific action plans for the implementation of anti-drug work in accordance with the relevant regulations and guidelines issued by the Royal Government and the National Anti-Drug Authority in the past.
* Second, to increase the education on the effects and dangers of drugs to all levels of the public in all public forums of the province, city, commune, sangkat, especially through social media, billboards, posters. Towns, resorts and resorts
* Third: Continue to increase administrative control over challenging targets such as guesthouses, hotels, bars, clubs and entertainment venues by managing, educating, guiding and contracting clearly with the owners and responsible persons of those businesses or locations.
* Fourth: Be careful to monitor all locations where there is a suspicion of drug processing, such as warehouses or remote farms near mountainous areas and in close contact with border countries.
* Fifth: To continue to implement the policy of safe villages, communes and sangkats effectively and adhere to the three national slogans, not to report.
* Sixth, to plan the intervention and send addicts to treatment and rehabilitation in the centers and to classify the first level addicts should be referred and referred to the treatment services in referral hospitals and health centers that provide counseling and treatment. Drug addicts.
* Seventh: To strengthen and promote good cooperation with the border provinces, including districts and districts, front-line law enforcement officers and front-line law enforcement officers working in the border areas of neighboring countries, especially through Use the Border Liaison Office (BLO) mechanism.
