ASEAN Secretary-General Meets Minister of Labor and Minister of Mines and Energy
(Phnom Penh): Dr. Kao Kim Hourn, Secretary-General of ASEAN, on November 24, 2023, met with Mr. Heng Sour, Minister of Labor and Vocational Training.
On that occasion, the Secretary-General of ASEAN congratulated Mr. Heng Sour for his appointment as Minister in the new term of the Royal Government of Cambodia and commended Cambodia for its contribution to the implementation of the ASEAN Labor Ministers' Work Program 2021-2025. .
The two sides also exchanged views on ways to further strengthen cooperation in the field of labor, including the protection and promotion of the rights of migrant workers in the region.
On the same day, Dr. Kao Kim Hourn continued to meet with Mr. Keo Rattanak, Minister of Mines and Energy. On that occasion, the Secretary-General of ASEAN congratulated Mr. Keo Rattanak on his appointment as Minister in the new term of the Royal Government of Cambodia and congratulated Cambodia on hosting and chairing the 9th ASEAN Ministerial Meeting on Mines and Related Meetings. Successfully.
Many countries, including India, do not recognize the Taliban as the official government of Afghanistan, but recognize that they are the ruling authorities there. This has left many Afghan embassies and consulates in a precarious position, with diplomats appointed by the previous government refusing to hand over control of the embassy to a new delegation elected by Taliban authorities.
In a letter posted on social media X, the Afghan Embassy in India announced: "The Embassy of the Islamic Republic of Afghanistan in New Delhi regrets the decision to close its diplomatic mission in New Delhi. This. Friday's announcement follows a statement last month that the embassy had decided to suspend operations.
The Taliban has full control over more than a dozen Afghan embassies abroad, including in Pakistan, China, Turkey and Iran. Embassies in other countries operate in a hybrid system in the absence of the ambassador, but embassy staff continue to perform routine tasks such as issuing visas and other documents.
(Phnom Penh): Ms. Pen Sophea, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Economy and Finance, Deputy Prime Minister Aun Porn Moniroth, Deputy Prime Minister, Minister of Economy and Finance and Chairman of the Board of Trustees of the Kantha Bopha Foundation of Cambodia, met with Dr. Philip Robinson, Chairman of the Board of Directors of Kantha Bopha Swiss Foundation. From continuing to strengthen cooperation between the two funds to ensure the sustainability of Kantha Bopha Hospital.
Past efforts have led to a significant drop in infant and child mortality rates, she said. Therefore, the support of the Kantha Bopha Swiss Foundation, as well as the Government and the people of the Swiss Confederation, is very important in helping to improve the well-being of children and women in Cambodia, in line with the Royal Government of Cambodia's first Pentagon strategy, which is A catalyst helps propel Cambodia towards achieving Cambodia's 2050 vision.
Mr. Nith also mentioned that after the absence of Professor Beatrice Rich, the founder of the Foundation began to think about the orientation and preparation of successors, while now he himself has become the Chairman of the Board of Directors of the third generation of the Kantha Bopha Swiss Foundation. In the search for philanthropists to support the fund for a long time to come.
He is committed to maintaining the continued cooperation with the Kantha Bopha Foundation of Cambodia for the sustainability of Kantha Bopha Hospital, which is on a mission to examine, treat and save the lives of children in Cambodia for free and with high quality.
Ms. Pen Sophea once again thanked the Swiss government as well as the Swiss Kantha Bopha Foundation for its continued support of Kantha Bopha Hospital for the past 31 years and for the future.
