The ADB press release said that the second sub-program of the Public Financial Management Strengthening Program is based on the achievements of the first sub-program to strengthen policies and regulatory frameworks for cost and revenue management as well as the absorption capacity of Ministries selected to implement PFM reforms and strengthen oversight responsibilities of the National Audit Authority.
Reform measures supported by the second sub-program to modernize PFM systems in Cambodia were fully implemented prior to approval. These include improving strategic plans and budgeting to strengthen compliance with policy goals, boosting revenue collection to increase fiscal liquidity for priority public expenditures, strengthening public investment management for public expenditure management. Effectively, and strengthening public debt management.
Increased efforts to promote the digitalization of PFM systems and strengthen internal and external auditing are among the reform measures to improve operational efficiency, promote financial accountability and improve public spending control.
