Minister Tho Chetha Meets Lao Minister for Natural Resources and Environment
(Siem Reap): Mr. Tho Chetha, Minister of Water Resources and Meteorology and Chairman of the Cambodian National Mekong River Commission, on November 24, 2023, met with Ms. Boun Khamvorak, Minister of Natural Resources and Environment of Laos. Involvement of senior leaders of both parties, as well as relevant professional officials.
The Minister expressed his pleasure and gratitude to the Minister and the delegation of the Ministry of Natural Resources and Environment of Laos for attending the 30th Mekong River Commission Council Meeting and Consultation Meeting with Partner Countries. 28th Development in Cambodia.
The Minister praised the full support and cooperation of the Lao side in the Cambodian mandate to chair the Mekong River Commission Council in 2023, which has achieved success and brought more great achievements for the River Commission. Mekong.
The Minister said that Laos and Cambodia have been brothers and good neighbors for a long time. The two countries are in the Mekong Basin, working together and collaborating with other countries along the Mekong River within the framework of the Mekong River Commission for Sustainable Development in the Mekong Region.
At the same time, the Minister also mentioned the challenges that have been occurring in the Mekong River Basin, such as population growth, development growth, demand for water, food and energy and climate change that requires member countries. Increase joint efforts and better cooperation.
During the meeting, the Minister reaffirmed Cambodia's position to continue working with Laos and other member countries of the Mekong River Commission within the framework of the One Mekong River, one Mekong spirit, to ensure the effective implementation of the statement. Vientiane City and the Mekong River Commission Basin Development Strategy 2021-2030 towards achieving the results that are the common aspirations.
The bilateral talks were held in a friendly, cordial and friendly atmosphere, with both sides expressing their willingness to push forward cooperation projects within the framework of the Mekong River Commission and achieve results with a commitment to strengthen and expand cooperation. Operations between the two countries, Cambodia and Laos, especially between ministries and ministries to be stronger and more developed.
