The northeastern region bordering China has been rocked by attacks by armed rebels against Myanmar's military regime for the past month. Meanwhile, Chinese and Myanmar government officials have cracked down on online fraud cases by Chinese in the area.
Attacks by insurgents on the Myanmar border and the crackdown on online fraud by the Chinese have led to increased attention on relations between Beijing and the Burmese military regime. China has blamed fraud on many of its people, while Myanmar handed over tens of thousands of Chinese suspects to Chinese authorities this November.
General Sar Thet urges all transport companies to instruct their drivers to obey traffic rules (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): General Sar Thet, General Commissioner of the National Police, on the morning of November 24, 2023 Transporting goods and food in Phnom Penh instructs the company's drivers to abide by traffic laws to reduce traffic accidents and fatalities.
The instruction of the General Commissioner of the National Police was made during the meeting on the introduction of traffic safety, drivers, passengers, goods and food on the occasion of the Royal Water Festival, floating lanterns and worshiping the moon Ok Ambok 2023.
During the meeting, General Sar Thet emphasized that the meeting with the transport companies and food now in order for the company to continue to disseminate traffic laws and continue to educate all drivers to drive at the speed limit, do not violate traffic lights. Traffic signs and rude driving by overtaking others to rush to deliver goods or food to the customer's order.
After meeting with the trucking and food companies, the National Police will continue to meet with large transport companies, especially container trucks, informal transporters, tuk-tuks and other stakeholders. All this always causes traffic accidents.
In order to strengthen traffic safety to be more effective, General Sar Thet advised some trucking and food companies such as:
* Agree to establish a telegram communication system between freight and food companies and the Traffic Police and Public Order Department and agree to prepare a basic document to facilitate standard training for truck and food drivers
* Encourage companies to increase the dissemination of traffic laws and ethics to truck and food drivers and educate them not to transport anything other than food and food services.
* The company continues to advise drivers to drive at the speed limit, do not violate traffic lights, traffic signs, do not drive, it overtakes disorderly
* Define clear routes and minutes of delivery to customers to avoid speeding and talking on the phone while driving.
After listening to the instructions of the National Police Commissioner, the participating trucking and food companies decided to participate in disseminating traffic rules to their truck drivers well and to set regular periods for moral education. And other principles for drivers to participate in reducing traffic accidents.
