Kampot Provincial Governor Continues to Solve 12 More Cases Out of Court for Citizens
(Kampot): Mr. New Saem, Chairman of Kampot Provincial Council and Mr. Mao Thinin, Provincial Governor, led a group of government officials, forces, authorities and stakeholders, as well as more than 300 people to participate in 12 disputes in Kampot Province. The above dispute was resolved on November 23, 2023 at Kampot Provincial Hall.
Speaking at the Dispute Resolution Forum, Mr. Mao Thinin said that the people are now living under the shadow of complete peace, and this peace is due to Samdech Techo Hun Sen, who has made every effort to bring to the people. As well as the whole of Cambodia with difficulty.
The provincial governor said that for the people who have received disputes outside the court system under the win-win mechanism, the people have received the truth, accuracy, justice and acceptance between the parties to the dispute.
Citizens who come to settle disputes outside the court system are happy and do not have to spend time and money to resolve disputes like going to court.
The provincial governor reminded that the mechanism of out-of-court settlement was encouraged by the head of the Royal Government of Cambodia and urged the sub-national authorities to resolve as much as possible to facilitate their local disputes without having to go to court.
At the same time, the Royal Government also issued a draft Royal Decree on the establishment, organization and operation of the National Authority for Dispute Resolution, which was fully approved recently.
Please note that in the 12 cases that are addressed today, most are land disputes between mothers and children, between siblings and debt cases. The extra-judicial settlement of the land dispute between the mother and the child was settled by both parties in accordance with the resolution mechanism of the provincial governor.
At the same time, the Governor of Kampot Province confirmed that the provincial administration will continue to resolve all disputes outside the court system at the local level in all cities and districts of Kampot Province through the mechanism of the Royal Government.
In this forum for resolving disputes outside the court system, the provincial governor also donated some money to the elderly grandparents and provided rice to the people who came to participate in this forum.
