WASHINGTON, Nov. 22 (Xinhua) - Israel and Hamas, under the coordination of Qatar, on Wednesday announced that they had reached a four-day ceasefire agreement in exchange for 50 hostages. Hamas also issued a statement welcoming the ceasefire, saying it would lead to the release of 150 Palestinians from Israeli prisons.
Hamas is believed to have taken more than 240 people hostage in the October 7 attack on Israel that killed 1,200 Israelis. But at the same time, according to Gaza officials, Israeli retaliatory attacks on Hamas-controlled Gaza have also killed 14,000 Palestinians, 40 percent of them children.
* This agreement is necessary but not a real ceasefire
However, a ceasefire or a moratorium is important as the death toll in Israeli retaliatory bombings in Gaza has risen to 14,000, with a population of 1.6. Millions of Gaza's total population of 2.1 million have fled their homes in the face of water, electricity and fuel shortages, and some key health systems have collapsed.
Israel has not yet achieved its goal of destroying Hamas, which is not clear, but could mean that Israel wants to change the Hamas regime. On the other hand, unlike the previous war with Hamas, this time the Israeli leadership will not stop the war until they feel they can declare their mission a success.
