President of the Cambodian Hotel Association encourages young people to participate in internships to gain work experience
(Phnom Penh): President of the Cambodian Hotel Association, Mr. Din Somethearith encouraged young people to participate in internships in companies in order to gain practical experience, both knowledge and skills before moving to get a job in the future.
His encouragement comes as the Royal Government is implementing vocational and technical training programs for 1.5 million young people from poor and vulnerable families across the country, and the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training Bio also encourages companies, enterprises and associations to provide internship and internship opportunities to students who will attend this training course.
Mr. Din Somethearith said that the internship is very important both knowledge and skills to get to the actual work for them to understand the actual work.
At the same time, he expressed optimism that the association that signed the Memorandum of Understanding (MoU) with the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training is to provide opportunities for young people who have learned in this program to show their abilities to all companies. Know their abilities, knowledge, skills.
He said: "Giving him the opportunity to train is a good time for both parties to understand each other, especially to provide job opportunities for the intern to gain knowledge, knowledge, make them practice. "How hot and cold the work is in practice."
In addition, Mr. Somethearith also supported the speech of His Excellency Hun Manet, Prime Minister of Cambodia, set the goal of this vocational training, focusing on the principle of "to be able to know and have a job" in order for this program. Effective.
Please be informed that on November 11, the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training signed a Memorandum of Understanding with the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce and 17 employers' associations on cooperation in internships and internships to support vocational training. Biology and techniques.
The Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training also considers this cooperation to pave the way for linking theory with practice to contribute to building, developing and strengthening human resources in Cambodia and enabling factory owners, enterprises and private companies to choose from. Among the interns who know and understand the existing workplace as their workers and employees.
