(Tbong Khmum): Tbong Khmum Provincial Administration organized a forum for dissemination and consultation of the third mandate provincial council in 2023 within the framework of Ou Raing Ov district, running smoothly with the active participation of the people in raising questions. Face expressions, requests and suggestions.
The forum was held at Wat Sothamma (Wat Chroul) in Chak commune, Ou Raing Ov district on November 22, 2023 under the chairmanship of Mr. Seak Leng, Chairman of Provincial Council and Dr. Cheam Chansophorn, Governor of Tbong Khmum Province.
On that occasion, the Chairman of the Provincial Council stated the purpose of organizing this forum to provide an opportunity for all citizens and stakeholders to understand the situation and general activities of the development of provinces, municipalities, districts, communes and challenges. Occurred some time ago.
The Chairman of the Provincial Council added that the forum will also provide an opportunity for all citizens and stakeholders to raise their questions, comments and suggestions related to past concerns and challenges to request and The actual needs at the local level for the competent authorities to respond and address.
Dr. Cheam Chansophoan said that through the efforts of the leaders and civil servants at all levels of the administration of Tbong Khmum, the whole province of Tbong Khmum, in general, Oreang district, in particular, has developed steadily.
Dr. Provincial Governor added that in the development and service of the administration to the people, there will be some problems, in which the provincial administration, especially the local authorities have solved and are continuing to solve for the people on behalf of the guardians.
Dr. Cheam Chansophoan emphasized that he accepted and requested the request of the people, and he assigned the departments, units, local authorities and stakeholders to solve all your concerns to make the people live in peace in accordance with The first phase of the pentagonal policy of the Royal Government of Cambodia, led by Samdech Mani Hun Manet.
On that occasion, Dr. Cheam Chansophoan reminded the authorities of Ou Raing Ov district to continue to provide public administration services as soon as possible to the grassroots to collect requests for solutions to the concerns of the people, especially to ensure safety and continue. Further local development.
Please be informed that in this forum and consultation, the people raised 17 questions and requests were answered, clarified and resolved immediately, including: Requesting the revision of the drainage system, part-time teaching Take electricity bills, apply for equity cards for poor families, land ownership planning, request for road construction and repair, and the problem of collecting slaughter tax has increased.
