130 students of the Royal University of Law and Economics were handcuffed as CRC youth
(Phnom Penh): After learning from the two-day basic training course, 130 students of the Royal University of Law and Economics were officially presented with handkerchiefs by the Cambodian Red Cross Youth, which was held. Held on the evening of November 21, 2023 under the chairmanship of Mr. Pit Chamnan, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports and a member of the Central Committee of the Cambodian Red Cross.
Speaking at the ceremony, Mr. Pit Chamnan stated that the Cambodian Red Cross, under the wise leadership of Samdech Kittipritthbandit, always pays attention, points out and encourages the management of higher education institutions to continue to build the Cambodian Red Cross Youth Network. Perform humanitarian activities in accordance with the current social situation.
He strongly hopes that the provision of towels to a total of 130 new youths is now a new part of strengthening and expanding the youth network to promote the seven fundamental principles and humanitarian values of the international movement in line with the priority areas. 4 of the Cambodian Red Cross Strategy 2021-2030.
On the other hand, all young people of the Cambodian Red Cross must continue to share the new knowledge that they have to other students to know and understand more about the Cambodian Red Cross, especially to continue to support the humanitarian activities of the Cambodian Red Cross better. Respond to the specific needs of victims and vulnerable people in their educational institutions and communities.
With 130 Cambodian Red Cross Youths provided with handkerchiefs today, the Secretary of State brought the key recommendations of Samdech Kittiprittbandit, President, to all university leaders and youth, including 6 points, including:
1: Continue to build the capacity of volunteers and youth to respond to the changing situation in the humanitarian field, to establish a network of experts and operators on the search for new solutions to humanitarian work to be able to share experiences, provide additional discussions New ideas and need to find common solutions.
2: Continue to build youth capacity, develop skills and build a network by empowering young people to participate in decision-making, approving and implementing work, training new ideas and methods to promote the sustainability of young humanitarian forces. Take turns helping the community to respond to disasters in a timely manner.
3: Pay attention to strengthen the activities of peer educators, peer assistants, know how to help students and youth of the Cambodian Red Cross who are living in poverty and are studying in educational institutions first and students, orphans and the elderly in the community later. .
4: Strengthen and expand the culture of sharing friends, educating friends among poor students and youth in educational institutions and communities.
5: Please continue to disseminate to members, youth and general students to continue to participate in all important national events to promote the prestige and nationalist spirit of the nation.
6. Continue to disseminate the guidelines of the Cambodian Red Cross effectively and comprehensively to facilitate humanitarian activities in all walks of life in educational institutions and communities.
