(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Posts and Telecommunications, the Ministry of Commerce and the Ministry of Inspection have signed a Memorandum of Understanding (MoU) on cooperation in the verification of verify.gov.kh, the provision of internet connection infrastructure and the provision of digital skills training. To civil servants between the Ministry of Posts and Telecommunications, the Ministry of Commerce and the Ministry of Inspection.
The signing ceremony of this Memorandum of Understanding was held on November 23, 2023 at the Ministry of Posts and Telecommunications, signed by Mr. Chea Van Det, Minister of Posts and Telecommunications, Ms. Cham Nimmol, Minister of Commerce and Mr. Huot Hak, Minister of Inspection. .
The MoU focuses on three main objectives: cooperation in the verification of verify.gov.kh, the provision of infrastructure and Internet connectivity, and the organization of digital skills training for civil servants under the Ministry of Commerce and the Ministry of Inspection. .
Please also note that the verify.gov.kh file verification nursery is a Royal Government nursery developed by the Ministry of Posts and Telecommunications and is intended to eliminate document fraud, make it easier to use and verify the authenticity of The document provides confidence, saves time and reduces costs, as well as promotes digital revolution in line with international best practices.
(Phnom Penh): The ASEAN Ministers of Mines will jointly promote the ASEAN region to become a sustainable mining investment destination, which will be part of the ASEAN Mining Cooperation in the future, as well as the development of a long-term ASEAN mining vision after 2025.
The Joint Meeting of the ASEAN Ministers of Mines to Promote the ASEAN Region to Become a Sustainable Mining Investment Target was held at the 9th ASEAN Ministers of Mines Meeting, which Cambodia is hosting on 23 November 2023.
Ung Eang, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Mines and Energy and Chair of the 9th ASEAN Ministerial Meeting on Mines, told reporters after the meeting that the 9th ASEAN Ministerial Meeting on Mines and Mines had adopted a declaration on "Promoting ASEAN "Becoming a sustainable investment destination."
This declaration is a testament to the joint commitment to secure the supply of metals and other minerals to meet the needs of the global turn towards low carbon technology and the need for energy and digital evolution in line with the push. Increasing mineral resources to enhance regional competitiveness and connect to global markets. As a result, this work will help push ASEAN to become a destination for sustainable mining investment.
"We are proud to announce the adoption of the ASEAN Sustainable Mining Development Principles," he said. These principles highlight our commitment to continuously improve the development of the mining sector through governance, economy, society and the environment. "The principles of sustainable mining development in the region will be part of future ASEAN mining cooperation as well as the development of a long-term ASEAN mining vision after 2025."
