During the meeting, Dr. Kao Kim Hourn also addressed the opening ceremony and emphasized ASEAN's commitment to strengthening the region's attractiveness as a sustainable investment destination and reaffirmed that Sustainable resource development and environmental initiatives remain at the heart of ASEAN's strategy for the mining sector.
The meeting discussed ways to further strengthen ASEAN cooperation in the mining sector and reviewed progress in implementing and monitoring the action plan for mining cooperation. The meeting was followed by high-level dialogues with ASEAN's external partners, including the International Energy Agency and the United Nations Economic and Social Commission for Asia and the Pacific (UNESCAP).
