At the same time, the Governor also handed over food and financial support to 4 committee members who will go to the competition in Phnom Penh on the occasion of the Water Festival, each boat received 500,000 Riels. Deputy PM Sun Chanthol Meets XDS Bicycle Leaders to Solve Company Challenges
(Phnom Penh): Deputy Prime Minister Sun Chanthol, First Vice President of the Council for the Development of Cambodia, met with the management of XDS Bicycle to provide interventions to help improve the company's production chain.
In October and November, Deputy Prime Minister Sun Chanthol met with the company's management three times. One meeting at a large company in China and two meetings in Cambodia.
During the meeting, Deputy Prime Minister Sun Chanthol informed the company about the efforts and attention of the head of the Royal Government of Cambodia in coordinating to solve the challenges that investors face in order to maintain the investment activities. Exist and encourage the company to expand its production line in Cambodia.
Bicycle manufacturer XDS has been operating in Cambodia since 2019, assembling and exporting various types of bicycles to major markets, including the United States and the European Union. The company is located in the Chiluchean Pouchai Special Economic Zone in Svay Rieng province, with an investment of about $ 19 million and has created about 1,600 jobs.
Deputy Prime Minister Sun Chanthol has expressed his intention to organize a cycling event in Siem Reap with the company's management to promote the company's bicycle products.
(Koh Kong): Duke Leng Pros, Representative of Duke Leng Navatra, CEO of Galaxy Shinawatra Group, on the afternoon of November 23, led a delegation of company leaders to lay a wreath and pay homage to the late Buddhist monk Yip Tham Kesen. The son-in-law of Samdech Pichey Sena Tea Banh.
Yip Tham Keson, a Buddhist devotee, passed away on November 20, 2023 at 12:20 at the age of 99. His body was laid to rest at his funeral home in Prek Svay village, Stung Veng commune. Royal Khmer, Koh Kong Province.
Please be informed that the great Buddhist devotee Yip Tham Keson is the mother-in-law of Samdech Pichey Sena Tea Banh, the King's personal adviser and the great-grandmother of General Tea Seiha, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of National Defense.
