The WEF Founder's passion and support for attracting investment to Cambodia was highlighted by Joo-Ok Lee, Asia-Pacific Program Director and Member of the WEF Executive Committee. Courtesy and discussion with Samdech Prime Minister Hun Manet, Prime Minister of Cambodia on the afternoon of Thursday, November 23, 2023 at the Peace Palace.
During the meeting, Mr. Chou Okli thanked Mr. Hun Manet for taking the time to allow him and the delegation to pay a courtesy call and to send a courtesy call from Professor Klaus Schwab, Founder of WEF. The Prime Minister also stated that the professors have always highly valued Cambodia and have always mentioned Cambodia's potential in meetings with countries around the world.
He welcomed the WEF delegation and thanked for the good cooperation between the Royal Government of Cambodia and the WEF in the past. In particular, co-hosting the WEF Meeting in Cambodia in 2017.
He also praised the important role of the WEF, an active forum for government-private sector relations, by introducing new government policies and initiatives related to business and investment. Original.
On behalf of the Royal Government of Cambodia, the President highlighted the continued support for WEF meetings, as well as the Royal Government of Cambodia in previous mandates. During the meeting, President Hun Manet thanked Mr. Chou Oxley for inviting him to the 54th Annual Meeting of the World Economic Forum in Davos, Switzerland in January 2024.
The World Economic Forum (WEF), a non-profit fund based in Geneva, Switzerland, is recognized by Swiss authorities as an international entity. The mission of the World Economic Forum is to promote trade, politics and set the agenda of regional and global industry-focused meetings.
The organization also holds about six to eight regional meetings a year in regions such as Latin America and East Asia, as well as additional annual meetings in China and the United Arab Emirates. In addition, the World Economic Forum conducts research reports and links its members in a clear direction.
