(Takeo): Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Chairman of the King's Personal Advisory Council, and Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen donated 5 million Riels and some food items to a family that gave birth to triplets (two girls and one boy). Residing in Tamao village, Cheung Koun commune, Samrong district, Takeo province.
The precious gift of Samdech Techo and Samdech Kittipritthbandit was handed over to the above family by Mr. Seng Teang, Deputy Director of the Cabinet of Samdech Moha Bovathibodi Hun Manet, Prime Minister of Cambodia, on the morning of November 22, 2023.
The family of three twins has a father named Tea Chandara, a chef, and a mother named Hem Savy, who works as a tailor. This is the first child in the family. In front of the family of three twins, Mr. Seng Teang brought a message from Samdech Techo and Samdech Kittipritthbandit to visit the above family.
Mr. Seng Teang reminded that from 1999 to the present, for the past 24 years, 407 families have given birth to triplets or four twins and have received generous donations from Samdech Techo and Samdech Kittipritthbandit to support the hardships in daily life. In particular, raising three twin babies must be the grandchildren of both Samdech when they give birth.
The father of three twins expressed his deepest gratitude to Samdech Techo and Samdech Kittipritthbandit, who always considered the vulnerable people as the personal hardship of both Samdech and Samdech always assigned representatives to bring money and materials. The highest price is given directly to the family who gave birth to three twins to help alleviate the difficulties in raising children to live and have a good future like other citizens in society.
