As a result of the meeting, the Constitutional Council unanimously decided to amend Article 4, Article 6 (two) and Article 29 (new) of the Internal Rules of the National Assembly of the Kingdom of Cambodia, which were approved by the National Assembly on November 16, 2023. The first session of the seventh legislature was declared unconstitutional.
The Internal Rules of the National Assembly, promulgated on October 27, 1993, have been amended 11 times in a row in order to be consistent with the provisions of the Constitution and the laws in force and in accordance with the actual situation.
