This announcement was made this morning, November 23, in a meeting with stakeholders on the posting of the initial voter list and the list of voters who will be removed from the voter list in communes across the country.
The posting of the first voter list and the list of voters to be removed from the 2023 voter list will be done on November 24, 2023 for voters who have already registered to vote to verify their data. Can file a complaint or objection in case of any mistakes.
According to the first official voter list, there are 9,871,502 registered voters, of whom 5,240,984 are women and have offices. A total of 24,034 polling stations. Separately, a total of 120,883 voters will be removed from the voter list due to relocation, death and disenfranchisement based on accurate and clear documents.
Currently, Preah Vihear is considered to be the leading producer and exporter of organic products in Cambodia, with farmers focusing on organic crops such as organic rice, organic cassava and organic cashew nuts.
He said that in order to promote Preah Vihear province to become a sustainable and leading organic farming province, ASSET project has chosen to implement in Preah Vihear province, currently training farmers in the district to practice organic farming. Agro-ecology.
He added that in order to maintain soil quality, farmers need to grow ground cover crops such as stilts, monkey stalks and other legumes to help maintain soil moisture and absorb organic matter and nutrients from the atmosphere into the soil through its root system. This cover crop can also act as a green manure for crops.
He added, "Our agro-ecological practice focuses on the diversification of his production and occupation, so that he can earn a living from a variety of products, regardless of natural disasters or disasters." "Down the market, he can still earn an income that guarantees the process of living, spending in the family."
Mr. Srun Borin, Deputy Director of the Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, said that Preah Vihear is the second largest province in Cambodia after Mondulkiri and has the potential to grow rice, cassava, bananas and cashews. About 80% of the population is engaged in agriculture. In addition, Preah Vihear is also the province with the most potential for organic farming.
He encouraged farmers to practice eco-agriculture in response to the new strategy of the Ministry of Agriculture, as well as the provincial administration, which wants to make Preah Vihear a potential province for organic farming in Cambodia.
