(Phnom Penh): On the morning of Thursday, November 23, 2023, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, Samdech Moha Bovathibodi Hun Manet, Prime Minister of Cambodia, attended the Cambodia Vision 2023 Conference held at the hotel. Sokha.
* Samdech Hun Manet stated that the Royal Government highly appreciates the Institute for Training and Research for Development of Cambodia (CDRI) for cooperating with many national and international institutions to organize this important conference.
* Samdech Thipadei Hun Manet would like to extend a warm welcome to the leaders of the Ministries - Institutions of the Royal Government, the private sector, research institutes, national and international organizations and development partners who were invited to participate in this conference.
* Samdech Hun Manet stated that the Royal Government of the 7th Legislature considers this conference as an important forum that provides an opportunity for all stakeholders, especially "research institutions" to discuss and exchange ideas on achievements, challenges and strategic directions for development. With a focus on practicality and flexibility in changing global and regional environments in order to bring Cambodian ships to prosperity, sustainability and environment.
* Samdech Hun Manet stated that over the last two decades, starting from the win-win policy of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Cambodia has built a strong economic foundation for development by adhering to a market economy, openness and trade. International karma is based on the principle of multilateralism.
* President Hun Manet stated that the promotion and attraction of foreign direct investment as a basis for building infrastructure to support economic growth.
* President Hun Manet stated that the strengthening and rehabilitation of solid infrastructure such as roads, water and electricity to improve connectivity, facilitate the mobility of resources and labor, as well as deploy production bases,
Samdech Hun Sen stated that the continued development and promotion of human capital to participate in economic activities and increase productivity,
* Samdech Manipadei Hun Manet stated that regular institutional and governance reforms to ensure the effective management of the political and economic system, including the public financial system and the banking system to be effective and efficient, as well as to distribute the fruits of growth equitably and environmentally.
* Samdech Hun Manet stated that although Cambodia continues to be affected by the Kovid 19 crisis and other crises that continue to occur, the Royal Government does not give up or change its long-term development direction, the Royal Government still maintains its goal of achieving its ambitions. Again, Cambodia will become a high middle income country by 2030 and a high income country by 2050.
* Samdech Mani Hun Manet stated that the Royal Government has not only set out strategies, but also set out a series of reform mechanisms and practical measures over the past three months, the Royal Government has set out a series of " Priority Policy Program »Five programs have been announced and launched, including:
* Samdech Thipadei Hun Manet stated that at the 19th Royal Government-Private Sector Forum, Samdech decided to introduce sharp measures aimed at deepening the reform of the new government to promote economic diversification and The height of Cambodia's competitiveness.
* Samdech Hun Manet stated that he was very interested in the three sessions, which are all important topics, especially in terms of policy for Cambodia to be well prepared and sufficient to achieve the 2030 and year milestones. Next up.
* President Hun Manet stated that the Cambodian economy is an open economy, so positive and negative changes from external factors will directly and indirectly affect Cambodia's medium-long-term growth potential.
Samdech Hun Sen stated that he would like to see our conference today as a forum for honest, constructive and constructive exchange of ideas and joint responsibility on the fate of Cambodia.
Samdech Hun Sen stated that he hopes that today's conference will run smoothly and fruitfully and would like to announce the opening of the Cambodia Vision 2023 conference from now on.
