SEOUL, Nov. 22 (Xinhua) - North Korea on Wednesday confirmed the successful launch of its first reconnaissance satellite into orbit and promised to launch more reconnaissance satellites. In the future, to defend itself against what Pyongyang considers dangerous military action from its enemies.
Third North Korea made its first attempt to launch a reconnaissance satellite into Earth orbit in late May, but the second batch of the rocket carrying the satellite failed and failed. Fall into the sea. North Korea's second attempt failed again as the rocket carrying the satellite exploded into pieces before crashing into the Yellow Sea, the East Sea and the Pacific Ocean. According to Japanese officials.
It was not until Tuesday night that the third attempt was made, and by Wednesday morning, November 22, North Korea had confirmed the success of launching a reconnaissance satellite into Earth orbit.
