(Guangdong): After nine days of joint training, the multinational exercise "Peace-Friendship 2023" in Zhangjiang, southern China's Guangdong Province, ended this morning. November 22, 2023, presided over by senior commanders of the six participating countries: China, Cambodia, Malaysia, Laos, Thailand and Vietnam.
General Vong Pisen, Commander-in-Chief of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces, who presided over the closing ceremony of the exercise, thanked the Chinese People's Liberation Army for initiating the multinational exercise with the aim of strengthening ties between countries in the region. Aims to promote military cooperation and a common security vision in the region.
The General described the joint exercise as a symbol of strong cooperation between the six participating countries and armies, and certainly provided important information to enhance the capacity and awareness of the Armed Forces, such as change. Mutual experience, how to lead problems, different tactics, tactics, techniques and new skills.
At the same time, the exercise also strengthened the army to strengthen good relations, increase solidarity, facilitate living and work together with other nations during joint operations to respond effectively and in a timely manner in operations at both the national and international levels, participate in prevention and resolution. Potential challenges eventually.
The Commander-in-Chief expressed his belief that the "Peace and Friendship" multinational exercise will continue to grow steadily and with the participation of more countries in the region in the future to contribute to the maintenance of peace, stability and prosperity. Local.
According to the report, this is the first time that China has organized this "Peace and Friendship" exercise, and many countries are participating in order to enhance the capacity of the participating parties for anti-terrorism operations in urban and maritime anti-piracy operations. Cross-border to increase military trust and practical cooperation.
