According to ancient history, the world has four ocean basins called the Atlantic Ocean, the Pacific Ocean, the Indian Ocean and the Arctic Ocean. Today, however, many countries, including the United States, are beginning to recognize the Southern Ocean, or Antarctic Ocean, around the Antarctic ice sheet as the fifth ocean basin.
