The Joint Research Initiative on "Cambodia Vision 2030: Assessing Cambodia's Goals for Becoming a High-Middle-Income Country for Sustainable and Sustainable Growth" is launched. Officially in response to a request from the Royal Government of Cambodia to the CDRI Institute during the Cambodia Annual Vision Conference in October 2022.
This study is evaluating Cambodia's long-term growth potential and identifying optimal policies to help Cambodia achieve sustainable, sustainable and sustainable growth.
CDRI organized a consultative workshop with the participation of stakeholders from the Royal Government of Cambodia, development partners, business associations, research institutes and civil society. In addition to data collection and analysis, CDRI is also reviewing in-depth policies and considering social impacts such as gender participation and climate impacts that affect growth.
"Cambodia has been severely affected by the recent global crisis, including the Kovid-19 pandemic and the war in Ukraine," said Justin Wyatt, Australia's ambassador to Cambodia. "This research is important to show how Cambodia can return to the status quo and overcome all obstacles to achieve its goal of being a high middle-income country by 2030."
Dr. Eng Netra added, "Cambodia's vision for 2030 embodies deep ambitions and visions of a glorious future. "Through research, we strive to provide an independent, in-depth, high-quality and influential analysis to guide Cambodia towards its goals while changing regional and global perspectives."
