Today, the 90th anniversary of the leadership of Samdech Hun Sen, President Hun Manet inaugurated the National Road No. 5 from Prek Kdam to Battambang and opened the construction site from Serei Sophorn to Poipet
The northern section of the road (Battambang-Serey Sophorn) was officially inaugurated on January 10, 2022. The other two sections, the southern section and the central section, were completed in May 2023 and officially inaugurated on November 22, 2023.
Southern Road Section (Prek Kdam-Thla Mam): 135.25 km long, starting from Prek Kdam Bridge, passing through Kandal, Kampong Chhnang and Pursat Provinces, including the construction of 33 new bridges and the repair of old bridges with a total length of 749 meters And installed 245 sewers.
Central Road Section (Thla Mam - Battambang): 110.90 km long, starting from Thla Mam, passing through Pursat and Battambang Provinces, including the construction of new bridges and the repair of 31 old bridges with a total length of 1,418 meters and installed 130 sewers.
Both sections are constructed in accordance with the same technical standards, including: Upgrading the quality of the concrete pavement (AC) with a thickness of 15 cm, widening the width of the road in the city by 29 meters and the width of the body. The road outside the town is 23 meters long and has 4 lanes of traffic (2 lanes to 2 lanes).
The two sections are also equipped with traffic signs, markers, kilometer markers, safety poles in accordance with the technical standards of the road and the planting of ornamental trees in parks, sidewalks and sidewalks between the towns.
Along with the inauguration of the above two sections, the Royal Government also started the construction of National Road No. 5 from Serei Sophorn to Poipet with a length of 35.14 km. The construction is an additional request to connect National Road 5 to Poipet and the Cambodian-Thai border (Poipet-Aranyaprathet).
The project will be constructed of 15 cm thick AC concrete pavement, extending the width of the inner road in the city by 29 meters and the width of the outer road by 23 meters with the same standard as the section. Other National Road 5.
The project will take 32 months to complete and is scheduled for completion in March 2025 with an additional $ 52.56 million. The construction money is a concessional loan from the Government of Japan, along with some contributions from the Royal Government of Cambodia.
