(Myanmar): The Burmese military regime has been facing attacks on several battlefields along the border as ethnic armed insurgents join forces with pro-democracy movements to step up territorial disputes and power struggles. Led by the current military regime.
On October 27, a coalition of ethnic armed groups launched an attack on a military post in Shan State, northern Myanmar, bordering China, capturing several military posts, including a strategic city. Also important in an operation they named "Operation No. 1027", which refers to the launch date of the attack.
China, a major regional power, has pushed for an end to hostilities. But some analysts and diplomats say it is unlikely that "Operation 1027" could have taken place without a green light from China.
Operation 1027, which has been hailed in Myanmar and is being closely watched in the media, is a major challenge to the Myanmar military's claim that its power is unmatched. . The Burmese military regime has little choice but to acknowledge that its power is under test after the junta's president warned that Myanmar was at risk of division.
In this sense, one possible scenario is that the military regime will lose control of some border areas, even if it retains control of the central government. On the other hand, prolonging the conflict will also be a test of the power and arsenal of both parties to the conflict.
