(Phnom Penh): Mr. Ly Chantola, Chairman of the National Committee of the ASEAN Law Association of Cambodia, gave a presentation on the roles and responsibilities of the National Committee of the ASEAN Law Association of Cambodia and the ASEAN Law Association to students of the profession, judges, students, prosecutors and A total of 139 registrar students of the Royal Academy of Cambodia.
The program was held at the Techo Heritage Hall of the Royal Academy of Justice of Cambodia on the afternoon of November 21, 2023, while the keynote speaker was Dr. Prohm Vichet Akra, Permanent Vice Chairman of the National Commission, accompanied by Mr. Bun Yay Narin, Deputy President of the Royal Academy of Justice of Cambodia and Mr. Srun Thirith, Member of the National Committee.
On that occasion, Mr. Ly Chantola said that in the past, the National Committee of the ASEAN Law Association has contributed to present the legal aspects of Cambodia to ASEAN countries to help promote Cambodia's economic development and attract foreign investors.
The National Committee of the ASEAN Law Association of Cambodia was established on September 18, 2017 by Sub-Decree No. 124 to bring together legal professionals such as lawyers, judges, prosecutors, law professors and law enforcement officers.
Pursuant to this sub-decree, the National Committee of the ASEAN Law Association of Cambodia has the following roles and responsibilities:
* Establish and implement its own bylaws * Participate in meetings and act in accordance with the bylaws of the ASEAN Law Association * Participate in presenting the legal aspects of Cambodia with lawyers of other ASEAN countries to help promote Cambodia's economic development And attract investors * Organize the event of the ASEAN Legal Association Meeting in turn in coordination with the ASEAN Supreme Court Presiding Council Meeting in collaboration with the Supreme Court.
