Thailand, Sri Lanka to sign trade agreement in February
Sri Lanka plans to conclude free trade agreement (FTA) talks with Thailand in December and sign them on February 3, a Sri Lankan cabinet spokesman said on Tuesday. According to Reuters.
The island nation has been focusing on trade agreements to boost growth and help its damaged economy recover from its worst financial crisis in decades.
Data from the Central Bank of Sri Lanka show that bilateral trade between the two countries is expected to reach $ 460 million by 2021. Sri Lanka exports precious tea and gems to Thailand and imports electronics, food, rubber, plastics and medicines.
Sri Lanka resumed talks on a trade agreement with India this month and said it wanted to reach an FTA with Bangladesh and become a member of the Regional Comprehensive Economic Partnership Agreement (RCEP), which includes China, Japan and South Korea.
