This statement was made by the President of the Japan-Cambodia Association (JCA) on the occasion that he led the President of some Japanese companies and investors to meet with Mr. Prak Sokhon, Member of the Standing Committee of the Central Committee and Chairman of the Foreign Relations Committee, High Representative of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, President of the Cambodian People's Party, on November 21, 2023 at the 7 Makara Palace.
Through a press release from the Cambodian People's Party, Mr. Kahasi Fumiaki stated his intention to establish an office of the Japan-Cambodia Association in Cambodia to facilitate and promote investment and business between the two countries.
He also mentioned that Japanese small and medium enterprises are interested in various technical fields, specializing in car repair and maintenance, information technology, nursing and beauty.
In response, Mr. Prak Sokhon welcomed and supported the idea of establishing an association office and the intention to promote investment. He also briefed on the stable political and social situation after the general election in July and the smooth transfer of power to the new generation of leaders, which has created a favorable investment environment in Cambodia, which is an opportunity. For Japanese investment and other countries in Cambodia.
Mr. Prak Sokhon emphasized that the Japanese investment has not only contributed to the economic development of Cambodia, but also promoted the development of human resources through the training of various technical skills to Cambodian employees and engineers.
The two sides pledged to further strengthen relations and cooperation to further promote mutual investment and business between the two countries for the benefit of the people and the two countries. Both sides congratulated the success of the rocket launch using Japanese technology on November 19, 2023 to celebrate the 70th anniversary of the establishment of diplomatic relations between Cambodia and Japan.
The Cambodian People's Party (CPP) issued a press release on the outcome of a meeting between Prak Sokhon, representative of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, President of the Japan-Cambodia Association (JCA) and Japanese investors.
(Phnom Penh): On the morning of November 20, 2023, Mr. Prak Sokhon, Member of the Standing Committee of the Central Committee and Chairman of the Foreign Relations Committee, High Representative of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, President of the Cambodian People's Party, received Mr. Takahashi Fumiaki. The President of the Japan-Cambodia Association (JCA) and former Japanese Ambassador to Cambodia, along with the President of the Company and some Japanese investors met at the 7 January Palace.
On that occasion, Mr. Prak Sokhon warmly welcomed the 3rd Japanese Investment Promotion Delegation to Cambodia and thanked and thanked HE Takahashi Fumiaki for his active role in initiating, promoting and directing the visit. As well as promoting Japanese investment in Cambodia.
He also celebrated the promotion of bilateral relations to the level of a comprehensive strategic partnership in 2023, the year of the 70th anniversary of Cambodia-Japan diplomatic relations.
He also thanked the Cambodian People's Party, the Royal Government and the Cambodian people for Japan's valuable contribution to the peace process, national reconstruction and socio-economic development as it is today.
Mr. Takahashi Fumiaki thanked Samdech Techo Hun Sen and the Royal Government of Cambodia for always supporting the activities of the Japan-Cambodia Association as well as Japanese investment projects.
