(Phnom Penh): Mr. Heng Sour, Minister of Labor and Vocational Training, stated that as of November 20, 2023, about 1,608 young people have registered for vocational and technical training courses throughout the country.
Speaking at a meeting with 18,108 workers from factories based in Kambol district, Phnom Penh on November 21, 2023, the Minister highlighted that out of 1,608 registered There are Phnom Penh, Battambang, Siem Reap and some other provinces.
He added that young people from poor and vulnerable families who enroll in this vocational training course will receive a stipend of 280,000 riels per month and study for free.
He said that in order to encourage young people to enroll more, the Ministry of Labor will cooperate with the Royal Government working group in all cities, districts, Khans, Sangkats to meet directly with young people from poor and vulnerable families to explain the benefits of This program goes to them.
"In order for this training to be successful, the Ministry of Labor is striving to achieve the motto of the President: learn to finish, learn to know, learn to have a job," he said.
In addition, the Minister stated that the Ministry of Labor has been cooperating with the private sector to make sure that the private sector can accept students who have completed this vocational training course.
This statement was made after November 14, 2023, under the presidency of His Majesty the King of Cambodia, Hun Manet, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, officially announced the implementation of vocational and technical training for young people from poor and vulnerable families. General Vong Pisen pays a courtesy call on Chairman of the Joint Chiefs of Staff of the Central Military Commission of China
On the afternoon of November 21, 2023, General Vong Pisen, Commander-in-Chief of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces, attended the closing ceremony of the "Peace and Friendship 2023" multinational exercise held in the southern Chinese province of Guangdong. Leading a high-level delegation of the Cambodian Army to pay a courtesy call on General Liu Chenlik, Chairman of the Joint Chiefs of Staff of the Central Military Commission of the People's Republic of China.
On behalf of the Ministry of National Defense and the Commander-in-Chief, General Vong Pisen expressed his deep gratitude to the Chinese People's Liberation Army for initiating the hosting of the six-nation multinational exercise, especially the Chinese friends who facilitated and supported it. Support the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces to contribute to the strengthening of Cambodia's independence and to raise Cambodia's profile in the region and the world.
The Commander-in-Chief affirmed the continued implementation of the Memorandum of Understanding and Protocol on Cooperation between the two Ministries of Defense, which have been agreed in the past, such as exchanges of visits at all levels, training of human resources, exchange of intelligence in The goal is to fight extremism, prevent the color revolution and prevent crime.
In response, General Liu Chenlik emphasized the good cooperation between China and Cambodia in all fields, especially the building of a common destiny of Cambodia and China in the new era 2024-2028. It is an important cooperation plan for the benefit of the people of both countries.
In the field of the military, General Liu Chenlik said that over the past few years, the Chinese People's Liberation Army and the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces have been in close and high-level communication and are making steady progress. Many fruitful results.
General Liu Chenlik believes that in the future, the relationship between the two armies will be strengthened through friendly relations and mutual respect, as well as close cooperation that brings benefits. Mutual development, common development and condolences on the basis of comprehensive strategic partnership "Steel friendship and community building, common destiny of Cambodia-China".
