The Minister stated that for the energy sector, the new government will not only fulfill its promise not to increase electricity prices, but also exceed its promises by lowering electricity prices for some priority sectors to boost national economic activity.
The Minister of Energy made the remarks at a press conference on "Mineral and Energy Policy in Cambodia" on November 21, 2023 at the Sokha Hotel in Phnom Penh.
Mr. Keo Rattanak stated that the main priority of President Hun Manet is to restore the economy after being affected by the 19-Kovid disease, the Russia-Ukraine war and the uncertainties in the Middle East, which continue to have a negative impact on the world. Mr.
Please be informed that His Excellency Hun Manet in public forums has always stated that although the world is facing an energy crisis that requires many countries to increase electricity prices, Cambodia will not raise electricity prices, even though the state has lost hundreds of millions of dollars in 1 year. The non-increase in prices is a consideration for the living standards of the people in times of economic hardship.
* 10% discount on the average monthly energy consumption from Monday to Saturday between 7am and 9pm.
* 20% discount on the average monthly energy consumption from Monday to Saturday between 9pm and 7am and 24 hours on Sundays and public holidays. Increase the above usage for 3 months from October to December 2023 and can be checked by 30 days notice according to the actual possibility of EDC.
* Consumers of industrial and agricultural electricity connected to medium and high voltage networks who feel they have the potential to increase consumption and wish to receive a preference today must apply to their local electricity supplier.
Separately, for agricultural pumps and all kinds of consumers in the agricultural sector, use at night from 9 pm to 7 am, the price is 480 riels per kilowatt hour.
