(Phnom Penh): On the morning of Tuesday, November 9, 2023, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, Samdech Moha Bovathibodi Hun Manet, continued to visit workers for the 10th time to fulfill their contract. Techo Hun Sen.
The 10th meeting was held with workers from factories and enterprises based in Phnom Penh. Dr. Heng Sour, Minister of Labor and Vocational Training, said that 18,108 workers, including 530 pregnant women from 13 factories in Kambol district, attended the event.
According to Mr. Heng Sour, the workers who participated in the above conversation came from 10 garment factories, 2 sewing shoes and 1 travel product and 1 bag.
Before the election of the 7th National Assembly, Samdech Techo Hun Sen announced to continue to visit workers 10 more times after the election. After the election, Samdech Techo Hun Sen decided to step down as Prime Minister instead of Samdech Thibodi Hun Manet. Samdech Techo also decided to assign the task to Samdech Thipdey to visit workers 10 times instead.
Do not delay and do not disappoint Samdech Techo with the workers. Immediately after the establishment of the Royal Government, Samdech Thipadei Hun Manet also organized a series of visits to factory workers. In these 10 meetings, Samdech Thipadei Hun Manet met with a total of 172,350 workers from 189 factories.
In this meeting with workers, Samdech Moha Bovathibodi Hun Manet presented 6 jobs to the Minister of Labor and Vocational Training to be implemented in 2023 and 4 jobs to be implemented in the following years for the benefit of workers.
The Minister of Labor and Vocational Training, Mr. Heng Sour, strives to implement those works with the highest sense of responsibility and achieve a series of results.
Samdech President Hun Manet has stated that the well-being of workers is the well-being of the Royal Government. Therefore, Samdech's program to meet with workers does not end 10 times, Samdech will continue to visit in the future.
