(Phnom Penh): Prof. Chheang Ra, Minister of Health, called on people over the age of 40 to go for a health check-up, especially blood sugar testing to prevent and treat diabetes. Timely.
This statement was made by the Minister on the occasion of presiding over the World Diabetes Day under the theme "Access to Diabetes Care" organized by the Ministry of Health in collaboration with the World Health Organization in Cambodia. WHO).
The Minister said that the effects of diabetes are very serious for health, so call on all our people to pay special attention, especially to be careful not to develop diabetes.
"Because diabetes has serious health consequences, it can lead to heart attack, stroke, blindness, kidney failure and paralysis," he said. But the disease can be prevented and avoided, and if it is sick, it can be prevented by treatment. "So let our people hurry to get a blood sugar test to know and treat on time."
He added that on behalf of the Ministry of Health, people should hurry to check their health, especially to check their blood sugar, which is an obligation to protect each family, which avoids losing money in the cost of diabetes. This will help protect your health and if you are diagnosed with diabetes, please get the right treatment and check your health regularly according to your doctor's appointment.
On that occasion, the Minister also gave key messages to people with diabetes to avoid diabetes, including: 1: Maintain weight (do not gain weight) 2: Exercise 3: Eat, avoid foods that contain Side effects such as sweet drinks, sugary foods (high in sugar) or red meat 4: Get a health check is a sugar test 5: Treat
For those who do not have diabetes, to prevent it, even as a child, do not drink orange juice, sweetened water and replaced with pure water. In addition, from adulthood to eat a healthy diet, reduce sugary, salty and high-calorie foods, as well as regular exercise, maintain a healthy weight, reduce harmful alcohol consumption and do not. Smoking cigarettes.
230 retired soldiers under the 5th Military Command were transferred from the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces
(Battambang): On the morning of November 20, 2023, a ceremony to equip officers and deputies to retire from the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces in 2023 under the chairmanship of Lt. Gen. Sam Oun, Deputy Commander of the Army, Commander of the 5th Army Division. Representing General Mao Sophan, Deputy Commander-in-Chief of the Army, the ceremony was held at the 5th Military Command.
Pursuant to the Law on Pensions and Disability Pensions in 2023, 230 soldiers will be transferred from the framework of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces in 2023.
On that occasion, Lt. Gen. Sam Oun, on behalf of the Royal Government of Cambodia, the Ministry of National Defense and the Commander-in-Chief of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces, expressed his gratitude to all the retired soldiers who have spent valuable time and almost all their lives. Make all kinds of sacrifices for the cause of serving the motherland.
Lt. Gen. Sam Oun stated that the heroic sacrifices and patriotic spirit at all stages of history have contributed significantly to the protection of territorial integrity, building and safeguarding peace, social stability, which is the foundation of national development for progress.
He recalled the achievements of retired disabled soldiers who have contributed to the society in the past, including: the overthrow of the genocidal regime of Pol Pot, the participation of Samdech Techo Hun Sen's win-win policy, the restoration and development of peacekeeping and stability. And the reform of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces.
The Lieutenant General stated that today, although you have been rested from work, but have left a lot of achievements and experiences for the next generation of soldiers, and the Royal Government, the Ministry of National Defense, the Commander-in-Chief of the Army, always remember the sacrifices and merits. Yours sincerely, ladies and gentlemen.
Lt. Gen., Deputy Commander of the Army, Commander of the 5th Army Division, instructed all units to continue to cooperate in organizing social programs, visiting and supporting retirees and disabled veterans in various ceremonies at the local level, and being hospitalized to connect emotions. On behalf of comrades who used to work together.
