Ministry of Commerce in collaboration with the Ministry of Agriculture plans to hold a cashew forum early next month to promote Cambodia's cashew potential
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Commerce, in collaboration with the Ministry of Agriculture and other stakeholders, plans to organize a cashew forum under the theme "Promoting the potential of Cambodian cashews" on December 6-7, 2023 at Stung Sen Park, Kampong Thom Province, which is a good opportunity for Craftsmen, owners of processing companies advertise their products and find business partners.
The forum will bring together all stakeholders in the cashew industry, display of cashew products and equipment related to the cashew production chain and business matching, etc., to promote and enhance the reputation of Cambodian cashews.
The Ministry of Commerce encourages the public and all stakeholders to participate in large numbers. For craft owners, company owners, enterprises who wish to participate in the exhibition and find business partners, please contact the Ministry of Commerce.
Please be informed that cashew is a strategic crop that the Royal Government has been paying attention to and promoting the largest export in the world, or can be said to be "the emperor" to export all the cashew in the future. The Royal Government has just launched a national policy on cashew nuts, a roadmap focusing on major strategic goals, such as increasing the cultivation, production, processing and export of more cashew nuts to international markets.
According to the report of the Cambodian Cashew Association, there are currently more than 700,000 hectares of cashew plantations in Cambodia. In 2022, Cambodia will export 670,000 tons of raw cashew nuts to the international market worth 1.77 billion US dollars, including Vietnam, Japan and China, while other countries are also Look for opportunities to import Cambodian cashew nuts to your home market as well.
