(Phnom Penh): Banteay Meanchey Polytechnic Institute announces the recruitment of 2,100 young people from poor and vulnerable families to enroll in 12 free vocational and technical training courses.
This announcement comes after His Excellency Hun Manet, Prime Minister, on November 14, 2023, officially announced the implementation of vocational and technical training for young people from poor and vulnerable families by providing a subsidy amount. 280,000 riels per month.
According to the Banteay Meanchey Polytechnic Institute, 2,100 young men and women from poor and vulnerable families who want to learn real technical skills for their careers are required to enroll in one technical and vocational degree training course.
