First baby successfully registered through communication and information technology system from health notification system to civil registration system, General Department of Identification
This work was piloted on November 1, 2023 in Po Sen Chey district, Phnom Penh.
Congratulations to Rith Srey Pich, born on November 12, 2023 in Sangkat Kakap 1, Khan Por Senchey, Phnom Penh, and the first baby to successfully register her birth from the health notification system to the General Registration Department.
This is a visionary step and a turning point in the history of civil registration in Cambodia in line with the first phase of the Pentagon strategy of the Royal Government, the seventh mandate of the National Assembly, which sets "economic development and digital society" as the core of the constitution. A strategy.
The test includes birth registration, death registration, marriage registration and the issuance of a unique identification number (UIC) to the newborn.
