(Phnom Penh): On November 20, 2023, the Minister of Foreign Affairs presided over the celebration of World Diabetes Day under the theme "Access to Diabetes Care" organized by the Ministry of Health. In collaboration with the World Health Organization in Cambodia (WHO).
"Diabetes in Cambodia is a chronic disease and a major health challenge for individuals, families and the health system," he said. In Cambodia, diabetes has a mortality rate of 2% of all deaths and a prevalence of 9.6% (based on the 2016 Non-Communicable Diseases Risk Survey in Cambodia).
The Minister of Health stressed that the main risk factors for diabetes are due to poor eating habits to maintain health and the habit of not working or getting enough exercise regularly. Diabetes can cause complications such as heart attack, stroke, blindness, kidney failure and paralysis.
Diabetes is a lifelong treatment, but diabetes can be prevented by changing healthy eating habits, such as eating a healthy diet (reducing sugary, salty and high-calorie foods). As needed, as well as regular exercise, maintain a healthy weight, reduce harmful alcohol consumption and quit smoking.
On that occasion, the Minister also recommended to all health officials and development partners to encourage diabetics to share life experiences before and during diabetes to the general public for Prevention, diagnosis and better management of health care.
At the same time, the Minister called on people who are at risk or have a family history of diabetes to come and get tested for diabetes at the nearest health center or hospital.
Please be informed that the main objectives of this year's World Diabetes Day Campaign are: 1: Raise awareness of type 2 diabetes risk, prevention and timely treatment 2: Encourage at-risk individuals to seek Diabetes Testing 3: Promote behavioral change by changing habits and personal activities toward a healthier lifestyle.
Royal Government to Build Irrigation System at Prek Neal Reservoir in Svay Rieng Province
(Phnom Penh): With the assistance of the Government of Korea through the Korea International Cooperation Agency (KOICA), the Royal Government of Cambodia will build an irrigation system at Prek Nal Reservoir in Svay Rieng Province. This irrigation system aims to reduce floods and droughts, supply irrigation, water supply to industrial households and increase agricultural productivity and efficiency.
