This morning, November 20, Mr. Chey Chap expressed his deepest gratitude to Samdech Techo Hun Sen for allowing a delegation of the Khmer Writers Association to pay a courtesy call at the 7 January Palace. Although the statue has a lot of work to do.
Mr. Preung Pronit, President of the Khmer Writers Association, briefed Samdech Techo on the past activities of the Khmer Writers Association on gathering researchers, compiling and compiling on the achievements of the Royal Government.
The President also informed Samdech Techo about the organization of the Association's annual essay competition under the theme "January 7 Peace Prize" which is planned to be held in the near future. The President also informed Samdech Techo about the purpose of organizing a gathering of writers of countries along the Mekong River to discuss research work and future directions on the composition.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen expressed his support for the purpose and direction of the Khmer Writers Association, which has achieved some achievements in the past. Samdech Techo highly appreciated the work of Khmer writers, but Samdech proposed to train and research thoroughly in order to make the works of the writers more famous and reputable.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen requested the Khmer Writers' Association to participate in reviewing the composition of educational short stories published on social media or in texts that have some parts that are different from the reality of the society, untrue, and affect the society.
Samdech Techo continued that if writing about history, the writer must clearly understand the history, research the history clearly, do not express his own ideas. During the meeting, Samdech Techo supported the writing contest for the "January 7 Peace" award and supported the gathering of writers in the Mekong countries and support the upcoming Writers' Day.
